hadiths[383]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8293","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf, the judge in Baghdad, told us, Abu Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Sulayman bin Abdullah Al-Dimashqi told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Yazid bin Saeed bin Dhu Aswan told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ata, on the authority of Muadh bin Saad Al-Saskiki, on the authority of Junada bin Abu Umayyah, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, said: While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we were standing when a man approached. He said: O Messenger of God, how long will your nation’s hope last? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent about him until he asked him three times. Then the man turned away, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “You have asked me about something that no one from my nation has asked me about. The hope of my nation is for a hundred years.” He said: He said: O Messenger of God, is there any sign for that? Or a sign or sign. He said: “Yes, the slander, the trembling, the shaking, and the sending of bridling devils from the people.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8293 - Its chain of transmission is dark"
"8294","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani informed us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah informed us Al-Asbahani, Abu Muhammad Al-Hussein bin Hafs Al-Hamdani told us, Sufyan bin Saeed Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Amr Al-Sibani, on the authority of Ibn Al-Daylami, on the authority of Hudhayfah Ibn Al-Yaman, said: “I know people of two religions from the nation of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he will be safe in the Fire: A people say: If our predecessors were astray, what is the matter with five prayers a day and a night? They are only the afternoon and dawn prayers. And there are people who say: “Faith is only speech, even if one commits adultery or kills.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8294 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8295","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abu Ayyub Al-Dimashqi told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Abdullah bin Al-Alaa bin Zubr Al-Rubi’i said: I heard Bishr bin Ubayd Allah Al-Hadrami speaking, that he heard Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, He says: I heard Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i saying: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the Battle of Tabuk while he was in a cloak of human beings, and he said To me: “O Auf, prepare six things before the Hour: my death, then the conquest of the Holy House, then two deaths that will take upon you like sheep’s punishment, then a large number of deaths.” Money is among you until a man is given a hundred dinars and he remains discontented, then there is a strife in which no Arab house will remain without entering it, then a truce will be established between you. And among the Banu Asfar, they will treacherously, and they will come to you under eighty and twelve thousand people.” Al-Walid bin Muslim said: So we mentioned this hadith. An old man from the city’s sheikhs. His saying: Then the Holy House was opened, and the Sheikh said: Sa’id al-Maqbari told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that he used to speak With these six on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he says: Instead of “the conquest of the Holy House” the construction of the Holy House “this is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs, and they did not take it out in this context.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8295 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8296","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, Al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told us, Na’im ibn Hammad al-Marwazi told us, in Egypt, al-Fadl ibn Musa told us, Abd al-A`la bin Abi al-Musawir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of al-Harith bin Umayrah, he said: I came from the Levant to Medina in search of knowledge, and I heard Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Those who love one another for the sake of God will have platforms of light on the Day of Judgment.” On the Resurrection, the martyrs will envy them.”
 So I stayed with him and mentioned the Levant, its people, and its poetry to him. He prepared for the Levant, so I went out with him, and I heard him saying to Amr bin Al-Aas: May God be pleased with them. You accompanied the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and you were more misguided than his family’s donkey. Then his son and his wife became afflicted with the plague and died. All of us, so he dug one grave for them, and we were buried. Then we returned to Mu’adh, and he was heavy, and we cried around him. He said: “If you are crying over knowledge... This is the Book of God before you, so follow it. If any of its interpretation is difficult for you, then you should follow these three: Uwaimir Abi Al-Darda’, And Ibn Umm Abd, and Salman the Persian, and beware of the slip of a scholar and the argument of a hypocrite.”
 So I stayed for a month, then I went to Iraq and came to Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, and he said: “How good the living are the people of the Levant, had it not been that they They bear witness against themselves of salvation.” I said: Muadh spoke the truth. He said: And what did he say? I said: He recommended you and Uwaimir, Abu Darda, and Salman Al-Farisi, and he said: And beware of the slip of a scholar and the argument of a hypocrite. Then I stepped aside, and he said To me: O my nephew, it was a mistake on my part, so I stayed with him for a month.
Then I came to Salman Al-Farisi and heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The souls are soldiers recruited, so he did not recognize them.” He made alliances, and none of them disagreed. So I stayed with him for a month, dividing the night and dividing the day between him and his servant. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not take it out.”"
"8297","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Bayruti told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shapur told us, Abdul Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhayriz, that Muadh bin Jabal used to say: “The construction of the Holy House, The ruins of Yathrib, and the ruins of Yathrib, the presence of the epic, and the presence of the epic The conquest of Constantinople, and the conquest of Constantinople, exit Al-Dajjal.” He said: Then Mu’adh struck Omar ibn Al-Khattab’s shoulder and said: “By God, that is true, just as you are sitting.” This hadith, even if It was suspended, as its chain of transmission is correct according to the conditions of the men, and it is appropriate for the chain of transmission that he presented.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8297 - Sahih Mawqoof"
"8298","Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abu al-Ahwas Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Qadi told us, Muhammad ibn Kathir told us Al-Musaysi, Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiya, on the authority of Dhu Mikhmar - a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he is my nephew. Al-Najashi - that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “You will make a safe peace with the Romans until you, while they are an enemy, attack behind them. So you will be helped, take spoils, and depart, until you land in a hilly meadow. Someone from the Romans will say: The cross has prevailed, and someone from the Muslims will say: Yes. God has defeated, so they exchange it among themselves, so the Muslim will revolt against their cross while they are not far away from them and attack it, and the Romans will revolt against the one who broke their cross. So they kill him, and the Muslims rise up and take up their weapons and are killed, so God Almighty honors that band of Muslims with martyrdom. Then the Romans will say to the companions of the Romans: Enough of you, the grandfather of the Arabs, so they will treacherously and gather for the battle, and they will come to you with eighty targets under each target. Twelve thousand: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8298 - True"
"8299","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Al-Awza’i told us, Hassan bin Attiya told me, he said: Makhoul and Ibn Abi Zakaria came to Khaled bin Ma’dan, and I stood with them, and he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr said: Go with us to Dhu Mikhmar, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “The Romans will make a safe peace with you, then you and they will fight an enemy, and you will be victorious, and you will submit and conquer. Then you will be victorious with a battle, and it will be raised.” They have a man from Christianity who crosses, and a man from among the Muslims becomes angry, so he rises up to them and strikes the cross. Then the Romans become angry and they gather together. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is better than the first.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8299 - True"
"8300","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Dawraqi told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told me, Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i told me, Al-Walid bin Al-Mughira, Abdullah bin Bishr Al-Ghanawi told me, my father told me, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Let it be opened.” Constantinople, and what an excellent prince its leader is, and what an excellent army that army is.” Ubayd Allah said: “So Maslamah ibn Abd al-Malik called me and asked me Concerning this hadith, I narrated it to him, and he invaded Constantinople. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8300 - True"
"8301","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Hashim bin Marthad told us, Sa`id bin Ufayr told us, Sa`id bin Abi Ayyub told us, on the authority of Abu Shortly before he told him, he heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them, saying: We remembered the conquest of Constantinople. And the Romans, so Abdullah bin Amr called for a box and he opened it and said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, writing, and a man said: Yes. Will the two cities be opened before, O Messenger of God? He said: “The city of Heraclius,” meaning the city of Constantinople. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8301 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8302","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul Hamid Al-San’ani told me about Mecca, which God Almighty protected, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Dabari told us, Abdul Razzaq reported, Muammar reported, on the authority of Abu Khuthaym, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Sabit, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Ka’b bin Ujrah: “May God protect you, O Ka’b, from the leadership of the fools.” He said: And what is the leadership of the fools? O Messenger of God? He said: “There will be princes after me who do not follow my guidance and do not follow my Sunnah. Whoever believes in their lies and helps them in their oppression, Those are not of me, and I am not of them, and they will not return to my coffin, and whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their injustice, those are of me. And I am one of them, and they will return to my basin. O Ka'b bin Ujrah, fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and prayer is an offering - or he said: proof -. O Ka’b bin Ujrah, meat that grew from evil will never enter Paradise, Hell is more deserving of it. O Ka’b ibn Ujrah, people are going astray, so someone buys his life and frees it - or he said: then he sets it free - “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8302 - True"
"8303","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Ubayd Allah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, On the authority of Saeed bin Hilal, on the authority of Aban bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i, may God be pleased with him, he said: While we are with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Battle of Tabuk, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in a cloak of human beings. When I passed by, he heard my voice, and he said: “O Awf bin Malik, come in. I said: O Messenger of God, should I eat or part of me? He said: “Rather, all of you.” He said: So I entered, and he said: “O Auf, enumerate six before the Hour.” I said: What are they, O Messenger of God? He said: “The death of the Messenger of God.” Awf cried, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Say: One.” I said: One, then he said: “And the house was opened.” The Holy Place, say: Two. I said: Two. He said: And death among my nation will be like the punishment of sheep. Say: Three. I said: Three. He said: And the world will be opened to them. Until a man is given a hundred and he is displeased with it, say: “Four,” I said: “Four,” “and a trial such that not one of the Muslims will remain without it entering his house. Say: Five. I said: Five. And there will be a truce between you and the Banu Asfar. They will come to you in eighty groups, each group twelve thousand. Then They deceive you to the point of impregnating a woman.” He said: When it was the year of Emmaus, they claimed that Awf bin Malik said to Muadh bin Jabal: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said to me: “Number six before the Hour.” There were three of them and three remained, so Mu’adh said: This will have a period of time, but five Overshadowing you are those of them who attained any of them and then were able to die. Let them die: for the cursers to appear on the pulpits, and to be given God’s wealth for lying. And slander and unjust shedding of blood, and relatives will be cut off, and the servant becomes lost, not knowing whether he is misguided or guided. This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it in this context.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8303 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8304","Muhammad ibn Ali al-San’ani informed us of Mecca, protected by God Almighty. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juni, Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Hakim Al-Dahqan informed us of Marw. Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Ibrahim Al-Sadusi informed us, narrated to us: Saeed bin Hubayra, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Abu Imran al-Juniy told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Abu Dharr, what do you do if people are hungry to the point that you are not able to get from your mosque to Your bed, or from your bed to your mosque? He said: I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “Be chaste.” Then he said: “How do you do when people die so that the house is empty?” He said: I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “Be patient.” Then he said: “What do you do when people come and attack those of high rank with bloodshed?” He said: I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “You come to whomever you are from.” I said: So if he comes to me? He said: “If you fear that the beam of the sword will dazzle you, then throw a piece of your cloak over your face, and he will carry your sin and his sin, and he will be among the companions of Fire.” I said: Should I not carry a weapon? He said: “Then you share with him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and Al-Bukhari narrated it from the hadith of Hammam, on the authority of Abu Imran, and he added in it. Its chain of transmission is between Abu Imran al-Juni and Abdullah bin al-Samit al-Mushath bin Tarif, with an addition in the text, and Hammad bin Zayd is more reliable than Hammad. Ibn Salama """"
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8304 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8305","Al-Hasan bin Hakim told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim Al-Sadusi told us, Saeed bin Hubayra told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, Abu Imran told us Al-Juni, on the authority of Al-Mush’ath ibn Tarif, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “O Abu Dharr.” I said: At your service, O Messenger of God, and your two Sa’ds. He said: “How do you do when people are afflicted with hunger? You come to your mosque but are not able That you return to your bed, and come to your bed and are not able to get up to your mosque.” I said: God and His Messenger know best - or what God has chosen for me. And His Messenger. He said: “You must maintain chastity.” Then he said: “O Abu Dharr.” I said: At your command, O Messenger of God, and I am pleased with you. He said: “How are you when you see Are the stones of oil identified with blood? I said: God and His Messenger did not choose. He said: “Catch up with whoever you are from - or he said: You must follow whoever you are from -” I said: Should I not take my sword and put it on On me? He said: “Then I participated.” I said: What do you command me to do? He said: “You stay at home.” I said: What do you think if he enters my house? He said: “If you fear that the beam of the sword will dazzle you, then throw your cloak over your face, and he will carry his sin and your sin.”"
"8306","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told me, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, on the authority of his father, that he heard Abu Tha’labah al-Khushani, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “God will not make this nation weak for half a day.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. """"
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8306 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8307","What Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Muhammad bin Al-Mutawakkil Al-Asqalani told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Maryam reported, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It will not be impossible for me before my Lord to postpone my nation for half a day.” It was said: What is half a day? He said: “Five hundred years.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"8308","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “A time will come upon you in which only those who pray will be saved.” “The supplication of drowning” This is an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8308 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8309","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman Al-Asbahani told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Damra bin Habib, that Ibn Zughb al-Iyadi narrated to him, saying: It was revealed to Abdullah bin Hawwala al-Azdi, and he said to me And he is descending upon me in my house: You have no mother. Isn’t it enough for a son of about a hundred to be given to him every year? Then he said: We sent the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, went around the city on our feet to take sheep. We returned but did not take any sheep. He saw the distress on our faces, so he spoke to us and said: “O God, do not leave them to me, lest I be weak in their charge, and do not leave them to themselves, lest they are unable to do it, and do not leave them to the people. So they gain influence over them.”
Then he said: “You will conquer the Levant and Persia - or the Romans and Persia - until one of you has such-and-such camels and such-and-such cows, until “One of you is given a hundred dinars and he becomes angry with her.”
Then he placed his hand on my head - or on my head - and said: “O Ibn Hawalah, if you see the Caliphate descending on the Holy Land, then you will Earthquakes, afflictions, and great matters. On that day, the Hour will be closer to the people than this hand of yours. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. He brought it out, and Abd al-Rahman bin Zugb al-Ayadi is well-known among the followers of the people of Egypt.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8309 - True"
"8310","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told me, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Abdul Hamid bin told us Ja`far, on the authority of Salih ibn Abi Urayb, on the authority of Kathir ibn Murrah, on the authority of Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, went out to them with containers hanging, and a portion of them was filled with a stick, and he had with him a stick. He stabbed the container with the stick and said: “If the Lord had willed.” “This charity is better than anything else. The one who gives this charity will eat dirt on the Day of Resurrection.” Then he came to us and said: “As for By God, O people of Medina, you will leave it humiliated for forty years according to Al-Awafi.” We said: God and His Messenger know best. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Do you know what Al-Awafi is?” They said: No. He said: “Birds and wild beasts.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8310 - True"
"8311","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Barni told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Maslamah told us, on the authority of Malik, On the authority of Yunus bin Yusuf bin Hamas, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Let Medina be abandoned.” “On the best of what birds and wild animals ate.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it, so let the seeker of this knowledge know that Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman was the confidant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he used to say: People used to ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about Good, and I used to ask him about evil for fear that I would fall into it, and it might be hidden from me except the knowledge of some scholarly council about some of the ailments of that kind. “It was hidden from Hudhayfah who would expel the people of Medina from the city, and someone else taught him.” The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, agreed on the hadith. Shu'bah, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed me And peace be upon him for what is going on until the Day of Resurrection. There is nothing of it that I did not ask him about, except that I did not ask him what would bring out the people of ""The city from the city""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8311 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8312","Mukarram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, Al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Othman bin Omar told us, Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Utbah, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “You are fighting the Arabian Peninsula.” Then God will grant them victory, then you will fight the Romans and God will grant them victory, then you will fight Persians and God will grant them victory, then you will fight the Antichrist and God will grant him victory.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8312 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8313","Professor Abu Al-Walid told me, Al-Haytham bin Khalaf Al-Duri told us, Al-Haytham bin Kharijah told us, Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr. Bin Abdullah bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid bin Qutayb Al-Sakouni, on the authority of Abu Bahria, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal May God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The great epic, the conquest of Constantinople, and the emergence of the Antichrist in seven months.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8313 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8314","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani told me about Mecca, which God Almighty guarded. Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, Abd told us Al-Razzaq, Muammar reported, on the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of Amr bin Wabisa Al-Asadi, on the authority of his father, he said: I am in Kufa in my home, when... I heard at the door of the house: Peace be upon you, what? So I said: And peace be upon you, and when he entered, it was Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, so I said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, what is the meaning of this? This was the hour of the visit - and that was in the afternoon - he said: The day had been long, so I remembered who I was speaking to, so he started talking to me about the Messenger of God. And I spoke to him. He said: Then he started speaking to me and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There will be a trial.” The one who sleeps in it is better than the one who lies down, and the one who lies down in it is better than the one who sits, and the one who sits in it is better than the one who stands, and the one who stands is better than the one who walks, and the one who walks is better than the one who is riding, and the one who is riding is better than the one running.” I said: O Messenger of God, and when is that? He said: “Those are the days of turmoil, when a man who sits with him will not be safe.” I said: What do you command me to do if I reach that time? He said: “Brace yourself and your hand and enter your house.” He said: I said: O Messenger of God, what do you think if he enters my house? He said: “Then enter your house.” He said: I said: What do you think if he enters my house? He said: “Then enter your mosque and do thus - and he held the elbow with his right hand - and say, ‘My Lord is God, until you die in this’.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8314 - True"
"8315","Abu Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahboubi informed us, Sa`id ibn Masoud informed us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Khams ibn al-Hasan informed us, On the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq Al-Uqaili, on the authority of Muhjan bin Al-Adra’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me for a need, then he opposed me in Some of the ways of the city, then he went up to Uhud, and I went up with him, and he turned with his face toward the city, and he said to it a word. Then he said, “Woe to your mother! Or woe to its mother - a town whose people abandon it wherever it may be, and it is eaten by healthy birds and wild beasts, and its fruit is eaten, and the Antichrist will not enter it unless God willing, whenever he wanted to enter her, he would meet him with every veil of hers, an angel of worship, preventing him from her. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it was not ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8315 - True"
"8316","Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Nahwi told us in Baghdad, Ahmad ibn Ziyad ibn Mahran told us, Shazan al-Aswad ibn Amir told us, Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ezra, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ubayy Ibn Ka'b, may God be pleased with him, said in this verse: {And We will certainly make them taste of the lesser punishment, apart from the greater punishment} [Al-Sajdah: 21] He said: “The calamities of this world are rum, oppression, or smoke,” he said: Then something stopped, and he said: “He is the Antichrist.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not They bring it out. I asked Abu Ali Al-Hafiz about this Ezra, and he said: Ezra bin Yahya. Shu’bah narrated, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ezra. Bin Tamim """"
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8316 - True"
"8317","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told me, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Imran bin Abi Imran told us Al-Sufi, Sadaqa bin Al-Muntasir narrated to us, Yahya bin Abi Amr Al-Sibani narrated to me, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami, Wathilah narrated to me Ibn Al-Asqa’, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “The Hour will not come until there are ten signs: an eclipse.” In the East, and an eclipse in the West, and an eclipse in the Arabian Peninsula, and the Antichrist, and smoke, and the descent of Jesus, son of Mary, and Gog and Magog, And the animal, and the rising of the sun from the west, and a fire emerging from the depths of Aden, driving the people to the gathering place, gathering together the atoms and the ants. “This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8317 - True"
"8318","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Shabib, on the authority of Garqada, on the authority of Al-Mustadhil ibn al-Husayn said: I heard Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, saying: “I have known, by the Lord of the Kaaba, when the Arabs will perish: then my guardian Their issue was that of those who did not accompany the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, and did not deal with the matter of pre-Islamic times. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8318 - True"
"8319","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Suleiman Al-Saadi told us, Aoun bin Amara told us Al-Abdi, Abdullah bin Al-Muthanna narrated to me, on the authority of his grandfather Thumama, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Qatada, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The verses after the two generations.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8319 - I consider it fabricated"
"8320","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi told us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim Al-Shadhuri told us, Saeed bin Hubayra told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Yahya told us Ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abu al-Tufayl, he said: Hudhayfah said: “How are you when the best of its people is a trial in which every rich person is hidden?” He said: I said: By God, it is nothing but the gift of someone who is asleep. We are thrown here and there, and we shoot at every target. He said: “Aren’t you like the son of milk? “A riding woman and she will be ridden, or a milking woman and she will be milked.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8320 - True"
"8321","Ali bin Issa told me, Musaddad bin Qattan Al-Qushayri told us, Othman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn al-Qibtiyya, who said: Al-Harith ibn Abi Rabi’ah, Abdullah ibn Safwan, and I with them entered Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with them. On her behalf, he asked her about the army that was being defeated. This was in the days of Ibn al-Zubayr, and Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: “A seeker seeks refuge in the Sanctuary, and an army is sent to it, and when they are deserted on the ground, they are swallowed up.” So I said: O Messenger of God, how about someone who goes out unwillingly? He said: “He will be eclipsed with them, but he will be raised to his intention on the Day of Resurrection.” Then she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He seeks refuge, he seeks refuge.” “By the House.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8321 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8322","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Shayban Al-Ramli told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Umayyah bin Safwan bin Abd Allah bin Safwan heard his grandfather Abdullah bin Safwan say: Hafsa, may God be pleased with her, told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he greeted him and said: “Let this house be secured by an army that will attack it, until when they are far from the land, it will cover the middle of them, and the first of them will be called. The last of them, and they will be completely destroyed, and no one will be saved except the fugitive who tells about them.” Then a man said to him: “I bear witness against you that you did not lie to your grandfather. “I bear witness that your grandfather did not lie to Hafsa, and I bear witness that Hafsa did not lie to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8322 - True"
"8323","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told me about Hamdan, and I asked him. Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Omar bin Hafs bin Ghiyath Al-Nakhai, my father told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Talha bin Musarrif, on the authority of Abu Muslim Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The mission will not cease invading the House of God Almighty until it is overwhelmed by an army of them.” This is a strange and authentic hadith. And they did not narrate it. I do not know of anyone who narrated it except Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath, on whose authority Imam Abu Hatim narrated it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8323 - Al-Dhahabi said: Sahih Ghareeb"
"8324","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid Al-Bayruti told us, Muhammad bin Shuaib bin Shapur told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, that he heard Sulaym bin Amer, saying: I heard Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad Al-Kindi, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Not a single house of mud or barren will remain on the face of the earth without God introducing the word to them. Islam with the honor of the Mighty, or with the humiliation of the humble. May God honor them and make them among its people, or humiliate them so that they do not submit to it. This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8324 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8325","Muhammad bin Al-Mu’mil bin Al-Hasan told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Hariz bin Othman, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Awf bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “My nation will divide into seventy-four sects, the largest of which will be a sect of people who measure matters according to their opinion and prohibit what is permissible and permit what is permissible. “Forbidden.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"8326","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Al-Yaman Al-Hakam bin Nafi’ told us, Safwan bin Amr, Sulaym bin Amir told us, on the authority of Tamim al-Dari, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Let them convey this The matter lasts for the duration of the night and the day, and God does not leave a house of mud or wool without this religion entering it with the glory of the mighty, or with the humiliation of the lowly, honoring with glory. God is in Islam, and He is humiliated by it in disbelief.” Tamim Al-Dari, may God be pleased with him, used to say: “I have learned of this among my family. It has befallen those who He is safe from among them goodness, honor, and glory, and whoever is an unbeliever has befallen humiliation, small children, and tribute. This is an authentic hadith, subject to the condition. The two sheikhs, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8326 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8327","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Suleiman bin Maysarah, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: “You are in A time in which one who speaks the truth is better than one who is silent, and one who stands is better than one who sits, and that after you there is a time in which one who is silent is better than one who speaks, and one who sits in it. Better than the one who is standing.” He said: Then a man said: O Abu Abdul-Rahman, how will the matter be? Whoever follows it today is guidance, and whoever follows it after Was today a mistake? He said: “You have done it. Think of it as two men who passed by a people who were committing sins, and they both disapproved of it, and one of you remained silent and greeted, and the other spoke. He said: You do and you do, so they took him and took him to their ruler, and he continued - or they did not stop - with him until he took him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8327 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8328","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein Al-Hamdani told us, Omar bin Asim Al-Kalabi told us, Abu Al-Awwam Al-Qattan told us, Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He pledges allegiance to a man from my nation between the Corner and the Maqam, like the number of the people of Badr, so the Asab of Iraq will come to him, and the replacements of the Levant will come to them, and an army from the Levant will come to them.” Until, when they were in Al-Bayda, they were destroyed, then a man from Quraysh whose uncle was a dog would march towards him, and God would defeat them. He said: “And it was said: “The one who is disappointed on that day is he who is disappointed by the spoils of a dog.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8328 - Abu Al-Awwam Imran’s weakness was more than one, and it was external"
"8329","Suleiman bin Bilal narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir bin Zaid, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, with a chain of transmission traceable to the Prophet: “The deprived of “The spoils of a dog are forbidden, even if they are a headband. By the One in whose hand is my soul, their women will be sold on the steps of Damascus, until the woman is restored from a wound found in her leg.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8329 - True"
"8330","Hamza bin Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl bin Al-Harith Al-Aqbi told us in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Saeed bin Amir told us, Abu Amer Saleh bin Rustum, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Qart, who said: I entered the mosque and saw a ring as if Their heads were cut off, and a man was among them speaking. Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, said: They were asking the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. About good, and I used to ask him about evil so that I would know it and fear it, and I knew that good would not escape me. He said: So I said: O Messenger of God, is he still Is this good that we are from evil? He said: “O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of God Almighty and act according to what is in it.” So I repeated my statement to him, and he said the third time: “Sedition and disagreement.” I said: O Messenger God, is there any good after that evil? He said: “O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of God Almighty and act according to what is in it.” So I said: O Messenger of God, is there any good after that evil? He said: “At its doors will be temptations that will lead to Hellfire. For you to die biting on the trunk of a tree is better for you than to follow one of them.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8330 - True"
"8331","Muhammad ibn Ali al-San’ani told us, about Mecca that God Almighty protected, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Ghayath told us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he informed us Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Sarjis, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “O people, Trials have overshadowed you as if they were pieces of a dark night. O people, therein - or he said: from it - a owner of a sheep eating from the head of his sheep, and a man from... Behind the path, he was taking his horse by the reins, eating from his sword.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8331 - Sahih Mawqoof"
"8332","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Nasr bin Asim, on the authority of Subay bin Khalid, said: I went out to Kufa at a time when cover was opened to bring mules from there, so I entered The mosque, and if there is a crack from men, you know when you see them that they are from the Hijaz. He said: I said: Who is this? He said: The people stared at me with their eyes and said: What do you know about this? This is Hudhayfah, the confidant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, said: The people were asking the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, about good, and I was asking him about evil. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, do you think this good that God has given us will come after it? Evil as it was before? He said: “Yes.” I said: O Messenger of God, what is the protection from that? He said: “The sword.” I said: Does the sword have any remnants? He said: “Yes.” He said: I said: Then what? He said: “Then a truce for Dukhan.” He said: “A group against a group. If God Almighty had a caliph on that day, He would strike your back and take What is the matter with you? Listen and obey, otherwise you will die biting a tree trunk.” He said: I said: Then what? He said: “The Antichrist will come out with a river and fire. Whoever falls into his fire will receive his reward and will be relieved of his burden, and whoever falls into his river will bear his burden and will be removed. His reward.” I said: Then what? He said: “Then it is only the coming of the Hour.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8332 - True"
"8333","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, On the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahb, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “Sedition has pauses and hardships, so whoever of you is able to die In its pauses, let him do it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8333 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8334","Al-Hasan bin Hakim Al-Maruzi told me, Ahmad bin Ibrahim Al-Shadhuri told us, Saeed bin Hubayra told us, Muhammad bin Sulaym told us, Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq al-Uqaili, on the authority of Murrah al-Bahzi, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Trials will be opened on the earth.” Like a hunter of cows.” Then a masked man passed by and said: “This is the day upon the truth.” So I got up to him and took hold of the hem of his garment, and said: This is him. O Messenger of God? He said: “This,” he said: Then it is Uthman. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8334 - Saeed bin Hubayra was accused by Ibn Hibban"
"8335","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Sakan told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Wahib bin Khaled told us, Musa bin Uqba told me, my maternal grandfather, Abu Habiba, told me that he entered the house while Othman, may God be pleased with him, was confined there. And he heard Abu Hurairah asking Othman for permission to speak, so he allowed him, so he stood up and thanked God Almighty and praised him, then he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “After me you will encounter strife and disagreement - or he said: disagreement and strife -” Then someone said to him: O Messenger of God. What do you command us to do? He said: “You should take care of the prince and his companions,” and he was referring to Uthman, may God be pleased with him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8335 - True"
"8336","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith, that Bakr ibn Sawada al-Judhami narrated to him, that Suhaim narrated to him, on the authority of Ruwaifa ibn Thabit al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, that He said: Dates and dates were offered to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they ate from them until nothing was left except a pit and nothing good in it, so the Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Do you know what this is? “You take away the good and the good, until nothing remains of you except the like of this.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8336 - True"
"8337","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati, and Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad, they said: Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Yunus bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Humaid, that He heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You will be picked just as dates are picked from a bud.” So let the best of you go and let the evil of you remain, so die if you can.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “And there is another narration.” On the authority of Yunus bin Yazid
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8337 - True"
"8338","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Imran told us. Al-Ansari, Talha bin Yahya Al-Zarqi narrated to us, Yunus bin Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Humaid, the servant of Musafa’, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, says: It is narrated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You will be picked just as dates are picked from a bud. Let your good people go and your evil ones remain, until only those whom God does not care about remain, so die if you are able. This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not take it out.”"
"8339","He has another narration on the authority of Yunus bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Humaid, that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, say: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You will be picked just as dates are picked from a bunch. Let the best of you go and the worst of you remain, so that they do not Only those whom God does not care about remain, so die if you can.”"
"8340","Abu Aoun Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahan al-Jazzar in Mecca, may God Almighty guarded it, told us at al-Safa, dictating to us. Abu Abdullah Muhammad told us Bin Ali bin Zaid Al-Sayegh Al-Makki told us, Saeed bin Mansour Al-Makki told us, Yaqoub bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Amara bin Hazm bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A time will soon come when the The people therein will be sifted, and what will remain is scum of people, whose covenants and trusts have been nullified, and they disagreed, and were like this.” He interlaced his fingers, They said: How do you command us, O Messenger of God? He said: “You take what you know and leave what you deny, and you accept the affairs of your elite and abandon the affairs of your common people.” Saeed bin Mansour said: “The scum of the people: their poor quality, and the meaning of his saying: Their covenants were canceled because they did not fulfill them.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8340 - True"
"8341","Ahmed bin Uthman bin Yahya bin Amr Al-Bazzar told us in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqashi told us, Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Warith, Hammam told us, Qatada told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Hour will not come until God Almighty takes His portion from the people of the earth, and there remain people who do not know.” ""This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, if Al-Hasan heard it from Abdullah bin Amr.""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8341 - According to the condition of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, if Al-Hasan is connected on the authority of Abdullah"
"8342","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Isfahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, On the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “There will be princes who will torture you and God will punish them.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8342 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8343","On the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “They still Fine, as long as you do not have princes over you who do not see you as having rights unless they want. This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of the two Sheikhs with all the chains of transmission.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8343 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8344","Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Aflah bin Saeed, a sheikh from the people of Quba told us, Abdullah bin Rafi’, the client of Umm Salamah, told me: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If you have been with you for a long time, you will soon see a people They will be exposed to the wrath of God in the morning, and they will go to His curse in their hands like the tails of cows.” This hadith has an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8344 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8345","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Abu Al-Mawjih told us, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Nafi’ informed. Ibn Omar Al-Jumahi, on the authority of Umayyah Ibn Safwan, on the authority of Abu Bakr Ibn Abi Zuhair Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in his sermon: “O people, you are about to recognize the people of Paradise from the people of Hell - or he said: Your choice is from The worst of you - “Then a man from among the people said: Why, O Messenger of God?” He said: “By good praise and bad praise, you are witnesses to one another.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8345 - True"
"8346","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Harun bin Marouf told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Wahb, Abdullah Ibn Ayyash Al-Qatbani told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Issa Ibn Hilal Al-Sadfi, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr Radi God said about them, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “At the end of this nation there will be men who will ride on wet-waters until they come. The doors of their mosques, their women clothed and naked on their heads like the lean humps of a camel, their curses, for they are cursed, if There was a group of Gentiles behind you, to serve you just as the women of the nations served you before you. So I said to my father: What is al-Miyathir? He said: “Bone saddles.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"8347","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Dhuhli told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal, Abdullah bin Bujayr told us, Sayyar bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “There will emerge from this nation at the end of time men bearing whips, as if they were the tails of cows. They will be in the wrath of God, and they will go away.” “In his anger” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8347 - True"
"8348","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, that he mentioned sedition, and said: “The man To leave his house with his debt, and come back with nothing of it. A man comes to him, neither for him nor for himself, neither harm nor benefit, and he apportions to him. By God, you have had pleasure and you have given, and the one who was free of his need for something will return, and God has been displeased with him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8348 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8349","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah Al-Hamdani told me, Al-Qasim bin Al-Hakam Al-Arni told us, Sulayman bin Abi Sulayman told us, Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “By the One who sent me with the truth, it will not be over. This world until eclipse, distortion, and slander befall them. They said: When will that be, O Prophet of God? May my father and mother be sacrificed for you? He said: “If you see women riding saddles, and many blasphemes, and false testimony being witnessed, and Muslims drinking gold from the vessels of the polytheists, And silver, and the men were enriched by the men, and the women by the women, so turn your backs and prepare.” And he said: Thus he raised his hand and covered his face.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8349 - Suleiman is Al-Yamami, weak and weak, and the report is objectionable"
"8350","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Hamid al-San’ani informed me, in Mecca, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Muammar informed me, on the authority of Tariq Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Mundhir al-Thawri, on the authority of Asim Ibn Damra, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Five temptations have been created in this nation: A general tribulation, then a specific tribulation, then a general tribulation, then a specific tribulation, then comes the blind, deaf, and absolute tribulation that People therein will become like livestock. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8350 - True"
"8351","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr told me, Muawiyah ibn Amr told me, Abu Ishaq told us Al-Fazari, on the authority of Al-A’mash, who said: Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Abu Thawr, who said: I gave to Hudhayfah and Ibn Masoud, and they are They were talking in the mosque, and they mentioned the sedition, and Ibn Masoud said: “I did not see her turning on her heels without a cup of blood spilled on her. A man may become a believer in the morning and be an unbeliever in the evening, and he will be an unbeliever in the morning and be a believer in the evening. He fights in strife today and God will kill him tomorrow. He will be defeated. Before him, then you will exalt his burden.” Then Hudhayfah said: “You are right. This is what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us about the strife. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not take him out, and this Abu Thawr is one of the major followers, and Abu Al-Bakhtari has overtaken Hudhayfah.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8351 - True"
"8352","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, who said: A sheikh told me that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A time will come upon the people. In it, a man is given the choice between impotence and immorality, so whoever realizes that time should choose impotence over immorality.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. They narrate it: “And the sheikh who was not named Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, is Sa’id bin Abi Khayra.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8352 - True"
"8353","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan bin Maimun told us, Saeed bin Sulayman told us, Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abu Hind, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Khayrah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He will come upon the people.” “A time in which a man will have to choose between impotence and immorality. Whoever among you realizes that time should choose impotence over immorality.”"
"8354","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Abdullah bin Salih told me, Muawiyah bin Saleh, Abu Al-Zahiriyya told me, on the authority of Kathir ibn Murrah, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “My nation will be covered after me with temptations like pieces of a dark night. A man will become a believer in the morning and an unbeliever by evening, and he will be a believer in the evening and become an unbeliever in the evening. He will sell... A people whose religion is a little bit of the world” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and he did not narrate it “and its witness is the hadith that defines this text.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8354 - True"
"8355","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, and Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Yaqoub told us Nasr, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith and Ibn Lahi’ah told me, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Sinan bin Saad, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “Before the Hour is temptation like pieces of a dark night. A man will be a believer in the morning and an unbeliever in the evening, and a believer in the evening and will be an unbeliever in the evening. Some people will sell their religion for a small sum of this world.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8355 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8356","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari informed us about Marwa, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Saeed bin Iyas informed us. Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Firas, said: Omar ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: “O people, we knew you when Among us is the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and when the revelation was sent down, and when some of your news was shared between us. Indeed, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had set out And the revelation was lifted up, and we only make known to you what I tell you: And whoever of you shows good, we think good of him and love him for it. An evil which we thought was an evil and we abhorred it because of your secrets between you and your Lord. Indeed, a time has come upon me when I think that he has read the Qur’an. What he means by it is God Almighty and what he has, and it has occurred to me at the end of it that some people are reading it wanting what people have. Indeed, they mean what God has. By your reading and your work, by God, I am not sending my workers to beat your people and take your money, but I am sending them That they may teach you your religion and your Sunnahs, and be just among you, and divide among you among you. Except whoever has had any of these things done to him, let him bring it to Me, by the One Omar’s soul is in his hand so that I can cut it off from him.” Then Amr ibn Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, jumped up and said: O Commander of the Faithful, have you seen if a man from He was among his subjects, and he disciplined some of his subjects. Indeed, you can cut it from him. He said: “Why should I not tell it when I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace?” And he said to himself, “Do not strike them and humiliate them, do not withhold their rights lest you make them disbelieve, do not force them to tempt them, and do not “You send them down in the rain and waste them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8356 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8357","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marw, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumayl told us, Muhammad informed us Ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Woe to the Arabs because of the evil that has “Death is drawing near, if you can.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8357 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8358","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sana'ani told me about Mecca, which God Almighty protected, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar informed us, On the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: “Sedition broke out, and the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, numbered ten thousand, and no one was afraid of it except some of them. Forty men, and two hundred and forty-four men from the people of Badr stood with Ali, including Abu Ayyub, Sahl bin Hunaif, and Ammar bin Yessir"
"8359","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Al-Harith Al-Dimashqi, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “The matter does not increase except in distress, nor does wealth increase except in abundance, and the Hour does not establish except against the wickedest of its creation.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it was not ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8359 - True"
"8360","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, Abu Dawud Sulayman bin al-Ash’ath al-Sijistani told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Abd al-Wahid told us Ibn Ziyad, Asim Al-Ahwal narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Kabshah, who said: I heard Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Indeed, before you are temptations like pieces of a dark night, during which a man will be a believer in the morning and an unbeliever in the evening, and a believer in the evening will be an unbeliever. He who sits in it is better than one who stands, and he who stands in it is better than one who walks, and he who walks in it is better than one who runs towards it. They said: What do you command us, O Messenger of God? He said: “Be the caretaker of your homes.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and he did not narrate it. “And this is how it was narrated by Abu Bakra Al-Ansari and Saad bin Malik, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8360 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8361","So Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, Abu Dawud al-Sijistani told us, Sulaiman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, and Ahmad told us Bin Sulaiman, Abu Dawud told us, Sahl bin Bakkar told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, all on the authority of Uthman al-Shaham, on the authority of Muslim bin Abi Bakra, He said: I heard Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, there will be tribulations, and then there will be tribulations.” The one who sits in it is better than the one who stands, the one who stands in it is better than the one who walks, and the one who walks in it is better than one who runs towards it, so when it descends, then whoever has camels Let him follow his camels, and whoever has sheep, let him follow his sheep, and whoever has land, let him follow his land.” Then a man said to him: Oh. Messenger of God, what did you see if he had neither camels nor sheep nor land? He said: “Let him take a stone and strike it at the edge of his sword, then escape if he can.” Then he said: “O God, have I conveyed the message” three times, and a man said: O Messenger of God, what do you think if I were forced to be taken to one of the two rows - or to one of the two groups - and a man would shoot me with an arrow or hit me? With a sword and he will kill me. He said: “He will commit his sin and your sin, and he will be one of the inmates of the Fire.” He said it three times.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8361 - True"
"8362","So Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Abu Dawud told us, Amr bin Aoun told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Othman Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Saad bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It will be a trial for the one sitting in it.” is better than one who stands, and one who stands in it is better than one who walks, and one who walks in it is better than one who runs, and one who runs is better than one who rides, and one who rides is better than one who places” and this The hadith is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it. This has become a major chapter and they did not narrate it. Rather, it was narrated by Abu Dawud, one of the imams. This knowledge
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8362 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8363","Issa bin Zayd bin Issa bin Abdullah bin Muslim bin Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel bin Abi Talib told us, Yunus bin Abd told us Al-A’la Al-Sadafi, Muhammad bin Idris Al-Shafi’i, may God be pleased with him, told us, Muhammad bin Khalid Al-Jundi told us, on the authority of Aban bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The matter does not increase except in distress, nor does the debt increase except in distress.” And the people are nothing but stingy, and the Hour will not come except on the worst of people, and there is no Mahdi except Jesus, son of Mary.” Samit bin Muadh said: I changed to The soldiers were two days’ march from Sana’a, so I went to a narrator of theirs and asked for this hadith and found it with him, on the authority of Muhammad bin Khalid Al-Jundi, on the authority of Aban bin Abi Ayyash, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a similar text was narrated on the authority of Abdul Al-Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace"
"8364","Al-Hasan bin Ali Al-Tamimi, may God have mercy on him, told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Dirhami told us, Mubarak Abu Suhaim, Abdul Aziz bin Suhaib told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “It will not increase Time is nothing but hardship, and the people will only increase in miserliness, and the Hour will not come except upon the most wicked of the people.” So I mentioned what I found of the reason for this hadith. Surprisingly and not as evidence in Al-Mustadrak on the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, it is more deserving of this hadith to mention it in this place.
The hadith of Sufyan Al-Thawri, Shu’bah, Za’ida, and other Muslim imams, on the authority of Asim Ibn Bahdala, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “The days and nights will not pass until a man reigns.” “From my family, his name will be the same as my name, and his father’s name will be the same as my father’s name, so he will fill the earth with equity and justice as it had been filled with oppression and injustice.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8364 - True"
"8365","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, said: “A time will come upon the people when they gather in the mosques when there is not a believer among them.” This is A hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8365 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8366","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali Al-Amiri told us, Abu Usama told us, Zaida told me, he said: I heard Al-A’mash He narrates, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Habib ibn Hamaz, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on a journey. When we returned, the people were in a hurry and entered Medina. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, asked about them, and he was told that they had hurried. To the city, and he said: “It is about to be called the best it has ever been. I wish I could see when a fire would emerge from Mount Warraq and illuminate the necks of the camels.” In Busra there are lamps like daylight.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “And it is witnessed by the hadith of Rafi’ al-Sulami, who
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8366 - True"
"8367","Ahmed bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad bin Al-Hasan Al-Awfi told us, Uthman bin Omar bin Faris told us, Abdul Hamid informed us Bin Ja'far, on the authority of Abu Ja'far Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, may God be pleased with them, on the authority of Rafi' bin Bishr Al-Sulami, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Fire emerges from the confinement of a torrent, moving at a slow pace. It lurks at night and moves during the day, coming and going. It is said: “The fire has come, O people, so go.” The fire said, “O people,” and they said, “The fire has departed, O people, so go. Whoever it overtakes, it will consume.” And it was narrated. On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in mentioning the signs of the Hour: the emergence of fire from the land of Hijaz, Asim bin Adi Al-Ansari, and Abu Hurairah And Abu Dhar al-Ghifari. It has been mentioned previously:
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8367 - Rafi’ bin Bishr Al-Sulami is unknown"
"8368","So Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Abaya told us Bin Bakr bin Abi Laila Al-Muzani, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Mujma’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Al-Badah bin Asim Al-Ansari told me, on the authority of his father, that he said: We asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Two things happened, so he said: “Where is Habs-Sil?” We said: We do not know, then a man from Banu Sulaym passed by me, and I said: Where did you come from? He said: From the imprisonment of a torrent, so I put on my shoes and went down to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, you asked us about the imprisonment. A flood, and we had no knowledge of it, and this man passed by me and I asked him, and he claimed that his family was afflicted by it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him. He greeted me and said: “Where are your family?” He said: By holding back a torrent, so he said: “Delay your family, for fire is about to emerge from it, illuminating the necks of camels in Busra.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8368 - Munkar"
"8369","So Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin al-Hajjaj bin Rushdin told us, my father told me, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab informed him that Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, informed him that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Hour will not come until a fire breaks out in the land of Hijaz, from which the necks of camels in Busra will be illuminated.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8369 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8370","Muhammad Ibn Ali Ibn Abd al-Hamid al-San’ani told me about Mecca, Ishaq Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Abbad told me, Abd al-Razzaq informed us. Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: It was said to Saad bin Abi Waqqas: Don’t you fight, for you are one of the people of the Shura Council, and you are more deserving of this. command from someone other than you. He said: “I will not fight until they bring me a sword that has eyes, a tongue, and two lips that distinguishes the unbeliever from the believer. I have fought and I know “Jihad, and I will not be of any benefit to myself if he is a better man than me.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8370 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8371","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Yahya told me Bin Ayyub, on the authority of Zaban bin Faid, on the authority of Sahl bin Muadh bin Anas, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “The nation will continue to adhere to the law unless three things appear among them: unless knowledge is taken away from them, the offspring of evil increase among them, and Among them are the saqaroon. They said: What are the saqaroon, O Messenger of God? He said: “There will be human beings at the end of time whose greeting will be between them when they meet and cursing.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8371 - Munkar"
"8372","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abd informed us Allah Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “My nation is a mercy nation, and there will be no punishment for it in the Hereafter. God has made its punishment in this world murder, earthquakes, and temptations.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8372 - True"
"8373","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl and Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, saying: Musa bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad told us, Muhammad bin Musab told us. Al-Qarqasa’i, Amara Al-Ma’awali narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “Lightnings will increase as the Hour approaches, and people will come in the morning and say, ‘Who was struck yesterday?’ They say, ‘So-and-so and so-and-so was struck.’” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"8374","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, said: It was said: O Abu Abdullah, what do you order us to do if the worshipers fight? He said: “I command you to look at the farthest house from your home and enter into it. If he enters upon you, you will say, ‘Behold, curse my iniquity and your iniquity,’ and you will be like a son.” Adam: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8374 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8375","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Sa’id bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sa’id bin Iyas told us Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’ bin Al-Shakheer, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Suhar Al-Abdi, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ The Hour will not come until some Arab tribes are eclipsed, and it is said: Who is left of the tribe of so-and-so?’” He said: “So I knew when he said tribes that they were the Arabs, because “The Persians are attributed to their villages” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8375 - True"
"8376","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Al-Hasan bin Amr told us Al-Fuqaimi, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “In my nation there is an eclipse “And distortion and slander.” If Abu al-Zubayr heard it from Abdullah bin Omar, then it is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8376 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8377","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, And he reported, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Sa`id bin Wahb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “It is as if I was riding a passenger who had descended between I show you, He came between orphans and widows, and what God bestowed upon their fathers, and said: “The money is ours.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8377 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8378","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Tajer told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Bashir bin Salman told us, on the authority of Sayyar Abi Al-Hakam, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, said: We were sitting with Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, and he came to his ear and said: It has risen. Prayer, so he stood up and we stood with him, so we entered the mosque and he saw people kneeling at the front of the mosque, so he said the takbir, bowed and walked, and we did the same as he did. He said: Then a man passed quickly and said: Peace be upon you, O Abu Abdul Rahman. Then he said: God has spoken the truth and conveyed the message to His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. So when we prayed He came back and went to his family, and we sat in his place waiting for him to come out, so we said to each other: Which of you should ask him? Tariq said: I am asking him, so Tariq asked him, and he said: The man greeted you, and you responded to him. God has spoken the truth and conveyed it to His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he said Abdullah: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, before the Hour is the delivery of the private goods, and the spread of commerce until the woman is helped.” Her husband is a merchant, until the man takes his money to the ends of the earth and comes back and says: I have not gained anything.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8378 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8379","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Amr bin Marzuq told us, Shu’bah reported, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abd al-A'la bin al-Hakam, a man from Bani Amir, on the authority of Kharijah bin al-Salt al-Burjami, who said: One day I entered the mosque with Abdullah, Then, when the people were bowing, a man passed by and greeted him, and he said: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth, God and His Messenger have spoken the truth, so I asked him about that, and he said: “It is not The Hour will come until the mosques will be occupied by roads, until a man will greet another man with knowledge, until a woman and her husband will trade, and until she will go to extremes. Horses and women, then be generous, so do not go to extremes until the Day of Resurrection. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. These words were attributed by Bashir ibn Salman in his narration, “Then the hadith according to this narration of Shu’bah became authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8379 - Suspended"
"8380","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sana'ani informed me of Mecca, which God Almighty protected, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed me, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Muammar informed me, On the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The best of people in A temptation is a man riding by the reins of his horse - or he said: by the reins of his horse - behind the enemies of God, frightening them and they fearing him, or a man secluded in his desert. He fulfills the rights of God Almighty who owe him “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8380 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8381","Muhammad bin Ahmad al-Qantari told me in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, about the lions. Ibn Al-Ala’, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The night and the day do not pass away.” Until Al-Lat and Al-Uzza are worshipped.” Aisha said: So I said: O Messenger of God, I thought when God, Blessed and Most High, revealed: {It is He who sent His Messenger with guidance and the religion of truth, that He might make it prevail over all religions, even though the polytheists disliked it.} [At-Tawbah: 33] That this will be complete, and He said: “Indeed, it will happen.” Of that, as God wills, then God will send a pleasant wind, and whoever had in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of goodness will die, and there will remain those who do not “There is good in it, and they will return to the religion of their fathers.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8381 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8382","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Isfahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, On the authority of Humaid ibn Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Samit, he said: I wished that when my family had their supper and fell asleep in the morning, Dead on their beds. It was said: O father of so-and-so, are you not rich? He said: Yes, but I heard Abu Dharr say: “My nephew, if you live close by, you will soon see a man feeling happy with the lightness of the situation as he feels Today he is the father of ten men, and it is likely that, if you live nearby, you will see a man whom the ruler does not know, does not approach, and does not honor, become envied. Just as happy is the day when a ruler knows him, approaches him, and honors him, and my nephew, if you live nearby, is about to pass by the funeral in the market. Then the man raises his head and says: “I wish I were on the trees.” He said: I said: Do you know what's wrong with them? He said: “As it happened.” I said: This is a great matter before me. He said: “Yes, great, great, great.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not take him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8382 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8383","Abu Muhammad bin Ja`far bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, Safwan bin Saleh al-Dimashqi told us, And Muhammad bin Al-Musaffa Al-Homsi, they said: Mubashir bin Ismail Al-Halabi told us, Artaat bin Al-Mundhir told us, he said: I heard Damra bin Habib, He says: I heard Salama bin Nufayl Al-Sakouni, who was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: While we were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Then a man came and said: O Prophet of God, have you been brought food from heaven? He said: “I brought hot food.” He said: Did you have anything left over from it? He said: “Yes.” He said: What was done to him? He said: “He was raised up to heaven, and He revealed to me, ‘I will not remain among you except a little while, and you will not remain after me but a little. Rather, you will remain tarry until you say How long? Then you will come as rivals, and some of you will annihilate others, and before the Hour there will be two severe deaths, and after them will be years of earthquakes. This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8383 - The news is one of the oddities of Al-Sihah"
"8384","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Rayhan bin Saeed, Abbad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, Abu Asma’ told me, on the authority of Thawban, may God be pleased with him, that he heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Hour will not come upon my nation until tribes among them join the polytheists, and until tribes among them worship Idols
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8384 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8385","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sana'ani informed me of Mecca, which God Almighty protected, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed me, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Muammar informed me, On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amara ibn Abd, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: “Beware of temptations that no one is diagnosed with, for by God no one has been diagnosed with them.” Unless it wipes it up just as a torrent wipes up blood, it is similar to one coming, to the point that the ignorant person says, “This looks like one coming, and it will appear as one approaching.” So when you see it, gather in your homes, break your swords, cut your bowstrings, and cover your faces.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8385 - True"
"8386","Abu Abdullah al-San’ani told me, Ishaq told me, Abd al-Razzaq told me, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyib said: “The first strife broke out, and no one remained from those who witnessed Badr. Then the second sedition occurred, and no one remained from those who witnessed it.” Al-Hudaybiyyah, and I think that if there had been a third temptation, it would not have been lifted, and there was a cook among the people.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8386 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8387","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abu Shuraih told me, on the authority of Umair bin Abdul Al-Maafiri, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Hamq, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “There will be a trial.” The people were safest there - or he said: for the best people there - the Western Soldier “For that reason I brought this hadith to Egypt with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8387 - True"
"8388","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, and Al-Hasan informed us Ibn Salih, on the authority of Simak Ibn Harb, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Samurah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “This will continue “The religion will stand and the Muslims will fight for it until the Hour comes.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8388 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8389","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Al-Walid told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There will still be a sect From my nation, they will prevail upon the truth until the Hour comes.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and no one narrated it. “It was narrated by Thaban and Imran bin Husayn. On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8389 - True"
"8390","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Ishaq bin Idris told us, Aban bin Yazid told us, Yahya bin Abi Kathir, Abu Qalaba Abdullah bin Zaid Al-Jarmi told us, Abu Asma Al-Rahbi told me, that Thawban told him, that He heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, my Lord has increased the earth for me until I have seen its easts and its wests, and He has given me two treasures. Red and white, and indeed my nation’s dominion will reach what has been set aside for me of it, and indeed I asked my Lord for my nation not to destroy it with a common law. So he gave it to me, and I asked him not to let an enemy of others dominate them, so he gave it to me, and I asked him not to let them taste the oppression of one another. So he prevented her from doing so, and said: O Muhammad, if I make a decree and it is not rejected, I have given you a guarantee for your nation that I will not destroy it according to a common law, nor will I prevail over them. Enemy from others, so He makes them permissible in general, even if those in its regions come together to the point that some of them are destroyed, some are taken captive, And I do not fear for my nation except the misguided Imams, and the Hour will not come until tribes from my nation join the polytheists, and until tribes from My nation of idols, and when the sword is placed among my nation, it will not be removed from it until the Day of Resurrection.”And he said: “Everything that exists in a hundred years, and thirty liars will emerge among my nation, all of them claiming to be a prophet, and I am the Seal of the Prophets. There is no prophet after me, but there will still remain in my nation a group fighting for the truth, victorious. They will not be harmed by those who abandon them, until the command of God comes.” He said: He claimed that “no man from the people of Paradise will take away any of its fruit unless God will replace it with something like it,” and that he said: “There is no dinar.” A man spends it with a greater reward than a dinar he spends on his family, then a dinar he spends on his horse for the sake of God, then a dinar he spends on... his companions in the path of God,” he said, and claimed, “that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, magnified the issue, and that when the Day of Resurrection The people of pre-Islamic times came carrying their idols on their backs, and their Lord, the Almighty and Majestic, asked them: What did you worship? So they say: Our Lord, you have not sent us a messenger, and no matter has come to us, and if You had sent us a messenger, we would have been the most obedient of Your servants to You. So he says to them: Their Lord: Have you considered that if I command you to do a matter, will you obey me? He said: They say: Yes. He said: Then he takes their covenants on that, and orders them to baptize for Hell and enter it. He said: Then they go off until they reach it. They saw her getting angry and growling,So they were terrified and returned to their Lord, and said: Our Lord, separate us from it. Then He says: Did you not give me your covenants to obey me? Baptize them and enter. So they set off until when they saw it, they dispersed and turned back, saying: Our Lord, we are not able to enter it. He said: Then He said: Enter it gathered together. “He said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If they had entered it the first time, it would have been coolness and peace for them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He narrated it in this context, and Muslim only narrated the hadith of Muadh bin Hisham, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Abu Asma al-Rahbi, On the authority of Thawban in brief.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8390 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8391","So Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, and Hajjaj bin Minhaal, they said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And peace be upon him. He said: “A group of my nation will continue to fight for the truth, defeating those who opposed them, until the last of them fights the Antichrist.” This is an authentic hadith. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8391 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8392","Muhammad ibn Ali al-San’ani informed me of Mecca, which God Almighty protected. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abbad informed me. Abd al-Razzaq informed me. Muammar, on the authority of Aban bin Sulaym bin Qais Al-Hanathili, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, addressed us and said: “The thing I fear most is After me, it is upon you that the innocent man among you be taken, and he will be marked as the camels are, and his flesh will be split as their flesh is split, and he will be called a sinner, but he is not a sinner.” He said: Then Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said while he was under the pulpit: “When is that, O Commander of the Faithful?” And when the calamity becomes severe, fever appears, and the offspring are taken captive, and temptations strike them as a millstone strikes its dung, and as fire strikes wood? He said: “When is that, Ali?” He said: “If the scholar understands something other than religion, and the learner learns something other than work, and the world is sought by work for the hereafter.”
Aban said: Al-Hasan told us, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I fear chaos for you.” They said: What is the commotion, O Messenger of God? He said: “Killing.” They said: And more than what is being killed today. Indeed, we will kill such-and-such polytheists today, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said. He said: “It is not the killing of the polytheists, but the killing of one another.” They said: And in us is the Book of God? He said: “And among you is the Book of God Almighty.” They said: And with us are our minds? He said: “He is taking away the minds of the common people of that time, and leaving people in vain who think they are on to something but are not on anything.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8392 - Aban said that Ahmad abandoned his hadith"
"8393","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf Al-Qadi told us, Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Raqashi told us, Azhar bin Saad told us, Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Hayya, the daughter of Abi Hayya, who said: “A man entered upon me.” At noon I said: O Abdullah, what is your need? He said: “A companion of mine and I came to prostitute camels for us, so I went in to seek shade and drink from the drink.” So I got up and picked up a piece of sour milk and sour milk and gave it to drink, and I said: O Abdullah, who are you? He said: “I am Abu Bakr, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, whom I heard about.” He said: So I mentioned Khath’ma, and we attacked one another in Pre-Islamic times, and the familiarity that God has brought and the abundance of carpets - like this and interlacing his fingers - she said: So I said: O Abdullah, until when Are people like this? He said: “The imams are not upright.” She said: I said: What are the imams? He said: “Have you not seen the time when there is a master in which they follow him and obey him as long as those are upright?” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8393 - True"
"8394","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Halim bin Ibrahim bin Maymun Al-Sayegh informed us, Ahmad bin Ibrahim Al-Shadhuri informed us, Saeed bin Hubayra told us, Abdul-Warith bin Saeed told us, Muhammad bin Juhadah told us, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Kharijah, he said: When the first temptation made me difficult, I said: Oh God, show me something of the truth that I can adhere to. He said: So I was shown this world and the hereafter. There was a not long wall between them, and when I was passing by, I said: If I cling to this passerby, perhaps I will fall to the death of the bravest. So that they would inform me, he said: So I landed in a land full of trees, and behold, I saw a group of people sitting, so I said: Are you the martyrs? They said: No, we are the angels. I said: Where are the martyrs? They said: Proceed to the highest levels to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I approached, and behold, I am in the degree of God, I know what it is in terms of capacity and beauty. So when I am with Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Abraham, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he is saying to Abraham, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Ask forgiveness for my nation. So Ibrahim said to him: You do not know what they did after you. They shed their blood and killed their imam. Did they not do what my friend Saad did? I said: He showed me that I should go to Saad and see who he was with and be with him. So I came to him and told him the dream, but he was not overjoyed by it. And he said: “He is wretched who does not have Abraham as a friend.” I said: Which of the two sects do you fall into? He said: “I am not with either of them.” I said: How do you command me? He said: “Do you have any livestock?” I said: No. He said: “Then buy livestock and isolate yourself from them until they are clean.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8394 - True"
"8395","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, and Abu Abdullah told us Muhammad bin Yaqoub, the memorizer and the pronunciation of it, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Ishaq bin Suleiman Al-Razi told us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Dhi’ib, narrating on the authority of Sa’id bin Sam’an, said: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, narrating to Abu Qatada that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He said: “A man pledges allegiance between the Rukn and the Maqam, and no one will make this house lawful except its people. If they make it lawful, do not ask about the destruction of the Arabs. Then The Abyssinians will come and destroy it with such destruction that it will never last again, and they are the ones who will extract its treasure.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not take him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8395 - They did not report anything to Ibn Sim’an"
"8396","Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Al-Khurasani Al-Adl told us in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Malaab bin Hayyan told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Zuhair bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Musa bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave Abyssinia as long as they leave you, for no one can extract the treasure of the Kaaba except the one with the two stalks of “Abyssinia” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
They all agreed to narrate the hadith of Sufyan, on the authority of Wathhab bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The one from Abyssinia will destroy the Kaaba.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8396 - True"
"8397","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and Ahmad bin told me Jafar Al-Quta’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Ataba, narrating, on the authority of Abu Saeed, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The Hour will not come until Hajj is not performed.” “The House” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and it was authenticated by Abu Dawud, on the authority of Shu’bah.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8397 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8398","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, by God I know, it has been authenticated and proven, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The Hajj and Umrah is performed at the House after the departure of Gog and Magog.”"
"8399","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, told us by Aban bin Yazid Al-Attar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Ataba, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let the House be Hajj and Umrah performed after the departure of Gog and Magog, for it is possible to perform Hajj and Umrah after That, then the Hajj is interrupted once.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8399 - True"
"8400","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab told us, about Ata, Saeed bin Iyas told us Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, said: The people of Iraq are about to not receive a dirham or a dirham. Qafiz, they said: What is that, Abu Abdullah? He said: The non-Arabs are forbidding that, then he was silent for a while, then he said: The people of the Levant are about to receive neither a dinar nor a mud. They said: Why? That? He said: The Romans prevented that, then he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “In my nation there will be a caliph who will strive for wealth without counting it.” Except»
Then he said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the matter will return as it began, and all faith will return to Medina as it began from it, until all faith In the city »
Then he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No man leaves the city out of his desire for it, but God will replace it with something better than him. And let people hear of cheaper prices and a countryside and follow it, and the city is better for them, if they only knew. This is an authentic hadith according to Muslim’s conditions. They did not expel him in this manner.”
Muslim only narrated the hadith of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “It will happen at the end of time.” A caliph who gives money without counting it as a gift.” This has a reason, as it has
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8400 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8401","Ali bin Issa told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Abu Musa and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, they said: Abd al-Wahhab bin Abd told us. Al-Majeed, Dawud bin Abi Hind narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Jabir, or Abu Sa’id, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It will happen at the end of This nation has a caliph who divides the money without counting it as a caliph.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8401 - Narrated by Muslim"
"8402","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Salamah bin Kuhail, on the authority of Abu al-Za’ra’, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: “A time will come upon the people when a man will come to the grave.” So he lies on it and says: I wish I were in the place of his companion. He has no love of meeting God except when he sees severe affliction. “This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8402 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8403","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sana'ani told me about Mecca, which God Almighty protected, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told me, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Muammar told us about... Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Kurz ibn Alqamah al-Khuza’i, who said: A Bedouin said: O Messenger of God, does Islam have an end? He said: “Yes, whichever family, Arabs or non-Arabs, for whom God intends good, He will bring Islam to them.” They said: Then what, O Messenger of God? He said: “Then there will be tribulations as if they were shadows.” He said: Then a Bedouin said: No, O Messenger of God? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will return therein black and white, some of you striking the necks of one another.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it in this context.”"
"8404","Abu Uwais Al-Madani told us, Thawr bin Yazid and Musa bin Maysara told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “You will surely replace the traditions of those before you, hand span by hand span, and a cubit by a cubit, until one of them entered the den of a lizard.” You would have entered, and even if one of them had had intercourse with his wife on the road, you would have done it.” Sahih
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8404 - True"
"8405","Muammar told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi’ah, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A wind will come between... The Hour of the Hour will take the soul of every believer.” Sahih
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8405 - There is an interruption"
"8406","Ismail bin Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, And Abu Alqamah Al-Farwi said: Safwan bin Sulaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salman Al-Aghar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God sends from Yemen a wind softer than silk, so do not leave anyone in whose heart is the weight of A grain of faith except that I seized it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and he did not narrate it. “And it has a reliable witness on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8406 - True"
"8407","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali told us, Suleiman bin Harb told us, Imran Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Adam, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Hour will not come until God sends a wind that will not leave anyone in whose heart is the weight of An iota of piety or prohibition will be taken away from him, and every people will follow what their fathers worshiped in the pre-Islamic period, and there will remain a group of people who do not They enjoin what is right and do not forbid what is wrong. They marry on the roads as animals marry. If that happens, God’s wrath will intensify against the people of the earth and established the Hour.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8407 - Suspended"
"8408","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Hasan told us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Bayhaqi told me, Nu’aym ibn Hammad told us, Abdullah ibn Wahb informed us, Muawiyah bin Salih told me, on the authority of Issa bin Asim, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: While the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying One night during prayer, he extended his hand, then closed it, and we said: O Messenger of God, we saw that you did something in this prayer that you had not done before. Before him, he said: “Yes, Paradise was presented to me, and I saw therein a dahlia with its harvest close by, and I wanted to eat some of it, so it was revealed to me. To delay, so I delayed, and the Fire appeared to me between me and you until I saw my shadow and your shadow in it, so I motioned to you to delay. So I was inspired to accept them, for you converted to Islam and they embraced Islam, and you emigrated and they emigrated, and you struggled and they struggled, and I did not see any superiority in you over them except By prophecy, so I interpreted that as the tribulations that my nation will encounter after me.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8408 - True"
"8409","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, That Yazid bin Abi Habib told him that Abd al-Rahman bin Shamasa told him that he was with Maslama bin Mukhlid, and he had a servant Allah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, and Abdullah said: “The Hour will not come except upon the worst of creation. They are worse than the people of pre-Islamic times. They do not call on God.” “With nothing but returning it to them.” While they were doing that, Uqba bin Amir came and Maslamah said: O Uqba, listen to what Abdul is saying. God, and Uqba said: He knows best.
As for me, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A group from my nation continues to fight according to the command of God, subjugating the enemy without Those who disagree with them will harm them until the Hour comes to them while they are in that state.” Abdullah said: Yes, “Then God will send forth a scent whose scent is the scent of musk.” And he touched it like the touch of silk, and not a soul would be left with a grain’s weight of faith in his heart except that it took hold of him. Then the worst of people would remain, upon whom the Hour would come.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8409 - True"
"8410","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: “Indeed, from the end of the matter of the Kaaba The Ethiopians are invading the House, and the Muslims are heading towards them, so God will send upon them an easterly wind, so God will not leave a servant in His heart is an atom's weight of piety except his fist, so much so that when they have made their choice, there will remain a group of people who are weak, neither enjoining what is right nor forbidding it. On the authority of evil, and every living person turned to the idols that their fathers had worshiped and worshiped them, until they wandered along the roads as animals wander, and they The Hour is upon them, and whoever tells you about anything after this has no knowledge.” The chain of transmission is authentic according to their condition.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8410 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, it is suspended"
"8411","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Bashir bin Al-Muhajir told us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God has a wind that He sends out upon the head of a hundred “A Sunnah that seizes the soul of every believer.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8411 - True"
"8412","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Darraj, On the authority of Ibn Hujayrah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “A time will come upon my nation when there will be many Readers, jurists will be few, knowledge will be diminished, and hoopla will increase. They said: What is the hoopla, O Messenger of God? He said: “Murder is among you, and after that will come a time when men will recite the Qur’an, but it will not exceed their throats. Then after that will come a time.” The hypocrite, the unbeliever, the polytheist in God, argues with the believer by something like saying, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8412 - True"
"8413","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: “A time will come upon the people in which no believer will remain unless he joins the Levant.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two sheikhs, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8413 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8414","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sirafi told us, Abdullah bin Raja’ Al-Iraqi told us, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Muhallab bin Abi Safra, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, said: “A fire will be sent that will drive people from the east of the earth to Its setting is like a broken camel being led to it, whatever of them is left behind, when they say, it says, and when they arrive, it remains.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two sheikhs, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8414 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8415","Ghailan bin Yazid Al-Daqqaq told us, in Hamadan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Qaridh bin Shaybah, on the authority of Abu Ghatafan, said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, saying: “Different minerals come out, some minerals... Among them is a person close to the Hijaz, and one of the worst people comes to him. He is called Pharaoh. While they were working there, he lost sight of the gold, and they were astonished. “His companion when it was swallowed up by him and them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8415 - True"
"8416","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi told me, Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Ibrahim Al-Shadhuri told us, Saeed bin Hubayra told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, Abu Al-Tayyah reported, saying: We prayed Friday, and the people gathered together until they were like moths around Abu Raja Al-Atardi. So they asked him about the sedition, and he said: Two men came to the meeting of Ubadah Ibn al-Samit and said: O Ibn al-Samit, repeat the hadith that you told us, so he said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “It is about time that the best wealth will be the two sheep of Mecca and Medina, grazing on the heads of the land, eating Of the leaves of astragalus and basam, and its people eat of its flesh and drink of its milk, and the germs of the Arabs tremble in temptations - he says Three times, then he said - By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if one of you has three hundred sheep, to eat from their flesh and drink from their milk, I would love to “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8416 - True"
"8417","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jablah bin Suhaim, On the authority of Aamir bin Matar, he said: I heard Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, saying: “How will you be if you renounce your religion like a woman renounces her religion? ""kiss her""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8417 - True"
"8418","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Salt bin Bahram, on the authority of Mundhir Ibn Hudha, on the authority of Kharshah Ibn Al-Hurr, who said: Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, said: “How will you be if you separate from your religion like a woman does? Does it not prevent anyone from coming to it? He said: Then a man said: May God be ugly to the incapable person. He said: “Rather, you are ugly.” These two hadiths have authentic chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8418 - True"
"8419","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Aqbi informed us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Uthman bin Amr told us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, he said: I went to see Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, one day, and he said: “I did not sleep last night until I woke up in the morning.” I said: Why? He said: “They said: The tailed star has risen, so I feared that the Antichrist had come. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. However, it is contrary to Abdullah bin Masoud, and that the verse of the Antichrist has passed.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8419 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8420","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Abdullah bin Salih told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Abi A while ago, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them, he said: “The Antichrist will have known signs: when the eyes become watered and they bleed. The rivers turned yellow, and Madhhij and Hamadan moved from Iraq, and Qinnasrin descended. So wait for the Antichrist, whether he is coming or smelling. “This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8420 - True"
"8421","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzar told us, Abu Al-Jamahir told us, Sa’id bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Uqba, on the authority of Amr bin Aws Al-Sadusi, said: “We brought Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them both, and he was wearing two Qatari garments. He was wearing a turban, but he was not wearing a shirt - meaning a shirt - so we said to him: You have narrated on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and you have narrated the books, so he said: “Who are you from?” He said: So we said: “From the people of Iraq.” He said: “Indeed, O people of Iraq, you lie and lie and mock.” He said: So I said: No, by God. We will not lie to you, nor will we mock you. He said: “For the children of Qantura and Korki will not leave until they tie their horses to palm trees.” Deer, how long is it between them and Basra? He said: So we said: Four farsakhs. He said: Then they will be sent if they leave between us and it. He said: A third will join them, a third will go to Kufa, and a third With the Bedouins, then they are sent to the people of Kufa if they leave us alone, and a third will join them, a third with the Bedouins, and a third with the Levant.” He said: So we said: What is the sign of that? He said: “When the earth settles, the leadership of the two boys” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8421 - True"
"8422","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid al-San’ani informed me of Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abbad informed us. Abd al-Razzaq, Muammar reported, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris al-Khawlani, who said: I met Abu al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, and I became aware of him. I met Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, and learned about him, and I missed Muadh ibn Jabal, may God be pleased with him, and Yazid ibn Umayrah informed me. He used to say in every session he sat in: “God is a just judge, blessed be His name. The doubters will perish. Indeed, behind you are temptations in which many will be Money, and the Qur’an is opened in it until the man and the woman, the free and the slave, the young and the old, take it. Then the man is about to recite the Qur’an. He says: I have read the Qur’an, so what do the people have if they do not follow me when I have read the Qur’an? Then he says: They are not my followers until I invent something else for them, so beware of you, and whatever he innovates, for what he innovates is misguidance. Beware of the slip of the wise man, for Satan instills error in the wise man, and instills in the hypocrite the word of truth. The truth, and that Satan casts a word of error into the wise man? He said: “Avoid from the words of the wise man anything that is similar, which when you hear it you say: What is this? And that does not tell you about him, for perhaps he will revise and tell the truth, so listen to it, for there is light upon the truth. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8422 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8423","Abu Mansour Muhammad bin Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Ataki told us, Abu Sahl Busr bin Sahl Al-Labbad told us, Abdullah bin Salih, Al-Layth bin Saad narrated to me, Abu Qabil narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them both, “that a man from The enemies of the Muslims in Andalusia are called: The one with the custom brings together a great multitude of polytheist tribes. Those in Andalusia know that they have no strength. For them, the strong Muslims flee in ships, so they cross to Tangier, and the weak people and their group remain, as they do not have ships. They pass over it, so God Almighty sends a deer and it crosses the sea for them, and the deer passes while the water does not cover its hooves, so the people see it. So they say: The Ibex, the Ibex, follow him, and all the people will pass by in his wake, then the sea will become as it was and the enemy will pass by in boats. If the people of Africa felt them, they would all flee from Africa, and with them were the Muslims in Andalusia, until they entered. Al-Fustat, and that enemy will advance until they descend between Mariut to the pyramids, a journey of five sacks, and they will fill what is there with evil. Then the banner of the Muslims will come out to them on the bridge, and God will grant them victory over them, and they will defeat them and kill them to the point of marching. Ten nights, and the people of Fustat will kindle their calf and their tools for seven years, and Dhul-Urf will escape from killing, carrying with him a book that does not He looks at it only when he is defeated, and finds in it mention of Islam, and that he is commanded in it to enter into peace, so he asks for safety for himself. And whoever of his companions who came with him converts to Islam, and he converts to Islam and becomes one of the Muslims, then a man from among the Muslims will come the second year. The Abyssinian is called Asis, and he has gathered a large crowd, and the Muslims flee from Aswan, so that nothing remains there or in it other than it. Not one of the Muslims entered Al-Fustat, and Asis descended with his army in Memphis, and he was at the head of a post from Al-Fustat, and a banner would go out to them. Muslims on the bridge, and God gives them victory over them, and they kill them and capture them, until the lions are sold for a cloak. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of narration is based on the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it is the basis for the knowledge that strife occurred in Egypt and they did not bring it out.” And Manf: This is what Mansour says. The jurist, may God have mercy on him:
[the uprooted sea]

Yesterday I asked about palaces... in Ain Shams and Manf.
About its people, where they lived... but he did not answer me a word.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8423 - Not according to their condition"
"8424","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Bashir al-Ansari, he said: A man came and called Ibn Masoud, and he fell upon him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, when Did he go astray, and I know? He said: “If there are rulers over you, if you obey them they will make you enter the Fire, and if you disobey them they will kill you.” This is a hadith with a valid chain of narration and it is not “He brings him out.” Al-Hakim, may God have mercy on him, said: “These are hadiths that Abdullah bin Wahb mentioned about epics, and I excelled in them and narrated them, even if they were not Supports
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8424 - True"
"8425","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told me, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Jubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah Al-Khushani, said: “If you see the Levant at the table of one man, and his family, then That was the conquest of Constantinople.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8425 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8426","Muhammad told us, Bahr told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Muawiyah told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Jabir, and Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Ka’b, he said: “ There are three strongholds: The people’s stronghold on the Day of the Epics is in Damascus, and the people’s stronghold on the Day of the Antichrist is the Abu Albatross River, through which some of the people will pass who say: “House.” The Holy Place, and their stronghold on the Day of Gog and Magog at Mount Sinai.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8426 - Interrupted"
"8427","Muhammad told us, Bahr told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of my father Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, said: “If you are given a choice between two lands, do not choose Armenia, for therein is a portion of the punishment of God Almighty.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8427 - True"
"8428","Muhammad told us, Bahr told us, Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Muawiyah told me, on the authority of Safwan bin Amr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr. Ibn Nufir, on the authority of Ka’b, said: “The island is safe from destruction until Armenia is destroyed, and Egypt is safe from destruction until the island is destroyed. Kufa will be safe from destruction until Egypt is destroyed, and the epic will not be completed until Kufa is destroyed, and the city of disbelief will not be conquered until the epic is accomplished. The Antichrist will not leave until the city of disbelief is conquered.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8428 - Interrupted and weak"
"8429","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Bahr told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Saleh told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, He used to say: “Noah, peace and blessings be upon him, begot three sons: Shem, Ham, and Japheth. Shem begot the Arabs, the Persians, and the Romans, and there was goodness in all of them. Ham begat the Sudan, the Berbers, and the Copts, and Japheth begat the Turks, and the Saqlabis, and Gog and Magog.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8429 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8430","Muhammad told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Ka’b, he said: “Do not be Epics, except at the hands of a man from the fourth - or fifth - family of Heraclius, called Tayyara.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8430 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8431","Muhammad told us, Bahr told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told me, on the authority of Safwan bin Amr, that he heard Abu Maryam, Abu Hurairah’s servant said: Abu Hurairah passed by Marwan while he was building his house in the middle of the city. He said: So I sat with him and the workers. They work. He said: Build hard, hope far away, and die soon. Then Marwan said: Abu Hurairah is speaking to the workers, so what do you say to them, O Abu? Kitten? He said: I said: “Build hard, hope far away, and die soon, O people of Quraysh - three times - remember how you were yesterday and how you are today.” You shall serve your slaves, Persia and the Romans. Eat wholemeal bread and fatty meat. Do not eat one another, and do not eat like ravenous sheep. And be “You are small today and you will be great tomorrow, and by God, no man among you will rise in rank except that God will place him on the Day of Resurrection.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8431 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8432","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha, On the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Asma, on the authority of Thawban, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He fights when Your treasure will be three, all of them Ibn Khalifa, and then it will not come to any of them. Then the black banners will rise from the east, and they will fight you in combat. No people fought him - then he mentioned something and said - If you see him, pledge allegiance to him, even if you crawl on the snow, for he is the Caliph of God, the Mahdi. This is a hadith. “Sahih according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8432 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8433","Abu Hafs Ahmad ibn Hanbal, the jurist in Bukhara, informed us. Abu Harun Sahl ibn Shadhawayh informed us, Yahya ibn Ja`far told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The best of people in times of turmoil is a man who takes the reins of his horse - or he said: by the reins of his horse - behind the enemies of God, frightening them.” And they fear him, or a man secluded in his desert, fulfilling the rights of God that he owes. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8433 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8434","Abu Bakr bin Darim Al-Hafiz told me, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Uthman bin Saeed Al-Qurashi told us, Yazid bin Muhammad Al-Thaqafi told us, Hanan told us Bin Sudair, on the authority of Amr bin Qais Al-Malali, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah bin Qais, and Ubaida Al-Salmani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: We came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he came out to us rejoicing and showing happiness on his face, so what we asked him about? Nothing except that he told us about it, and we did not remain silent except that we began, until young men from Banu Hashim passed by, including Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn. When he saw them He turned to them and his eyes fell down, so we said: O Messenger of God, we still see something in your face that we hate. He said: “We are the people of a household that God has chosen for us.” After me, my family will face expulsion and displacement in the land, until black flags rise from the east. So they ask for the truth and are not given it, then they ask for it and are not given it, then they ask for it and are not given it, then they fight and are victorious, so who will realize it? From among you or from your descendants, let the imam of my family come, even if they are crawling on the snow, for they are signs of guidance. They are to be given to a man from my family. His name will be the same as my name, and his father’s name will be my father’s name. So he will possess the earth and fill it with equity and justice, as it had been filled with oppression and injustice.”
[Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8434 - This is a topic"
"8435","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, said: “Sedition has come upon you, accusing us of contempt. Black and dark sedition has come upon you. There are pauses and pauses for temptation, so whoever of you is able to die during its pauses, let him do so.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8435 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8436","Ahmed bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Hilal bin Al-Alaa Al-Ruqi told us, Amr bin Uthman Al-Kalabi told us, Abdullah bin Amr told us, Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “There will be a trial by which people will fight “And they killed her in Hell.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8436 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8437","Muhammad ibn Ali al-San’ani informed me, in Mecca, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told me, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Muammar informed me, on the authority of Abu Khuthaym, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Sargis, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: “O people, a trial has overtaken you like parts of a dark night, but the best of people is In it - or he said: in it - the owner of a sheep eats from the messengers of his sheep, or a man behind the path, taking the reins of his horse, eats from his sword. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"8438","Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Tamimi informed me, Abu Muhammad Al-Hasan bin Ibrahim bin Haider Al-Himyari informed me, in Kufa, Al-Qasim bin Khalifa told us, Abu Yahya Abdul Hamid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Hamani told us, Omar bin Ubaid Allah Al-Adawi told us, on the authority of Muawiyah Ibn Qurrah, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He will descend upon my nation.” At the end of time, there will be a severe affliction from their rule. A more severe affliction has never been heard of, until the spacious land becomes narrow for them, and until the land is filled with oppression. Unjustly, the believer does not find a refuge to which he can turn from injustice, so God Almighty sends a man from my family, and he fills the earth with justice. And justice, just as it was filled with injustice and injustice, is satisfied with the inhabitant of heaven and the inhabitant of the earth. The earth does not store anything of its seed unless it brings it up. The sky does not have any diameter except that God pours it on them in abundance. They live in it for seven, eight, or nine years. The living wish for the dead. “Of what God Almighty and Majestic has done for the people of the earth of His goodness.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8438 - Its chain of transmission is dark"
"8439","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Abd told us Al-Malik bin Qudamah Al-Jumahi, on the authority of Ishaq bin Bakr bin Al-Furat, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah May God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Years will come upon the people in which the liar will be believed and the truthful will be lied to. The traitorous person will be trusted therein, and the trustworthy person will be betrayed therein, and the Ruwaybidah will speak among them. It was said: O Messenger of God, and what is the Ruwaybidah? He said: “The frivolous man speaks about public affairs.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8439 - True"
"8440","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi told us, Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Ibrahim Al-Shadhuri told us, Saeed bin Hubayra told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Ayoub reported, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Yazid ibn Umayrah, on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal, may God be pleased with him, who said: “There will be a trial in which there will be many money, and the Qur’an is opened in it so that the believer and the hypocrite, the young and the old, the men and the women, read it. The man recites it secretly, and it is not followed. On it, so he says: By God, he will recite it publicly. Then he recites it publicly and it will not be followed on it. So he takes a place of prostration and invents speech that is not in the Book. By God, nor from the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so beware of you and him, for everything that is invented is misguidance.”
He said: When Muadh bin Jabal fell ill during which he was arrested, he would sometimes faint, and sometimes wake up, until he fainted, we thought. He was arrested, then he woke up and I was facing him crying, so he said: “What makes you cry?” I said: By God, I do not cry over the world that I gained from you, nor over the lineage between you and me, but I cry over the knowledge and wisdom that I hear. He goes from you. He said: “Do not weep, for knowledge and faith are their place. Whoever seeks them will find them, seek them where Abraham sought them.” Prayers and peace, for he asked God Almighty while he did not know, and recited: {Indeed, I am going to my Lord. He will guide me} [Al-Saffat: 99] And seek Him after me when Four people, and if you do not find him with one of them, then ask the most prominent people: Abdullah bin Masoud and Abdullah bin Salam. And Salman, and Awimir Abu Darda, and beware of the deviation of the wise man and the judgment of the hypocrite. He said: I said: How can I know the deviation of the wise man? He said: “A misleading word that Satan places on the tongue of a man, but he does not bear it or take heed of it. The hypocrite may speak the truth, so take knowledge.” “However did he come to you? Indeed, upon the truth is light, and beware of difficult matters.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8440 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8441","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Aoun bin Sufyan Al-Tai told us in Homs, Abu Al-Mughirah Abd told us. Al-Quddus bin Al-Hajjaj, Abdullah bin Salem Al-Homsi told us, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Utba Al-Yahsbi, on the authority of Umair bin Hani Al-Absi, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, saying: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he mentioned temptations and mentioned them repeatedly until He mentioned the temptation of Ahlas, and someone said: What is the temptation of Ahlas? He said: “It is the trial of flight and war, then the trial of secret times - or ease - then the people reconcile against a man like a corner on a side, then the trial of mobs.” Do not leave any of this nation except that you strike it with one blow. And when it is said, ‘It will end,’ it will continue. A man will become a believer in it and one evening will become an unbeliever, until he becomes The people will be taken to two camps: a camp of faith in which there is no hypocrisy, and a camp of hypocrisy in which there is no faith. If that is the case, then wait for the Antichrist from today. Or tomorrow: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8441 - True"
"8442","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Waki’ told us, al-Qasim bin al-Fadl told us. Al-Harrani, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah Al-Abdi, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “And who My soul is in His hand. The Hour will not come until wild lions speak to man, and until the stick of his whip and the strap of his sandal speak to a man, and tell him what He told his people after him, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8442 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8443","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “If one of you wants to know whether temptation has afflicted him or not, So let him consider it. If he sees what is lawful, he sees it as forbidden, then temptation has befallen him, and if he sees what is forbidden, he sees it as lawful, then it has befallen him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8443 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8444","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Waki` told us, Al-Qasim bin Al-Fadl, Abu Nadrah told us, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: We saw a shepherd grazing with a free animal, except for the wolf on One of the sheep, then the shepherd came between the wolf and the sheep, so the wolf fell on its tail, and said: O Abdullah, come between me and the sustenance of its leg. God to me? The man said: What a strange wolf that speaks to me in human words. The wolf said: Shall I not tell you something that is more amazing than me? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, explained Al-Haratayn informs the people of the news of what had happened before, so the shepherd moved his sheep to a corner of the city, then he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he informed him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to the people, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He has spoken the truth, and by the One in whose hand is my soul.” An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8444 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8445","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul Hamid Al-San’ani told me about Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded. Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad, Abd al-Razzaq informed, Muammar informed, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Uqba ibn Aws, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them, said: “Two factions fight over a pre-Islamic claim when a prince or tribe emerges, and the faction that emerges emerges. She will be humiliated, and her enemy will fall in love with her, and will be thrown into the Fire.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8445 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8446","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Nasr al-Muddhikir told us about Marw, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Issa al-Qadi told us, Abu Nu`aym and Abu Hudhayfah told us, They said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Nubait bin Shurayt, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “It is presented It is a temptation on the hearts, so any heart that denies it will have a white mark on his heart, and any heart that does not deny it will have a white mark on his heart. black, then another temptation is presented to the hearts, and if the heart that denied it the first time denies it, a joke will be marked in his heart. White, and if he does not deny it, a black joke will be made, then another temptation will be presented to the hearts, and if the one who denied it both times will deny it. The first two times he became strong, white, and kind, and no temptation ever harmed him, and if he did not deny it in the first two times, he became black and apostatized and relapsed, then he will not know. Truly, and let no one deny it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8446 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8447","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn al-Musayyab told us, Nu’aym ibn Hammad told us, Yahya ibn Sa’id told us, Al-Walid bin Ayyash, brother of Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, said: Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: He told us The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I warn you of seven trials that will occur after me: a trial that will come from Medina, a trial that will come from Mecca, and a trial that will come from Yemen, and a trial is coming from the Levant, and a trial is coming from the East, and a trial is coming from the West, and a trial is coming from the heart of the Levant, and that is the Sufyani.” He said: Ibn Masoud said: “Among you is the one who realizes the beginning of it, and among this nation is the one who realizes the end of it.” Al-Walid ibn Ayyash said: “So it was.” The strife of Medina by Talha and Al-Zubayr, the strife of Mecca by the strife of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, and the strife of the Levant by the Banu Umayyad. “And the temptation of the East by these people.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8447 - This is from the chapters of Nu’aym ibn Mahdi"
"8448","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told me, my father told me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, Ikrimah bin Ammar narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdullah Al-Filastini, Abdul Aziz, my nephew Hudhayfah, narrated to me, on the authority of Hudhayfah May God be pleased with him, he said: “The first thing you will lose from your religion is humility, and the last thing you will lose from your religion is prayer, and the bonds of Islam will be torn down once and for all.” loop, and let the women pray while they are menstruating, and let you follow the path of those before you, like moth with moth, and sandal with sandal. You will make their path wrong, and they will not make you wrong until two groups remain out of many, and one of them says: What is the matter with the five daily prayers? He has gone astray. It was before us. God, Blessed and Most High, only said: “Establish prayer at both ends of the day and during the night.” [Hud: 114] Do not pray except three times, and it says The other: The faith of the believers in God is like the faith of the angels. There is neither an infidel nor a hypocrite among us. It is God’s right to gather them together with the Antichrist. “This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8448 - True"
"8449","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hisham bin Abi Abdullah told us, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Abu al-Tufayl, he said: Omar, Ibn Dhali’, and I went to Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, who had two sittings among the people, so we said: O Hudhayfah, You realized what we did not realize, and you knew what we did not know, and you heard what we did not hear, so tell us something that perhaps God will benefit us with it, so he said: If only I told you everything I heard while you waited for me the recent night. He said: We said, “We are not asking you about this, but tell us about a matter that perhaps God will It will benefit us. He said: If I had told you that the mother of one of you was fighting in a group until she struck with a sword, you would not have believed me. We said: Not about this. We ask you, but tell us something that perhaps God will benefit us with. Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “This neighborhood of Mudar will continue to kill, destroy and annihilate every righteous servant until God overtakes them with armies of Then you kill them until the sin of Tal’ah is not prevented.” Amr ibn Dhali’ said: And his mother was burdened with the divinity of people unless it was harmful. He said: “Aren’t you one of the A foolish warrior? He said: Yes, he said: “If you see Qays approaching the Levant, be careful.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8449 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8450","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, On the authority of Malik bin Zalim, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying to Marwan bin Al-Hakam: My beloved Abu Al-Qasim Al-Sadiq told me Al-Masduq, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The corruption of my nation is at the hands of foolish people from Quraysh.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman testified to the authenticity of this hadith.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8450 - True"
"8451","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqqashi told us, Yahya bin Hammad told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Tharwan, on the authority of Amr bin Hanzalah, said: When Othman, may God be pleased with him, was killed, we entered Hudhayfah and found the people with him. He said: “By God, an oppressor will not let a believing servant of God be harmed unless they kill him or tempt him so that God will harm them, and the believers so that they will not prevent The tail of a sting.” A man said: Are you saying this when you are a man from Mudar? He said: I do not say anything except what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8451 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8452","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan informed me, Abdullah informed me, Awf informed me, on the authority of my father Al-Minhal, on the authority of Abu Barza Al-Aslami, may God be pleased with him, said: “Indeed, he who is in the Levant - meaning Marwan - by God, he will not fight except on the authority of world, and that he who is in Mecca - meaning Ibn al-Zubayr - does not fight except for the sake of this world, and that those whom you call are your readers, and by God they fight Except for this world.” Then my father said to him: What do you command us then? He said: “I do not see the best of people except a cluttered band of people - and he said with his hand - those who wash their bellies with people’s money, and their backs with their blood.”
Abdullah said: Malik bin Mughal told me, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, that he said to a man asking him about Fighting with Al-Hajjaj, or with Ibn Al-Zubayr. Ibn Umar said: “Which of the two groups did you fight with? You were killed in the clashes.” This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8452 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8453","Abdul Rahman bin Hamdan Al-Jallab told me about Hamdan, Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Ruqi told us, Abdullah bin Ja’far told us, Ubaid Allah bin Amr, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Anisa, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Khaythamah bin Abdul Rahman, he said: We were with Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, So some of us said: Tell us, O Abu Abdullah, what you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: If I had done so, you would have stoned me. He said: We said: Glory be to God, do we do that? He said: “What if I told you that one of your mothers was coming to you in a large group, so powerful that you would believe it?” They said: Glory be to God, and who believes in this? Then Hudhayfah said: “Al-Humayra came to you in a group led by her healers wherever your faces look bad.” Then he got up and entered a room. “This is a hadith.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8453 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8454","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab said: Abu Idris, may God forbid, Al-Khawlani said: I heard Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, saying: “By God, I am the most knowledgeable of people.” With every temptation that is present between me and the Hour, and that is not because the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to me something about it that he did not narrate. Other than me, but the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He was speaking to a gathering I was in about temptations, and he “counted temptations among them as three that you will not abandon.” “Some of them are like the summer winds, some of them are small and some of them are large.” Then all of them went away except me. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8454 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8455","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul Hamid Al-San’ani informed us of Mecca, which God Almighty protected. Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar reported, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “Indeed, I know of a trial about which what was before it will soon become like the breath of a rabbit, and I know the way out of it.” We said: And what is the way out? From her? He said: “Hold my hand until someone comes to kill me.”
Muammar said: A sheikh of ours told me that a woman came to one of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said to her: “Pray to God to divorce me.” My hand,” she said: “And what about your hand?” She said: “I had two fathers. My father had a lot of money, a lot of favor, a lot of virtue, and a lot of charity, and my mother had nothing of that. I think she never gave anything in charity except that we slaughtered a cow and she gave a poor person a lobe on his hand and dressed him in a rag, so my mother died and my father died, so I saw My father is at a river giving people water, so I said: Father, have you seen my mother? He said: No, did she die? I said: Yes, he said: So I went to look for her and found her standing naked, with nothing on her except that rag and that robe in her hand, and she She strokes it with her other hand, then bites its mark, and says: And he made him thirsty. So I said: O mother, shall I not give you something to drink? She said: Yes, so I went to my father and mentioned that to him, and I took a vessel from him and watered it, and someone who was standing with her alerted me about me. He said: Whoever gives it to drink, God will paralyze his hand. I woke up and my hand was paralyzed. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8455 - Abu Hurairah’s report according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim. As for the dream, its chain of transmission is weak."
"8456","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, saying: Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr reported. Al-Azdi, my grandfather Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaida told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God rose among us May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He told us what would happen therein until the Hour comes. His mind is among us from his mind, and he who forgets it has forgotten it. This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Abu Awanah and Aban bin Yazid Al-Attar, on the authority of Asim, and Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud is an imam whose imamate is agreed upon in the Qur’an. As for all other sciences, if it is unique to the hadith, we are obligated to accept it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8456 - True"
"8457","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub and Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, they said: Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the Martyr told us, they told us: Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose He remained in a position, and did not leave anything without mentioning it until the Hour comes.” His mind is from his mind, and he who forgets it forgets it."
"8458","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, Ibn Al-Harith told us Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, said: When it was the day of the dose, Jundub said: “By God, blood will be shed,” and a man said: No, by God. He said: I said: I see you sitting in a bad mood today. “You hear me talking, and I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so do not forbid me.” So he said: What is the matter with you? What about anger? He said: So I started to ask him, and it was Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, may God be pleased with him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8458 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8459","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi told me, Ahmad bin Ibrahim Al-Shadhuri told me, Saeed bin Hubayra told us, Ismail bin Ayyash told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Hamza bin Suhaib, who said: I heard Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar narrating, on the authority of his father, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, used to say: “God began this matter when He began with prophecy and mercy, then He returned to a caliphate, then He returned to Sultan and mercy, then he returns as king and mercy, then he returns as a coercive force, toiling like donkeys. O people, you must wage conquest and jihad. It was not sweet and green before it was bitter and hard, and it was perfect before it was rubble - or it was rubble -, so when the battles get wild And the spoils have been devoured and the forbidden has been made lawful, so you must adhere to the bond, for it is the best of your jihad.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8459 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8460","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ahmed Al-Hafid told me, my grandfather told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Abu Muawiyah told me, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He studies Islam as he studies something.” The garment, so that the meaning of fasting, charity, or ritual rituals will not be known, and the Book of God will be spread over one night, so that not a single sign of it will remain on earth, and groups of people will remain. People, the old man and the old woman, say: We taught our fathers this word: There is no god but God, so we say it.’” Silah said. Ibn Zufar told Hudhayfah: What is of no use to them? There is no god but Allah, when they do not know what fasting, charity, or rituals are? So Hudhayfah turned away from him, so he repeated it to him three times, each of which Hudhayfah turned away from him, then he turned to him for the third time, and said: “O connection that will save them.” “From the Fire.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8460 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8461","Abu Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahboubi informed us, Sa`id ibn Masoud informed us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Ibn Aoun informed us, about Khaled bin Al-Huwaith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The verses are arranged beads. In a wire, the wires are cut and one of them follows the other.” Khalid bin Al-Huwaith said: We were calling for the morning, and there was Abdullah bin Amr, and he was There is a woman from Banu al-Mughirah called: Fatima. I heard Abdullah bin Amr say: “That is Yazid bin Muawiyah,” so she said: Is that the case, O Abdullah bin Amr, that you find written in the book? He said: “I do not find him by his name, but I find a man from the tree of Muawiyah who sheds blood, takes money for granted, and tears down a stone from this house.” A stone. If that happens while I am alive, otherwise remember me.” He said: “Its residence was on Abu Qubays. When the time of al-Hajjaj and Ibn Al-Zubair saw the house being demolished and said: May God have mercy on Abdullah bin Amr, he told us about this.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8461 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8462","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Isfahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Zayd ibn Yatha’, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, he said: “How about you, when you ask for the right and you are given it, and when you ask for your right? So you prevented him.” They said: “We will be patient.” He said: “You have entered it by the Lord of the Kaaba.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8462 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8463","Abu Al-Nadr Muhammad bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told us, and Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Anazi told us, saying: Muadh bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Bashir bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “A people will come With small eyes and broad faces, as if their faces were hollow, they accompany the people of Islam with wormwood plants, as if I were looking at them tied up. Their horses were mounted on the pillars of the mosque. Then it was said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: O Messenger of God, who are they? He said: “The abandonment.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, agreed on the hadith of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The Hour will not come until you fight the Turks with broad faces and small eyes. Their noses were turned, as if their faces were hammered.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8463 - True"
"8464","I heard the only jurist and writer, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ali Al-Qaffaffal, more than once, saying: I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Sawli The grammarian says: “The first of the Arab poets to praise the Turks was Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Rumi, when he said:
[abundant sea]
If they establish corruption of iron...our eyes will be confused about it.
And if they emerge, fires will blaze... against the enemies, and they will be deflected by a metaphor.
“The kings of the earth have small eyes... when they emerge, but their souls are great.”"
"8465","Muhammad ibn Ali al-San’ani informed me of Mecca, which God Almighty protected. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us. Abd al-Razzaq informed us. Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: “It is as if by abandoning it I had come to you upon two leper The call to prayer until you connect it to the shore of the Euphrates.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8465 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim
 Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Du’ali. I heard Abdullah bin Amr saying: “It is likely that he will not remain in the land of the Persians.” Of the Arabs, except one who is killed or a prisoner, his blood will be judged.” Zur’ah bin Damra said: Do the polytheists support Islam? He said: Who are you from? He said: From Banu Amir bin Sa’sa’ah. He said: “The Hour will not come until the marches of the women of Banu Amir attack Dhul-Khalasa.” He said: So he mentioned His statement to Omar bin Al-Khattab, and he said: Abdullah knows best what he is saying three times, according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim."
"8466","Abu Amr Othman bin Abdullah bin Al-Sammak Al-Zahid told us in Baghdad, Abu Muhammad Abdul-Rahman bin Mansour Al-Harithi told us, Muadh bin Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakra, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr May God be pleased with them. He said: “The Banu Qantura bin Karkar are about to expel the people of Iraq from their land.” I said: Then will they return? He said: “Do you desire that?” He said: “And it will be a source of comfort for them.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8466 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8467","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-San’ani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra, who said: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-Aas said: “The Banu Qantura are about to expel you from... The land of Iraq.” He said: I said: Then they will return? He said: “And that is more beloved to you. Then they will return and have a place of livelihood therein.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “And the children of Qantura are the Turks.”"
"8468","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ghayath Al-Abdi told us in Baghdad, Ibrahim bin Al-Haytham Al-Bakri told us, Ali bin Ayyash told us, Abdul Rahman bin Thabit bin Thaban told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Al-Araj, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the Hour will not come until you fight the Turks with small eyes and red faces. “The noses are turned, as if their faces were hammered.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not include in it: “red faces.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8468 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8469","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Al-Ghaith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Have you heard of the city of Janab? Some of it is on land and part of it is at sea? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “The Hour will not come until seventy thousand of the Banu Ishaq will invade it. When they reach it, they encamp. They fight with weapons but do not shoot an arrow.” He said: “Then they say: There is no god but God, and God is the Greatest,” and one of its sides falls. “Thor said: No.” I only know that he said: “The side of it that follows righteousness. Then they say the second: There is no god but God and God is great,” and the other side of it falls. Then they say the third time: There is no god but God, and God is the greatest, and relief is given to them and they enter it and take spoils, while they divide the spoils. When the one shouting that the Antichrist has come to them comes to them, they will leave everything and return. “It is said that this city is Constantinople, and it has been restored.” The narration is that he opened it at the beginning of the Hour.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8469 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8470","Muhammad Ibn Ali Ibn Abd al-Hamid al-San’ani informed me about Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded. Ishaq Ibn Ibrahim informed me. Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i informed me, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed me, my father informed me, Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Muammar informed me, On the authority of Hammam bin Munabbih, that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Hour will not come until You are fighting Khuz and Karaman, a people of foreigners, red-faced, snub-nosed, small-eyed, as if their faces were hammered shields. “Their shoes are hair.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8470 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8471","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, the Imam of the Muslims Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah told us, Ya’qub told us Ibn Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, Ibn Ulayya told us, Ayoub told us, on the authority of Humayd ibn Hilal, on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of Asir ibn Jabir, he said: She attacked A red wind in Kufa, and a man came to Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, and he had no response: Except, O Abdullah bin Masoud. The Hour has come, he said: Abdullah was reclining, then he sat down and said: “The Hour will not come until an inheritance is not divided and an enemy does not rejoice in the spoils. They gather for the people of Islam, and the people of Islam gather for them.” - And he moved with his hand towards the Levant - I said: What do you mean by the Romans? He said: “Yes, and in that case there will be severe apostasy in the fighting, so the Muslims will set a death penalty that will not return except a victorious one, so they will fight until The night separates them between them, and these fight and those fight, each one is not victorious, and the stage disappears. Then the Muslims stipulate a stage for death. It does not return unless it is victorious, so they will fight until the night closes between them, and some of them will flee, each of them will not be victorious, and the force will disappear, and then The Muslims stipulate a death penalty that will not return except a victorious one, so they fight until they are touched, then some of them will fulfill, and all of them will not be victorious, and they will perish. The police, and if it is the fourth, then the rest of the people of Islam will attack them, and God will set a course upon them, and they will be killed with great slaughter - or he said: The like of it has not been seen, or he said: We will never see the like of it - so much so that the bird would pass by them and not leave them until it fell dead, and the children of Banu would become hostile to each other. The father, and there were a hundred of them, and they did not find any of them remaining except one man. So, with what spoils should he rejoice or what inheritance should be divided? He said: While they were like that When they heard of a people who were larger than that, the one crying out came to them that the Antichrist had left among their offspring, so they rejected what was in their hands and accepted it. Then they will send ten knights as a vanguard.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, I know their names and the names of their fathers, and the colors Their horses, they will be the best horsemen on the face of the earth that day.” And he said: “They will be the best on the face of the earth.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. The two sheikhs, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8471 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8472","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, Sufyan said: I do not know unless he raised it. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said And he said: “The Hour will not come until the land of the Arabs returns to pastures and rivers.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8472 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8473","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi told me, Ahmad bin Ibrahim Al-Shadhuri told me, Saeed bin Hubayra told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Al-Sakhtiyani, and Ali bin Zayd bin Jad’an, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, who said: We came to Othman bin Abi Al-Aas on Friday to review our Qur’an. With his Qur’an, when Friday came, he ordered us to wash and perfume ourselves, and we went to the mosque, and we sat with a man who was speaking, then Othman bin Abi Al-Aas, so we turned to him, and Othman, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The Muslims shall have three Egypt: Egypt at the junction of the two Bahrain, Egypt on the Peninsula, and Egypt in the Levant. The people will be terrified in three terrors, and the Antichrist will emerge in the presence of an army. He will be defeated by the East, and the first to be defeated by Egypt is the one at the junction of the two Bahrains, and its people will become three groups: one group that establishes and says We will look at it and see what it is, and a group will join the Bedouins, and a group will join the Egyptian next to them, then the Egyptian next to them will come and become Its people are three groups: a group that says “Nashama” and “we will see what it is,” a group that joins the Bedouins, and a group that joins the Egyptians who are next to them, then The Levant will come, and the Muslims will be drawn to the Aqabat of Afiq, and they will be sent with a troop for them, but their troop will be affected, and this will become difficult for them. Severe famine and hardship, to the point that one of them burned his bowstring and ate it. While they were like that, a herald called out to them from magic: O people, relief has come to you, and they say to one another: This is the voice of a full man. Then Jesus, son of Mary, descends to pray upon him. And greetings at the dawn prayer, and the imam of the people says to him: Come forward, O Spirit of God, and lead us. Then he says: You, this nation, are princes. One of you over others. You go forward and lead us. He will go forward and lead them in prayer. When he departs, Jesus, may God’s prayers be upon him, takes his spear towards the Antichrist. If he sees him, he melts like bullets melt, and his spear falls between his wings and kills him, then his companions are defeated, and there will be nothing on that day. One of them will be imprisoned, to the point that the stone says: O believer, this is an infidel, so kill him. This hadith has an authentic chain of transmission, on the condition that a Muslim mentions Ayoub al-Sakhtiyani, and they did not expel him.”
[p. 525]
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8473 - Abu Hubayra is weak"
"8474","Makram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi narrated to us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker narrated to us, and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq and Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi said: Affan ibn Muslim informed us, Hammad ibn Zayd told us, on the authority of Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jad’an, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, he said: Othman bin Abi Al-Aas believed us. Then he mentioned a hadith similar to it, but he did not mention Ayyub, and God knows best.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8474 - This has been preserved"
"8475","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Utbah Ahmad bin Al-Faraj Al-Hijazi told us in Homs, Baqiyya bin Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “When the Umayyads reached the age of forty, they took the servants of God as horses, and God made them as bees, and God’s book as bush.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8475 - Interrupted"
"8476","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan ibn Issa told us, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told us, Nu’aym ibn Hammad told us, Baqiyya ibn Al-Walid and Abdul-Quddus bin Al-Hajjaj said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Maryam told us, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “When the Umayyads reach forty, they will take the servants of God as horses, and God will provide them with horses. And the Book of God is a jungle.”
Abu Bakr bin Abi Maryam said: Ammar bin Abi Ammar told me that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “The destruction of this nation is at the hands of the oppressors of Quraysh.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “This hadith has consequences and evidence from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, his pure companions, and the imams from among the followers. I could not help but He mentioned it, and I mentioned some of what I had come across from it.”"
"8477","Among them is what Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul Hamid Al-San’ani told us in Mecca, protected by God Almighty, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, and Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, we told him Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hanthali, Muhammad bin Rafi’ Al-Qushayri, and Salama bin Shabib Al-Mustamli said: Abdul Razzaq bin Hammam told us. The Imam said: My father told me, on the authority of Mina, the servant of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, may God be pleased with him, he said: It was No child is born to anyone unless it is brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He prayed for him and Marwan ibn al-Hakam came to him and said: “It is the lizard.” “Ibn al-Wazagh, the cursed son of the cursed.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"8478","Among them is what Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani narrated to us in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri Al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us. Ibn Ja`far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ishaq Ibn Yusuf al-Azraq, Ishaq Ibn Yusuf narrated to me, Sharik Ibn Abdullah narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of my brother Ibn Salamah, on the authority of Hallam ibn Jadhal al-Ghifari, who said: I heard Abu Dharr Jundub ibn Junada al-Ghifari, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, he says: “When the Banu Abi Al-Aas reach thirty men, they will take God’s money as horses, God’s servants as horses, and God’s religion as a jungle.” Hallam said: This was denied to Abu Dharr, and Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, testified that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “What “The green shade has increased, and the dust has not diminished over someone with a more truthful dialect than Abu Dharr.” And I bear witness that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him, “This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.” This was witnessed by the hadith of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8478 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8479","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Musa bin Harun bin Abdullah Al-Imam told us, Zakaria bin Yahya told us Hamawiyah, Salih bin Omar told us, Mutarrif bin Tarif told us, on the authority of Atiya, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “When the Banu Abi Al-Aas reached thirty men, they would take the religion of God as a bush, the servants of God as camels, and God’s wealth as countries.” This is how he narrated it. Al-Amash, on the authority of Atiya"
"8480","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Humayd told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Saeed, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When the sons of Abu Al-Aas reach thirty men, they will take God’s money as a state, and a debt God is a jungle, and the servants of God are insolent.”"
"8481","Among them is what Abu Ahmad Ali bin Muhammad Al-Azraqi narrated to us in Marw, Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ismail bin Salim Al-Sayegh narrated to us in Mecca, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Al-Walid Al-Azraqi, the muezzin of the Grand Mosque, told us, Muslim bin Khaled Al-Zanji told us, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abdul Rahman, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, I saw in my dream that Bani Al-Hakam bin Abi The disobedient ones descend upon my pulpit as monkeys descend.” He said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was never seen gathered together and laughing until he died.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8481 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8482","Among them is what Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hajjaj narrated to us. Ibn Muhammad, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, he said: I heard Humayd ibn Hilal, narrating, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Barza Al-Islami said: “The most hated of the living to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were Banu Umayyah, Banu Hanifa, and Thaqif.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8482 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8483","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Marwazi Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Durhami told us, Umayyah bin Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, who said: When Muawiyah pledged allegiance to his son Yazid, Marwan said: The Sunnah of Abu Bakr, And Omar, and Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr said: The Sunnah of Heraclius and Caesar, and he said: God revealed about you: {And he who said to his parents, “Fine to you.” [Al-Ahqaf: 17] The verse, he said: Then the news reached Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and she said: He lied, and God is not in it, but “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed Marwan’s father, and Marwan is in his loins.” Marwan is a story from the curse of God Almighty. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8483 - There is a break"
"8484","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Ja’far bin Sulayman Al-Dabai told us, Ali told us Ibn Al-Hakam Al-Bunani, on the authority of Abi Al-Hasan Al-Jazari, on the authority of Amr Ibn Murrah Al-Juhani, and he was a companion of his, that Al-Hakam Ibn Abi Al-Aas He asked permission to call upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recognized his voice and his words, so he said: “Admit permission for him. May the curse of God be upon him, and upon whomever.” He will emerge from his loins, except the believers among them, and they are few. They are honored in this world and degraded in the Hereafter. They are deceitful and deceitful. They are given in this world, and they have no share in the Hereafter.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “And it is witnessed by the hadith of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, who"
"8485","Ibn Nusayr Al-Khalidi told us, may God have mercy on him, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Al-Hajjaj bin Rashidun Al-Masry told us in Egypt, Ibrahim bin Mansour Al-Khorasani, Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqa, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr Radi God said on their authority: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed Al-Hakim and his son.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “Al-Hakim said May God Almighty have mercy on him: “Let the seeker of knowledge know that this is a chapter in which I have not mentioned a third of what was narrated, and that the first temptations in this nation I tempted them, and I could not, between me and God, remove the book from mentioning them.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8485 - Al-Rushdini was deemed weak by Ibn Adi"
"8486","Sheikh Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq Al-Faqih, may God be pleased with him, told us. Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ismail bin Abi told us. Uwais, my brother told me, on the authority of Sulayman bin Bilal, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The Hour will not come until the Romans descend into the depths and bring to them from Medina some of the best of the people of the land.” On that day, when they line up, the Romans will say: Leave us alone with those who were taken captive from us, and we will fight them. The Muslims will say: No, by God, we will not leave you alone. And among our brothers, they fight them and a third are defeated and God will never forgive them, and a third are killed. They are the best martyrs in the eyes of God Almighty. Glory be to Him, and in the morning a third will never be tempted, so they will reach Constantinople and conquer, while they are dividing their spoils, and they have been suspended. Their weapons were with olives, when Satan shouted: Indeed, Christ has succeeded you in charge of your families, and that is false. When they come to the Levant, he will leave, while they are They prepare for battle and straighten the ranks when the morning prayer has been established, and Jesus, son of Mary, may God’s prayers be upon him, descends and leads them. If an enemy sees him God melted as salt dissolves, and if he had left it, it would have melted until it was destroyed, but God will kill him with his own hand and show them his blood on his spear. “This is a hadith It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8486 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8487","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us Al-Asbahani, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Abu Qais Al-Awdi, on the authority of Huzail bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: “You are in a time when scholars are many, preachers are few, givers are many, and prayers are short. The sermon therein is long, so shorten the sermon and lengthen the prayer, and indeed part of the statement is magic, and whoever desires the Hereafter will be harmed. This world, and whoever desires this world harms the hereafter. O my people, harm what will perish for the rest.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8487 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8488","Abu Bakr bin Abi Nasr al-Muzaki told me about Marw, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, we told him Kathir bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Awf Al-Muzani, and Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq narrated to us, and he has the wording. Al-Hussein bin Ali bin Ziyad, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Kathir bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not pass away from this world, O Ali bin Abi Talib.” Ali said: At your service, O Messenger of God. He said: “Know That you will fight the Banu Asfar, or those after you among the believers will fight them, and the pride of the believers will go out to them, the people of Hijaz who They strive in the cause of God. Do not let the blame of a critic seize them in the name of God, until God Almighty conquers Constantinople and Rome over them with praise. And the takbeer, and its fortress collapses, and they strike a great arrow, the like of which they have never struck, to the point that they are divided by the shield, then he shouts Screaming: O people of Islam, the Antichrist has come out in your countries and your offspring, and people are turning away from money. Some of them are taking, and some of them are giving up money. The one who leaves, the taker is regretful, and the one who leaves is regretful. They say: Who is this shouter? They do not know who he is, so they say: Send a group to Lydda, and if the Messiah has come out, they will bring you his knowledge. So they will come. So they look and do not see anything, and they see the people doubting, and they say: The one who shouted only shouted for news. So they resolve, then they seek guidance and resolve to We will go out all of us to Lydda, and if the Antichrist is there, we will fight him until God judges between us and him, and He is the best of judges. “The other is your country, your clans, and your armies, to which you have returned.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8488 - It is very weak"
"8489","Muhammad Ibn Ali Ibn Abd al-Hamid al-San’ani informed me about Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded. Ishaq Ibn Ibrahim informed me. Abd al-Razzaq informed me, Muammar reported, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who narrated it. He said: “Woe to the Arabs from the evil that has Approaching the age of sixty, trustworthiness will become a spoils, charity a fine, testimony based on knowledge, and judgment based on inclination. This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, they did not impose these additions.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8489 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8490","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Amr bin Muhammad Al-Anqazi told us, Talha bin Amr Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair Al-Laithi, on the authority of Abu Al-Tufayl, on the authority of Abu Sariha Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “An animal will have three appearances over a period of time. It will make its first appearance in the farthest part of Yemen, and its memory will be public.” In the desert, and her male does not enter the town - meaning Mecca - and then stays for a long time after that, then comes out again near Mecca, and its mention is spread among the people of the desert, and its mention is spread in Mecca, then it lies for a long time, then while the people are in the greatest mosques. It is sacred and the most beloved to God and the most honorable to God Almighty. The Sacred Mosque did not look after them except when it was in the direction of the Mosque, approaching and approaching between The Black Corner, and between the Banu Makhzum Gate on the right of the outside, in the middle of that, so people will reject it from all sides, and it will be established A group of Muslims knew that they would not defeat God, so she went out to them, shaking the dirt off her head, and appeared before them. Their faces until they left them as if they were the shining stars, then they passed away in the earth, no seeker overtaking them, no fugitive unable to defeat them, even a man So he would seek refuge from her with prayer, and she would come to him from behind him and say: Which so-and-so are you praying now? So he turns to her and she slaps him in the face, then she goes away, and the people live next door to them in their homes, accompany them on their travels, and participate in Money, a believer knows an infidel to the point that the infidel says: O believer, fulfill my due, and the believer says: O infidel, fulfill my due. This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, and it is the clearest hadith in mentioning an animal of the earth, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8490 - Talha bin Amr Al-Hadrami considered it weak and Ahmad abandoned it."
"8491","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abd al-Ala told us, On the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, he said: We were sitting at Hudhayfah, and the animal was mentioned, and Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, said: On his authority: “It will emerge in three outings in some desert areas, then it will lie in wait, then it will emerge in some villages until they become terrified and until the princes flee therein.” The bloodshed, then the bloodshed. He said: While the people were at the greatest, best, and most honorable mosque - we even said, the Sacred Mosque and what he called it - when The earth rose and the people fled, and a group of Muslims remained, saying: Nothing will save us from the command of God, so you go out and flee. Their faces until you make them like the shining stars, and they follow the people, neighbors on the quarter, partners in wealth and companions in Islam. “This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8491 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8492","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, Al-Walid bin told us All, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Bilamani, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “People spend the night They are going to gather, and the animal of the earth stops at night and runs towards them, and in the morning it has placed them between its head and its tail, so there is no believer but it wipes it. There is no hypocrite or infidel but you will strike him, and indeed repentance is open until the Antichrist comes out, and the believer is seized by him like the body of a cold. And it enters the ears of the disbeliever and the hypocrite until it becomes like a pure thing, and indeed repentance is open, then the sun rises from the west.” This An authentic hadith according to the two sheikhs’ conditions: “And they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8492 - Ibn Al-Bilmani is weak, and so is Al-Walid"
"8493","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Hatim told us, Abu Sa`id al-Ashjaj told us, Abu Usama told us, On the authority of Idris bin Yazid Al-Awdi, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Amr, may God be pleased with them both, in His Almighty saying: {And when the saying occurs against them We brought forth for them an animal from the earth} [An-Naml: 82] He said: “If they do not enjoin what is right and do not forbid what is wrong.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8493 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8494","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Wasiti told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Aws bin Khaled, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The animal will come out, carrying the staff of Moses. And the Seal of Solomon, so you mark the face of the believer with a stick, and you poke the nose of the disbeliever with the ring, to the point that the people of the traitors gather together and say: For this reason: O believer, and they say to this person: O disbeliever.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8494 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8495","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Walid told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Za’ra’, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: “A time will come upon people in which a man will be envied by his lightness, just as a man today is envied by his money.” And the child.” He said: Then a man said to him: Which money will be better on that day? He said: “A good weapon, and a good horse that goes with it wherever it goes.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8495 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8496","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Muhammad bin Wahb Al-Dimashqi told us, Sadaqa bin Abd told us. By God, Khalid bin Dahqan told me, he said: I heard Zaid bin Artaat Al-Fazari, saying: He heard Jubayr bin Nufayr Al-Hadrami, saying: I heard Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, says: He heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “The day of the great battle against the Muslims. In a land called Al-Ghouta, in which there is a city called Damascus, the best of Muslims’ homes on that day.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8496 - True"
"8497","Abu Abdullah Al-San’ani told me, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq told me, Muammar told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab said: When the pledge of allegiance to Yazid bin Muawiya came, I said: If I went to the Levant and avoided the evil of this pledge, I would go out. Until I came to the Levant, I was informed of a place where Nawf was standing, so I came to him, and behold, there was a man with damaged eyes, wearing a quilt, and behold, it was Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them both. When Nouf saw him, he stopped talking, and Abdullah said to him: Tell us what you were talking about. He said: You have more right to hadith than me. You are the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: These people have prevented us from having hadith - meaning the princes - he said: I insist on you, except for what you told us of a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard him say: “It will be a migration after A migration. People will cross to the migration of Abraham. Nothing will remain in the land except the worst of its people. Their land will consume them and make them filthy. themselves, and God will gather them to the Fire with the apes and the pigs. You will spend the night with them when they spend the night, and you will dine with them when they wake up, and you will eat “Who fell behind”
He said: And I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “People from my nation will emerge from the East, reciting the Qur’an without going beyond “Their collars, whenever a century emerges from them, it will be cut off until the Antichrist emerges among the rest of them.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8497 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8498","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Khuzaymah al-Kashshi told us in Nishapur from his book, Abd ibn Humayd al-Kashshi told us, Abu Asim al-Nabil told us, Ezra bin Thabit told us, Alaba bin Ahmar told us, Abu Zaid Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, told us: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led us in prayer.” He said the dawn prayer, and he addressed us until noon, then he went down and prayed the noon prayer, then he addressed us until the afternoon prayer, so he came down and prayed the afternoon prayer, then he went up and addressed us to the afternoon prayer. Morocco, and he told us about what is going to happen.” So we learned and we memorized “this hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8498 - True"
"8499","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Shaiban told us, about Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose among us, and he did not leave anything to take his place.” That is until the coming of the Hour. Unless we tell it to us. Whoever memorizes it will remember it and whoever forgets it will forget it. These companions of mine have taught it, for it will be Some of it I forgot, so I see it and remember it just as a man recognizes the face of a man whom he has missed. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He takes him out in this context.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8499 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8500","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad told us, Nu’aym ibn Hammad told us, al-Walid ibn Muslim told us, on the authority of Abu Rafi’ Ismail bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, who said: Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The My family will be killed and displaced from my nation after me, and indeed our people who hate us the most are the Banu Umayyah, the Banu al-Mughirah, and the Banu Makhzum: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"8501","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Dhuhli told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in the dam, he said: “They dig it every day until They almost broke it, and those who were in charge of them said: “Go back and you will break it tomorrow.” He said: “Then God Almighty will restore it as it was as strong as it was, until when they reach It extended them, and God Almighty wanted to say to those who were against them: “Go back, and you will destroy it tomorrow, God Almighty willing.” He made an exception. He said: “And they will return while it is It was like it was when they left it, and they would pierce it and attack the people, and they would draw water, and the people would flee from them, and they would shoot their arrows into the sky. Then it will return covered in blood, and they will say: We have vanquished the people of the earth, and we have vanquished whoever is in the heaven in power and majesty.” He said: “Then God Almighty will send On them is a nap on their backs.” He said: “Then He will destroy them.” He said: “By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the animals of the earth will grow fat and grow tall, and will be grateful.” “Thank you, and you will be intoxicated with intoxication from their meat.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8501 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8502","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Awwam bin Hawshab informed us, Jablah bin Suhaim narrated to me, on the authority of Muathir bin Afaza, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: “When it was the night of his captivity With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he met Abraham, Moses, and Jesus, peace be upon them, and they remembered when the hour was, so they started with Abraham and asked him About it, but he had no knowledge of it, so they asked Moses, but he had no knowledge of it, so they referred the hadith to Jesus, and he said: God’s covenant with me. And no one knows it except God Almighty, so he mentioned the appearance of the Antichrist and said: Then I will go down and kill him, then the people will return to Their country, and Gog and Magog will meet them, and they will descend from every direction. They will not pass by any water without drinking it, nor by anything without spoiling it. Then they would come to me, so I would call upon God, and He would kill them, and the earth would be empty of their scent. Then they would come to me, so I would call on God, and He would send water from the sky. Then he would carry them and throw their bodies into the sea, then the mountains would be blown away and the earth would expand to the depths of the earth, so God covenanted with me that if This is because the hour of the people is like a pregnant woman who has died, her family does not know when she will surprise them with her birth, day or night.” Al-Awwam said: I found confirmation of that in the Book of God Almighty, then he read: {Until when Gog and Magog are opened, and they are slipping away from every side. And the true promise has drawn near.} [Al-Anbiya’: 97] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8502 - True"
"8503","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sana’ani informed me of Mecca, which God Almighty protected. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari informed me. Abd al-Razzaq informed me. Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, the client of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them, on the authority of Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi’ah, may God be pleased with him, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The wind will come before the Hour, and it will seize the soul of every believer.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not take him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8503 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8504","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, Asim told me Ibn Omar Ibn Qatada Al-Ansari, then Al-Dhafri, on the authority of Mahmoud Ibn Labid, brother of Bani Abd Al-Ashhal, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Gog and Magog will be conquered, they will attack the people as God Almighty said: {From They will spread out, [Al-Anbiya’: 96], and they will spread throughout the land, and the Muslims will withdraw to their cities and fortresses, and will join them. their livestock, and they drink the water of the land, to the point that some of them pass by a river and drink what is in it until they leave it dry, so that some After them, he passed by that river and said: There was once water here, until, when not one of the people remained, he took to a fortress or a city. Their speaker said: These are the inhabitants of the earth. We have finished with them. The rest are the inhabitants of heaven. He said: Then one of them shakes his spear, then throws it. To the sky, and it returns drenched in blood due to affliction and temptation. While they were in that, God sent worms on their necks like the moth, and it came out in Their necks and they become dead, and no sense can hear them. Then the Muslims say: Is there a man who would sell himself to us and see what this man has done? The enemy, he said: Then a man from among them strips himself, claiming that he has declared himself to have been killed, and goes down and finds them. The dead of one another, then he would call: O community of Muslims, rejoice, for God has sufficed you with your enemy. So they would emerge from their cities. And their fortresses, and they let go of their livestock, so they have no pasture except for their meat, and they are grateful for it just as they are grateful for any plant. It never happened to him: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8504 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8505","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Musayyab bin Zuhair told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Wahb bin Jabir narrated, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, who said: “Gog and Magog, the first of them passes by a river like The Tigris, and the last of them would pass by and say: There was once water in this river, and no man dies but leaves behind a thousand of his descendants and upwards, and whoever After them were three nations: Tawis, Taweel, Nasik, and Mansik. “Shak Shu’bah” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8505 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8506","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muadh bin Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Amr bin Marzuq told us, Imran Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Maadan bin Talha, on the authority of Amr Al-Bikali, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, said: “Indeed, God God Almighty divided creation into ten parts, and made nine parts the angels, and part the rest of creation, and divided the angels ten parts. parts, so He made nine parts to glorify Him day and night without faltering, and as a part of His message, and He divided creation into ten parts, so He made Nine parts of the jinn, and a part of the children of Adam, and he divided the children of Adam into ten parts, so he made nine parts Gog and Magog, and a part “All of mankind and the same heaven.” He said: “The seventh heaven and the Sacred Place and the Throne around it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8506 - True"
"8507","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Muhammad ibn Shadhan al-Jawhari told me, Sa`id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti told us, Khalaf ibn Caliph Al-Ashja’i, Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Rab’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman Radi On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I know what the Antichrist has with him. Two rivers: one of them is a fire that rages in the eyes of the one who saw it, and the other is white water, so if any of you sees it, let him close his eyes, and drink from what he sees as fire, for it is cold water, and beware of you. And the other is temptation, and know that written between his eyes is an unbeliever, whoever writes it and whoever does not write it, and that one of his eyes reads it. anointed with victory over it; for he shall rise at the end of his decree into the belly of the Jordan; to his house I will wake up, and every one who believes in God And the last day in the depths of Jordan, and he kills a third of the Muslims, defeats a third, leaves a third alive, and the night descends upon them. Then some believers will say to others: Do not wait to join your brothers in pleasing your Lord. Whoever has food left over, let him eat in the morning. with it upon his brother, and pray when the dawn breaks, and hasten the prayer, then attack your enemy.When they stood up to pray, Jesus, son of Mary, may God’s prayers be upon him, descended in front of them and led them in prayer. When he left, he said: Thus, separate between me and the enemy. “God.” Abu Hazim said: Abu Hurairah said: “It will melt as crescent moons melt in the sun.” Abdullah bin Amr said: “Just as salt dissolves in water, and God has given the Muslims authority over them, so they kill them to the point that trees and stones To call: O Abdullah, O Abdul Rahman, O Muslim, this is a Jew, so kill him. Then God will banish them and the Muslims will appear and be defeated. cross, and they killed the pig, and imposed the tax. While they were doing that, God brought out the people of Gog and Magog, and the first of them drank The lake, and the last of them will come having drawn water, and they will not leave a drop in it, and they will say: We appeared against our enemies. There was a trace of water here. Then the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions follow him, until they enter one of the cities of Palestine, which is called Lydd. They say: We have given victory over those on earth, so come, let us fight those in heaven. Then God will call upon His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at that time, and God will send against them An ulcer in their throats, and not a human being would remain of them, and their smell would harm the Muslims, so Jesus would pray, may God’s prayers be upon them,Then God will send a wind upon them and it will throw them all into the sea. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not bring it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8507 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8508","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us - he gave dictation in the mosque before the building of the house for the Sheikh Imam in Sha’ban in the year three hundred and thirty - twice. Abu Muhammad al-Rabi` bin Sulayman bin Kamil al-Ramadi - in the year sixty-six - Bishr bin Bakr al-Tanisi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, Yahya bin Jabir al-Homsi told me, Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr al-Hadrami told us, my father told me that he heard al-Nawwas bin Simeon Al-Kalabi said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned the Antichrist one morning, and he lowered it and raised it, until they thought he was in a group of palm trees. When We went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He recognized this about us, and he said: “What is the matter with you?” So we said: O Messenger of God, you mentioned the Antichrist in the morning, so you lowered and raised your voice until we thought he was in a group of palm trees. He said: “If he emerges, I will be among you.” So I am his guarantor rather than you, and if he comes out and I am not among you, then every man is his own guarantor, and God is my successor over every Muslim. He is a young man. His beard is straight, as if he resembles Al-Uzza ibn Qatan, so whoever of you sees him should recite the openings of Surah Al-Kahf.” Then he said: “I see him coming out.” Between the Levant and Iraq, it spread to the right and to the left.O servants of God, stand firm. We said: O Messenger of God, how long did he stay on earth? He said: “Forty days are like a year, and one day is like a month, and one day is like a Friday, and the rest of its days are like your days.” He said: We said: O Messenger of God. So that is like a year, for which one day’s prayer is sufficient for us? He said: “No, estimate for him his destiny.” We said: O Messenger of God, what is his speed on earth? He said: “Like a rain driven by the wind.” He said: “Then it comes upon the people, and they call upon them, and they believe in Him and respond to Him, and He commands the heavens.” Then it rains, and He commands the earth to bring forth, and He spreads upon them the length of their wings, the longest of their udders, and the longest of their loins, then The people come and invite them, and they respond to what he said, and he departs from them, and their money follows him, and in the morning they carry nothing in their hands. Then he passes by the desolation and says to it: Bring out your treasures. So he sets off, and her treasures follow him like bee flies. Then he calls a young Muslim man. So he strikes him with the sword and cuts him in two parts, like the cutting of a target. Then they invite him and he kisses, his face shining and laughing. He said: While... This is also the case when God Almighty sent Jesus, son of Mary, to disembark at the white minaret east of Damascus in Mahroditin, placing his palms on the The wings of two angels, when he lowers his head, he drops.And when he raises it, a mountain like pearls flows from it, and it is not permissible for an infidel to smell his own breath unless he dies, and it ends where his limb ends. So he pursues him until he overtakes him at the gate of Lod, and God kills him. Then comes Jesus, the son of Mary, peace be upon him, a prophet of God to a people whom he has protected. God is from him, so he wipes his face and tells them about their ranks in Paradise. While they were like that, God revealed to him: O Jesus, I have I have brought forth My servants whom no one will be blamed for fighting. Bring My servants to Mount, and God will raise Gog and Magog, and they will slip away from every direction. The first of them will pass by Lake Tiberias and drink what is in it, then the last of them will pass by and say: There was once water in this, and a Prophet will be trapped. God bless Jesus and his companions, so that the head of a bull for one of them that day will be better than a hundred dinars for one of you today, so the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, desires May peace and blessings of God be upon him and his companions to God Almighty, and God will send upon them sickness on their necks, and they will become as miserable as the death of a single soul. Then the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, descended while his companions could not find a place even an inch of space except that God had filled it with their scum, their stench, and their blood. The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions turn to God,Then He sends birds like the necks of a camel, and they pick them up and cast them wherever He wishes. Then God sends rain from which there will be neither mud nor dander. Then he will wash the earth until he leaves it like a slippery tree, then he will say to the earth: Grow your fruit and restore your blessing. On that day the group will eat of The pomegranate tree, and they take shade from its top, and the messengers are blessed, to the point that a morsel from camels is sufficient for a group of people, and a morsel from cows is sufficient. The tribe, and a piece of sheep from the sheep is enough for the thigh. While they were like that, God sent a pleasant wind that would reach under their armpits and capture the soul. Every Muslim, and the rest of the people will continue to jest like the reds jest, and upon them the Hour will come. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8508 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8509","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn al-Musayyab told me, Nu’aym ibn Hammad told us, al-Walid ibn Muslim told us, about Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: A boy was born to my brother Umm Salamah, so they named him Al-Walid. This was mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “You have named him after the names of your pharaohs, so that there will be in this nation a man called Al-Walid is more evil to this nation than Pharaoh was to his people.” Al-Zuhri said: “If Al-Walid ibn Yazid is appointed as successor, then it is he. Otherwise “Al-Walid bin Abdul-Malik” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Al-Hakim said: “He is Al-Walid bin Yazid, without a doubt or without any doubt.” ""mirror""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8509 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8510","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Asam told us, Yahya bin Nasr told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Al-Awza’i told us, Ismail bin Ubayd Allah, he said: Anas bin Malik came to Al-Walid bin Yazid, and Al-Walid said to him: What did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mention? The hour? He said: I heard him say: “You and the Hour are like these.” The two sheikhs agreed to quote it from the hadith of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada and Abu al-Tayyah. On the authority of Anas"
"8511","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Sarram told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, Muhammad bin Abi Safwan Al-Thaqafi told us, Bahz told us Ibn Asad, from Shu’bah, told us about Ali Ibn Al-Aqmar, who said: I heard Abu Al-Ahwas, speaking on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The Hour will not come until it is not said on earth, ‘God, God’.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. They did not narrate it, but Muslim, may God have mercy on him, was the only one to narrate the hadith of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The Hour will not come except upon the worst of people.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8511 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8512","Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muzaki informed us, Ahmad ibn Salamah informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Fayyad informed us, Abd al-A`la told us Ibn Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The Hour will not come until it is not said “On earth there is no god but Allah.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"8513","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein bin Dizel told us, Ali bin Uthman Al-Lahiqi told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Hour will not come until it is not said on earth, ‘God is God,’ and until A woman passes by a piece of sandal and says: This man once had a husband, and until the man is the guardian of fifty women, and until the sky rains and there is no fruit. “This is a hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8513 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8514","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told me, Muhammad ibn Ismail and Muhammad ibn Raja told us, they said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb, my uncle told me, Amr bin Al-Harith and Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Sinan bin Saad, on the authority of Anas bin Malik May God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the Hour will not come upon a man who says: There is no god but God. And he enjoins what is right and forbids what is wrong. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"8515","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani narrated to us in Bukhara, Abdullah bin Najiya narrated to us, Abd Al-Warith bin Abd narrated to us Al-Samad bin Abdul-Warith, my father told me, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The Hour will not come until it is not said on earth, ‘Allah, Allah,’” and until a woman passes by wearing sandals and takes them off and says: “It was.” This is for a man, and until there are fifty women the one is the guardian, and until the sky rains and the earth does not grow. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim. And they did not take it out.”"
"8516","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah Al-Hamdani told us, Al-Qasim bin Al-Hakam Al-Arni told us, Sulayman bin Abi Sulayman told us, Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “Do not The Hour when there will not remain on the face of the earth anyone for whom God has a need, and until a woman will be found openly having sex in the middle of the road during the day. This will not be denied. No one will change it, and he will be like them on that day who says: If we move it out of the way for a little while, then that will be like Abu Bakr and Omar among you. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8516 - The news is almost a myth"
"8517","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told me, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, my father told me, Ali bin Thabit told me, Abd told me Al-Hamid bin Hafs, my father told me, on the authority of Alaba Al-Sulami, may God be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “The Hour will not come.” Except for the scum of people.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8517 - True"
"8518","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abu Shurayh Abd al-Rahman bin Shurayh told me, On the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abu Farwa, Abu Jahl’s client, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited: {When God’s victory and conquest come and you see the people entering into God’s religion in crowds} [Al-Nasr: 2] Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Let them expel them.” “From it in droves just as they entered it in droves” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8518 - True"
"8519","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, On the authority of Abu al-Za’ra’, he said: We were with Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, and the Antichrist was mentioned to him, so Abdullah bin Masoud said: """" O people, you will be divided into three groups after his departure: a group that will follow him, a group that will join the land of its fathers in the wormwood beds, and a group that will take the The Euphrates fights them and they fight it until the believers gather in the villages of the Levant, and they send to them a vanguard among them is a knight riding a blond and white-haired horse. He said: “Then they will be killed, and not a single one of them will return.” - Salamah said: Abu Sadiq told me, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Najid, that Abdullah bin Masoud - He said: “A blond horse.” Abdullah said: “And the People of the Book claim that the Messiah will descend to them.” He said: I heard him mentioning about the People of the Book. A hadith other than this - “Then Gog and Magog will come out and rejoice in the land and spread corruption therein.” Then Abdullah read: {And they will come from every direction. They will descend} [Al-Anbiya’: 96] He said: “Then God will send against them an animal like this nag, and it will enter their ears and nostrils and they will die from it.” Then the land will stink of them, so he will turn to God, and He will send water to purify the land of them.”He said: “Then God will send a wind containing a cold, whistling wind. No believer has been left on the face of the earth but that wind has restrained him.” He said: “Then you will rise.” The Hour is upon the wickedest of people. Then the Angel will establish the bridge between the heavens and the earth and blow into it - and the pictures are a horn - so no creation will remain in the heavens and the earth. Unless he dies, except whom your Lord wills, then between the two blowings there will be as long as God wills, for there is no creation from the children of Adam except something from him.” He said: “Then God will send water from under the throne like the cum of men, and their flesh and their bodies will sprout from that water, just as He causes the earth to sprout from the dirt.” Then Abdullah recited: {And it is Allah who sends the winds and they stir up the clouds, so We drive them to a dead land and thereby revive the earth after its death. Thus An-Nushur} [Fatir: 9] He said: “Then an angel will stand between the heavens and the earth, and blow into it, and every soul will go into its body until it enters into it. Then they will rise and live the life of one man, standing up for the Lord of the worlds.” He said: “Then God Almighty will go to the creation, and will meet them, but there is not a single one.” He worships anything besides God unless it is raised up for him. He follows it.” He said: “Then he meets the Jews and says: Who do you worship? “He said: “Then they say: We worship Uzair.He said: Does water please you? And they say: Yes, when He showed them Hell in the appearance of a mirage. 100] He said: “Then he will meet the Christians and say: Who do you worship? They say: The Messiah. He said: Then he says: Does water please you? He said: And they say: Yes. He said: Then He will show them Hell as it looks like a mirage, and then likewise for whoever worships anything besides Allah.’ He said: Then Abd recited God: {Stop them, for they will be questioned} [Al-Saffat: 24] He said: “Then God Almighty will appear to the creation until He passes over the Muslims.” He said: “And whoever Do you worship? They say: We worship God and do not associate anything with Him. Then he rebukes them two or three times, and says: Who do you worship? They say: “We worship God and do not associate anything with Him.” He said: “And He says: Do you know your Lord?” He said: “And they say: Glory be to Him when He confesses to us, we recognize Him.” He said: “Then a leg will be uncovered, and no believer will remain except that he bows down in prostration to God. And the hypocrites will remain with their backs in one row, as if there were foot-biters in it.” He said: “And they will say: Our Lord.” He will say: You were being called to “Prostrate while you are safe.” He said: “Then he will be commanded to take the path and it will be set upon Hell, and people will pass by according to the extent of their deeds, in groups like the flash of lightning.Then like the wind, then like the bird, then like the fastest of animals, then like that until a man passes by running, then walking, then the last of them is a man shuffling. On his stomach,” he said: “And he says: “O Lord, why have you been so slow with me? He says: “I did not slow you down, but rather slowed down your work.” He said: “Then God Almighty will permit intercession, so the first intercessor will be the Holy Spirit Gabriel, peace and blessings be upon him, then Abraham, the friend of God, then Moses, then Jesus, may the blessings and peace of God be upon them.” He said: “Then your Prophet will rise as a fourth, and no one after him will intercede for what he intercedes for, and he is the place of residence.” The Praiseworthy, which God, Blessed and Most High, mentioned: {Perhaps your Lord will raise you to a place of praise} [Al-Isra: 79] “He said: “There is not a soul but it is “You are looking at a house in Paradise or a house in Hell.” He said: “And it is the Day of Heartbreak.” He said: “Then the people of Hell will see the house that is in Paradise, then it will be said: If only you had done so.” He said: “Then grief will overtake them.” He said: “And the people of Paradise will see The house will be in Hell, and it will be said: “Had it not been that God has bestowed upon you.” He said: “Then the angels and the prophets and the martyrs and the righteous and the believers will intercede.” Then God will intercede for them. He said, “Then God will say: ‘I am the Most Merciful of the merciful,’ and He will bring out more from the Fire than He brought out of all creation by His mercy.”He said: “Then He says: I am the Most Merciful of those who are merciful.” He said: Then Abdullah recited: {What led you in Saqr} [Al-Muddaththir: 43] They said, “We were not of those who prayed, nor were we provided with food.” The poor. And we were quarreling with the adversaries, and we were denying the Day of Judgment. He said: Then Abdullah held four with his hand, then said: “Do you see among these people? “There is good in it. There is nothing good in it that anyone descends upon. So if God Almighty wanted no one to leave it, He would change their faces and colours.” He said: “Then a man comes and looks and does not know anyone, and the man calls him and says: O so-and-so, I am so-and-so, and he says: I do not know you. Then he says: {Our Lord, remove us from it. But if we return, then indeed we are wrongdoers} [Al-Mu’minun: 107] Then He will say: “Be humiliated therein and do not speak to Him.” So when He said that. It was closed upon them, and not a single person would emerge from them. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8519 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8520","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, and Abu Muslim Al-Musayyab bin Zuhair al-Dhabi, they said: Abu Ja`far Abdullah bin Muhammad al-Nufaili told us, Zuhair bin Muawiya told us, Mutarrif bin Tarif told us, on the authority of al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Nu’aym ibn Dajaja, said: I was sitting with Ali, may God be pleased with him, when Uqba Abu Masoud came to him, and Ali said to him: Oh Farrukh, you are the one who says, or you are the mufti who issues fatwas to the people. He said: As for me, I will tell them the other and the other is evil. He said: Tell us what you heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say about the hundred. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “There will not be a hundred years on the earth while a single eye blinks.” He said: “You have sinned and you have sinned.” At the beginning of your fatwa, “That is only for whoever is alive on that day, and is there prosperity and relief except after the hundredth?”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8520 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8521","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abu Shurayh Abd al-Rahman bin Shurayh told me, He said: I heard Saeed bin Abi Shimr Al-Shaybani, saying: I heard Sufyan bin Wahb Al-Khawlani, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “The hundred will not come while there is no one remaining on the face of the earth.” He said: So I narrated it to Ibn Hujairah. He said: Then Abd al-Rahman bin Hujairah entered Abdul Aziz bin Marwan brought Sufyan, who was an old man, to him, so Abdul Aziz asked him about this hadith, so he told him, and Abdul Aziz said: Perhaps he means that none of those who were with him will remain until the end of the hundred. Sufyan said: This is how I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it” and the clear evidence of the validity of the statement of the Commander of the Faithful, Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. By Abu Masoud Uqba bin Amr Al-Ansari, and the words of Abdul Aziz bin Marwan to Sufyan bin Wahb Al-Khawlani “
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8521 - True"
"8522","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz did not tell us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Ali bin Issa bin Ibrahim, Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Jurashi told us, Abdullah ibn Maslamah ibn Qa’nab told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said a month before his death, or something like that: “What Of a soul that has been destroyed today, one hundred years will come of age, and it will be alive that day.” Muslim narrated this hadith with this chain of narration in The correct one
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8522 - Narrated by Muslim"
"8523","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, my father told me, Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, Ismail bin Abdul Karim Al-San’ani told us, Ibrahim bin Aqeel bin Maqil bin Munabbih told me, on the authority of his father Aqeel, on the authority of Wahb bin Munabbih, he said: This is what I asked Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, told me that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say a month before his death: “They ask about The Hour, but knowledge of it is with God, and I swear by God that there is not a living soul on the earth today, a hundred years will come upon it.” And this is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, and they did not narrate it with this understandable and reasonable wording, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only wanted that on earth. Today a baby has been born. He will be one hundred years old from that time when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed them with this speech. Whoever is born after that year will not live for a hundred years. Do you not see that the Commander of the Faithful, may God be pleased with him, had harsh words regarding Abu Masoud? Al-Ansari, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and indeed one of the great companions, may God be pleased with them.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8523 - True"
"8524","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub also informed us of the validity of what we mentioned, Abu Hatim Al-Razi narrated to us, Junada bin Marwan Al-Raqi narrated to us, Muhammad Al-Qasimi Al-Homsi said: I heard Abdullah bin Basr, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited our house with... Abu Bakr, he said: I was arguing between my father and my mother, so we prepared food for him, and he ate and said a supplication for us that I cannot remember, then he wiped his hand on the My head, and he said: “This boy will live for a century.” He said: So he lived for a hundred years.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8524 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8525","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Hatim told us, Dawud bin Rashid told us, Shuraih bin Al-Numan told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Ziyad. Al-Ilahani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Busr, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Long live this boy.” A century.” He said: So he lived for a hundred years and there was a wart on his face, so he said: “This man will not die until the wart goes away from his face.” So he did not die. Until he went
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8525 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8526","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Sana’ani told us about Mecca, which God Almighty guarded. Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Dabari told us, Abd informed us Al-Razzaq, Muammar reported, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Wahb, on the authority of Jabir al-Khaywani, who said: I was with Abdullah ibn Amr when a raid came upon him. From the Levant, and there were two nights of Ramadan remaining, so Abdullah said to him: Did I leave with my family enough for them? He said: I left an allowance with them, and Abdullah said: I bequeathed to you when you returned, so you left for them what was sufficient for them, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “It is enough sin for a man to neglect those he supports.”
He said: Then he started narrating to us, and said: “When the sun sets, it says salutation, prostrates, and asks for permission.” He said: “Then permission is given to it even if it is a day.” “She set, and she saluted, and prostrated, and asked for permission, but permission would not be given to her.” Then she would say: “O Lord, the east is far away, and if permission is not given to me, I will not reach it.” He said: “She will be imprisoned for as long as God wills, then it will be said to her: ‘Go away from where you went.’” He said: “And from that day until the Day of Resurrection, no soul will benefit.” She had not believed before.” He said: “And he mentioned Gog and Magog.” He said: “And a man from among them does not die until a child is born to him from his own loins.” A thousand, and behind them are three nations whose number is known only to God Almighty: rituals, interpretations, and rituals. “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8526 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8527","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahb, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Sedition has hardships and pauses. “If you are able to die while standing, then do so.” Abd al-Rahman said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Hasira, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, was asked: What are its stances? He said: “When the sword is sheathed.” He said: What are its burdens? He said: “When the sword is drawn,” this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8527 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8528","Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih told us, in Baghdad, Ahmad ibn Zuhayr ibn Harb informed us, Musa ibn Ismail al-Tabadhukhi informed us, al-Sa’q ibn al-Sa’q ibn Sadness, Ali bin Al-Hakam Al-Bunani praised us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The princes of The Quraysh did not do three things to you: they were not merciful when they asked for mercy, they were just when they swore, and they were just when they ruled. “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that The two sheikhs, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8528 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8529","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Affan told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Mujalid bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Masruq, said: We were sitting at Abdullah’s house one night, and he was reciting the Qur’an to us, and a man asked him, and he said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, did You asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, how many caliphs this nation has? Abdullah said: No one has asked me about this since I came to Iraq before you. He said: We asked him, and he said: “Twelve leaders of Bani “Israel” “I cannot forgive the story of Mujahid and his peers, may God have mercy on them, in this book.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8529 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8530","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Nu’aym ibn Hammad told me, al-Walid told us, and Rishdin told us, they said: Ibn Lahi’ah, on the authority of Abu Qabil, on the authority of Abu Ruman, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Sufyani will appear in the Levant, and then there will be There will be a battle between them in Qarqisa until the birds of the sky and the wild beasts of the earth are satisfied with their carcasses, then a hole will be opened upon them from behind them, and a group will come forward. From them until they enter the land of Khorasan, and the horses of the Sufyani come in pursuit of the people of Khorasan, and they kill the Shiites of the family of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. In Kufa, then the people of Khorasan will go out in search of the Mahdi.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8530 - Fake news"
"8531","Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Khalid informed us Al-Hudha’, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Asma’, on the authority of Thawban, may God be pleased with him, who said: “If you see the black banners coming out from the direction of Khurasan So go to it, even if you crawl, for therein is the Caliph of God, the Mahdi.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not take it out."
"8532","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Salman bin Rabi’ah, he said: I set out with a group of my companions until we came to Mecca. He said: So we asked Abdullah bin Amr and we did not agree with him, then suddenly three hundred people were approaching, so we returned to him in the mosque, then he saw an old man over him. He was wearing a Qatari robe and a turban, and he had no shirt on. He said: “So who are you?” We said: From the people of Iraq. He said: “You, people of Iraq, lie, deny, and mock.” We said: We do not lie, nor do we deny, nor do we We scoffed. He said: “How much distance is there between you and the deer?” We said: Four farsakhs. He said: “It is about to be that the Banu Qantura ibn Karkar will drive you from Khorasan and Sijistan in a violent manner, then they will leave.” Until they tie their horses to the Tigris River, a people with small eyes and small noses, as if their faces were like hammered shields.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but he did not narrate it."
"8533","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Suwayd Abu Hatim Al-Yamami told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Zayd bin Salam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that when Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman was dying, some Bedouins came to him, They said to him: O Hudhayfah, we only see you arrested, so he said to them: A happy servant, and a lover who came in need. No one is successful who regrets. Oh God, I I did not participate in the treachery of a treacherous person, so I seek refuge in You today from the evildoer. People used to ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about good, and I used to ask him about evil, and I said: O Messenger of God, we were in evil. So God brought us good, so is there evil after that good? He said: He said: “Yes.” I said: Is there any evil behind that good? He said: “Yes.” I said: How? He said: “After me there will be imams who do not follow my guidance and do not follow my Sunnah, and there will arise men whose hearts are the hearts of men in the corpse of a human being.” So I said: What should I do if this happens to me? He said: “You listen to the greatest prince, even if he strikes your back and takes your money.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8533 - True"
"8534","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asbahani Al-Zahid told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin told us Hafs, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ataba, on the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Ansari May God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “This matter will continue among you and you are its guardians as long as you do not do deeds.” Take it away from you, and if you do that, God will make the worst of His creation over you, so you will be bent as a penis is beard.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not take him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8534 - True"
"8535","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ya’la al-Thawri, on the authority of Sa’d ibn Hudhayfah, he said: The faults of Sa’id ibn al-Aas were raised to Hudhayfah, and he said: “I don’t know.” Either of the two things: you wanted to seize the authority of a people that is not yours, or you wanted to repel this sedition, for it is sent from God and takes root in the earth. Until it sets foot on it, no one will oppose it, no one will prevent it, and no one will be left behind, saying: “Allah is Allah,” unless he is killed, and then God will send a people. “Qaza’ is a piece of thin cloud as if it were a shadow when it passed under a large cloud.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8535 - True"
"8536","Ali bin Issa told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Amr told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Jami’, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: He said: Abdullah: “If the balance is low, the rain is shut down, and if adultery increases, murder increases and plague occurs, and if lying increases, chaos increases.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8536 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8537","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad told us, Nu‘aym ibn Hammad told us, Abu Yusuf al-Maqdisi told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “In Dhul-Qa’dah, tribes fight each other.” Then she leaves, and the pilgrim is plundered, and there is a battle in Mina, in which there are many deaths and blood flowing, until their blood flows at Aqaba. The Jamarat, and until their companion escapes and comes between the corner and the shrine, and pledges allegiance, although he is unwilling. It is said to him: If you refuse, we will behead you. He pledges allegiance to him. Like the number of the people of Badr, the inhabitant of the sky and the inhabitant of the earth are satisfied with them.” Abu Yusuf said: Muhammad bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, said: “People perform Hajj together and identify together someone other than an imam, so while they are landing at Mina, when he seized them like a dog, and the tribes revolted against one another, and fought until the Aqaba was dripping with blood, and they would panic. The best of them, and they would come to him while he was facing the Kaaba and crying as if I could see his tears, and they would say: Come, let us pledge allegiance to you. Then he says: Woe to you, how many covenants you have broken and how much blood you have shed, so he pledges allegiance by force, so if you catch him, then pledge allegiance to him, for he is the Mahdi in earth, and the Mahdi is in heaven.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8537 - Its chain of transmission is invalid"
"8538","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Balawayh told me, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, said: I heard Shaddad bin Maqil, the owner of this house, saying: I heard Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, saying: “The first thing You will lose from your religion trustworthiness, and the last thing that remains is prayer, and this Qur’an which is before you is about to be taken up.” They said: “How will it be taken up?” Has God established it in our hearts and confirmed it in our Qur’an? He said: “It will be spread over him for a night and he will remove what is in your hearts and what is in your copies of the Qur’an.” Then he recited: “And if We will, We can certainly take away what We have revealed to you.” [Al-Isra: 86]
Sufyan said: Al-Masoudi told me, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his father, he said: Abdullah said: “You will soon be searched in your villages.” This is a basin of water, and you will not find it. Every water is divided into its element, so there will be in the Levant the remnant of the believers and the water.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8538 - True"
"8539","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Humaid bin Ayyash Al-Ramli told us, Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “There will be princes over you who will torture you and God will punish them.” Sahih chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8539 - True"
"8540","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Urumah told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mundhir Al-Thawri, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: “There will be five tribulations in this nation: a general tribulation, And a specific trial, then a general trial and a specific trial, then there will be a black and dark trial, in which people will be like animals. “This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8540 - True"
"8541","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ishaq bin Al-Hussein Al-Harbi told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashib told us, Shayban bin Abd told us Al-Rahman, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Ulaqah, on the authority of Qutubah ibn Malik, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: “You know that To the extent that mankind differs between Babylon and Al-Hira, you will know that nine tenths of good and tenths of evil are in the Levant. You will know that nine tenths of evil and tenths of goodness besides them, and by the One in whose hand is the soul of Ibn Masoud, it is about to be the most beloved thing on the surface of the earth to “One of you might have a wife who is transporting his family to the Levant.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8541 - True"
"8542","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hadrami told us, Wasil bin Abdullah Al-Ala told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Fudayl, Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Rab’i ibn Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “He studies Islam as The garment covers the creation until they become aware of what is prayer, fasting, or rituals, except that the man and the old man say: We have overtaken the people and their illusions. They say, “There is no god but God.” Then Silah ibn Zufar said to him: And there is no substitute for them, “There is no god but God,” O Hudhayfah, and they know neither prayer nor fasting. Or rituals? Hudhayfah said: “O companions, they will be saved from the Fire. There is no god but Allah from the Fire.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"8543","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ali bin Uthman Al-Lahiqi told me, and Musa bin Ismail told us, they said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, Ali bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led us in prayer. He said the afternoon prayer, then he stood up and preached after the afternoon prayer until the setting of the sun. He who memorized it memorized it, and he who forgot it forgot it, and he told therein as it will be until the Day of Resurrection. He thanked God Almighty and praised Him, then said: “As for what follows, the world is sweet and green. God Almighty has appointed you as your successor therein, and is watching how you do. Indeed, fear the world and fear women. Indeed, the children of Adam were created in various classes, and some of them Who is born a believer, lives as a believer, and dies as a believer, and among them is he who is born a disbeliever, lives as a disbeliever, and dies as a disbeliever, and among them is he who is born a believer. He lives as a believer and dies as a disbeliever, and among them is he who is born as a disbeliever and lives as a disbeliever and dies as a believer. Indeed, anger is an ember that is kindled in the belly of the son of Adam. Have you not seen the redness of his eyes and the swelling of his cheeks? If any of you finds any of that, let him stick to the ground. Indeed, the best of men are those He was slow to anger and quick to rebuke, and the worst of men is he who is quick to anger and slow to rebuke, so if a man is quick to anger and quick to rebuke It is due to it, and if a man is slow to anger and slow to retaliate, then it is due to it. Indeed, the best of merchants is he who is a good judge and has good demands, and is evil. Merchants: Whoever has bad judgment will have bad demand, so if a man has good judgment and bad demand then she gets it, and if the man is bad Judgment is done well, for it is due to it. The fear of people does not prevent a man from speaking the truth when he knows it. Indeed, every treacherous person will have a banner on the Day of Judgment. Resurrection is proportional to his treachery. Indeed, the greatest treachery is the treachery of a public leader. Indeed, the one who betrays his banner is at the time of his attack. Indeed, the best “Jihad is a word of truth before an unjust ruler.” And when it was at sunset, he said: “The likeness of what remains of this world and what has passed from it is like a parable.” “What remains of this day of yours is what has passed.” This is a hadith that was unique in this context to Ali bin Zayd bin Jud’an Al-Qurashi, on the authority of Abu Nadrah. The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, did not use Ali bin Zaid as evidence.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8543 - Ibn Jadaan Saleh Al-Hadith"
"8544","Ali bin Isa bin Ibrahim told us, Musaddad bin Qatn told us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Book of God is descended upon and raised to heaven, but it is not “The earth is a verse from the Qur’an, nor from the Torah, the Gospel, or the Psalms, and it is snatched from the hearts of men, so they wake up and do not know what it is.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8544 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8545","Abu Muhammad al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Hadrami told us, Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, Abu Malik Al-Ashja'i, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha'atha', said: We went out with Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, and we said to him: Make a commitment to us. He said: “You must fear God, and adhere to the group of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, for God Almighty will not unite the group of Muhammad upon misguidance, even if The religion of God is one, and beware of variation in the religion of God, and you must fear God and be patient until a righteous person is relieved and he is relieved from an immoral person. This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and we wrote it with a chain of narration from a source that is not authentic according to this book.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8545 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8546","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Sa`id al-Muddhikir narrated to us, Al-Hussein ibn Dawud ibn Muadh narrated to us, Ali ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayman ibn Nabul, on the authority of Qudamah bin Abdullah bin Ammar Al-Kalabi, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “You must By fearing God and the community, for God Almighty will not unite this nation in misguidance, and you must be patient until righteousness is relieved and relieved from “This is an immoral person. We have only written one hadith with this chain of transmission.”"
"8547","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Maruzi told us, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Ayman bin Nabel, on the authority of Qudamah bin Abdullah bin Ammar Al-Kallabi, may God be pleased with him, who said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, shooting “The Jamarat on the Day of Sacrifice, no beating, no expulsion, and no ‘to you, to you’” This is a hadith with multiple narrations, on the authority of Ayman bin Nabul, and Imam Muhammad protested. Ibn Ismail Al-Bukhari with Ayman Ibn Nabul in Al-Jami’ Al-Sahih”"
"8548","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Abu Al-Mahdi Saeed bin Sinan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Abu Shajara Kathir ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he was He says: “You will never cease to be well as long as the people of your bedouins do not need the people of your city.” He said: “And let them go on for years and years until they are with you in homes, and do not withhold them from them because of the large number of them who hide from you.” He said: “They say, ‘As long as we are hungry and you are full, and as long as we are afflicted and you are blessed. So console us today and we will make the land difficult for you until the people of your city envy your Bedouins because of the difficulty of the land.” He said: “And the earth will move with you in a way, from which whoever perished will perish and whoever remains will survive until the slaves are freed, then the earth will calm down through you after That is until the freedmen regret it.” He said: “Then after that the earth will move with you another way, and in it whoever perished will perish and those who will remain.” It remains until the slaves are freed, then the earth calms down over you, and they say: Our Lord, we will set you free. Our Lord, we will set you free. Then God will deny them: You have lied, I have lied. He was freed.” He said: “And the last women of this nation will be afflicted with trembling. If they repent, God will accept them.” He said: “And if they return, God will repent to them.” With shaking, slander, throwing, eclipsing, distortion, and lightning bolts. When it is said: The people will perish, the people will perish, then they will perish, and God Almighty will not punish. A nation until it betrays.” They said: What is its treachery? He said: “They confess their sins but do not repent, and hearts will be reassured by what is in them of righteousness and immorality just as a tree is reassured by what is in it, until It is not possible for a doer of good to increase his benevolence, nor is it possible for a wrongdoer to reproach him.” That is because God Almighty said: “No, but He has seen it over their hearts.” They did not earn.} [Al-Muttaffifin: 14] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8548 - Saeed is a fallen accused"
"8549","Muhammad ibn Ali al-San’ani informed me of Mecca, which God Almighty protected. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abbad informed me. Abd al-Razzaq informed me. Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, supervised a number of The ruins of the city, and he said: “Do you see what I see?” They said: No. He said: “For I see temptations occurring within your homes like raindrops.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8549 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8550","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Nu‘aym ibn Hammad told me, Abdullah ibn Wahb told me, Yahya ibn Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qabil, heard Abdullah bin Amr say: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was asked which of the two cities would be conquered. First? - Meaning Constantinople or Romans - He said: “The city of Heraclius first,” meaning Constantinople. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it is not He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8550 - True"
"8551","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Sana’ani told me about Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded. Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar narrated, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Hisham bin Amir Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said And he said: “Indeed, the head of the Antichrist will have behind him a hole like yours, and he will say: I am your Lord. So whoever says: You are my Lord will be tempted, and whoever says: You have lied.” My Lord is God, and in Him I put my trust, and to Him I turn, and He will not harm him - or he said: There will be no temptation against him - “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8551 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8552","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, and Yahya bin Saeed, And Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Hind bint Al-Harith, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “What Did he come down from the temptation tonight? And what was opened from the treasures? “Wake up the companions of the rooms - his wives - for perhaps she who is clothed in this world will be naked on the Day of Resurrection.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8552 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8553","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ahmad Al-Shairi told me, Ahmad bin Muadh Al-Sulami told me, Hafs bin Abdullah told me, Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj ibn Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, he said: While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we discussed which of them is better: the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, or the mosque of the Prophet’s house. The Holy Mosque, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than four prayers in it. What a wonderful place to pray, and it will soon be There is nothing for a man like the ground of his horse, from which he can see the Holy House, which is better for him than the entire world - or he said: better than the world. What is in it - “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8553 - True"
"8554","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Lakhmi told us, in Tinnis, Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, Saeed bin Abd told us. Al-Aziz, on the authority of Yunus bin Maysara bin Halbas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said And he said: “Indeed, I saw as if the pillar of the Book had been taken from under my pillow, so I followed it with my sight, and behold, it was a bright light with which I was heading to the Levant. “And faith when temptations break out in the Levant.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8554 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8555","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Quraysh told me, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told me, Safwan bin Saleh told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told me, he told me Abu Aidh Ufeir bin Maadan, that he heard Sulaym bin Amir Al-Kala’i, narrating, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The Levant is God’s elite from His country, to which He drives the elite of His servants. Whoever leaves the Levant for another country will be displeased with Him. And whoever enters it from other than it, it is by His mercy.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8555 - No, Afir is dead"
"8556","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Saeed bin Abdul Aziz told me, On the authority of Makhul, that he narrated it on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hawwala, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “You will be recruited into soldiers: soldiers in the Levant, soldiers in Iraq, and soldiers in Yemen.” I said: O Messenger of God, choose for me. He said: “You must stay in the Levant. Whoever refuses, let him follow his right and drink from its treachery, for God Almighty has taken care of the Levant and its people for me.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 Ufair, on the authority of Sulaym bin Amir, on the authority of Abu Umamah, with a chain of transmission traceable to the Prophet: “The prophecy was revealed to me in three places: in Mecca, Medina, and the Levant.” True
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8556 - True"
"8557","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi informed me, Yahya bin Uthman bin Saleh told me, my father told me, Bakr bin Mudar told me, about Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Jamil bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “O God, let no time overtake me - or let me not overtake the time - of people who do not follow knowledge and are not ashamed of the forgiving, whose hearts are foreigners. “And their tongues are the tongues of the Arabs.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8557 - True"
"8558","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Musa bin Ali bin Rabah, he said: I heard my father, saying: I went out on Hajj, and Suleiman bin Anz, the judge of the people of Egypt, said to me: Convey my greetings to Abu Hurairah, and inform him. In the morning, I asked forgiveness for him and his mother, so I met him and told him. He said: And I asked forgiveness for him. Then he said: How did you leave Umm Hanoo? He means Egypt -? He said: So I mentioned to him about its luxury and livelihood. He said: The land was first desolate, then Armenian. I said: I heard that from the Messenger of May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: No, but Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them, told me: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “It will be a migration after a migration, and the choices of the people of the earth will bind them to the migration of Abraham, and the worst of its people will remain on the earth.” “Their land will consume them, and the soul of God will filth them, and the Fire will gather them together with the apes and the swine.”
And I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “People will come out from the East and recite the Qur’an, but it will not exceed their throats. Whenever it is interrupted, “A century after another generation, until the Antichrist will emerge among the rest of them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it, as they all agreed on The hadiths of Musa bin Ali bin Rabah Al-Lakhmi, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8558 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8559","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yunus told me, about Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, say: “It is about to be that the Muslims’ ultimate weapons will be a weapon, and a weapon will soon be From Khaybar"
"8560","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, and Ja’far bin Ahmad Al-Samani told us, they said: Abu Abdullah Ahmad bin Abdul Rahman bin Wahb, my uncle told me, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with him. On their authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Muslims are about to be besieged in Medina until their furthest weapon will be a weapon.” Hadith Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Jarir, is authentic according to Muslim’s conditions. In his book, may God have mercy on him, he cited Abu Abdullah, may God have mercy on him, as evidence.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8560 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8561","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abu al-Ahwas Muhammad bin al-Haytham al-Qadi told us, Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam bin Nafi told us, Saeed bin Sinan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Kathir bin Murrah, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about The food of the believers in the time of the Antichrist. He said: “The food of the angels.” They said: What is the food of the angels? He said: “Their food is glorification and sanctification, so whoever’s motive on that day was glorification and sanctification, God will remove hunger from him. “He fears hunger.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8561 - No, Saeed is a corrupt accused"
"8562","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad al-Marwazi told us, Abu al-Ahwas al-Qadi told us, Nu`aym bin Hammad told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told me, On the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays ibn Ubadah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, he said: “Whoever reads Surah Al-Kahf as it was revealed. Then he went out to the Antichrist, but he was not overpowered - or: he had no way over him - “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and it was not He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8562 - True"
"8563","Abdan bin Yazid Al-Daqqaq told me, in Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, On the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “You are about to be filled by God with foreigners. “So they will become ungrateful lions, and they will kill those who fight you and eat your prey.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8563 - True"
"8564","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Faqih told us about Al-Ray, Abu Bakr bin Al-Faraj Al-Azraq told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, Abd al-Malik ibn Qudamah al-Jumahi told us, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Abi Bakr, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abi Sa`id, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God have mercy on him. God said on his authority, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “Years will come upon the people in which the liar will be believed, the truthful will be lied to, and the truthful will be betrayed.” The trustworthy, the traitorous will be entrusted therein, and the Ruwaybidah will speak on it.” He said: It was said: O Messenger of God, and what is the Ruwaybidah? He said: “The fool talks about the affairs of the public.” Ibn Qudamah said: Yahya bin Sa’id Al-Ansari told me, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, he said: “And it spreads. Therein is an indecency.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. It is a very strange hadith from Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Al-Maqbari.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8564 - True"
"8565","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Adl told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Marzuq told us, Salih bin Omar bin Shuaib, he said: I heard my grandfather Shuaib bin Omar Al-Azraq, he said: We performed Hajj and passed by the Al-Munkadir road, and the people were taking On it, we lost our way. He said: And while we are like that, we are Bedouins as if it sprang upon us from the earth. He said: O Sheikh, do you know where you are? I said: No. He said: You are in the hills, and this is the white hill that you see are the bones of Bakr ibn Wa’il, and he defeated, and this is the grave of Kulaib and his brother. Sloppy, he said: So he showed us the way, then he said: Here is a man who has companions from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Do you have any companions with him? He said: So I said: Yes, he said: So he took us to an old man whose eyebrows were bound with a bandage in the head of Adam, so we said to him: Who are you? He said: I am Al-Adda bin Khalid, a knight of companions in the pre-Islamic era. He said: So we said to him: Tell us, may God have mercy on you, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. With a hadith, he said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he stood up as if he was frightened, then he came back and said: “I warn you of the three impostors,” so he said Ibn Masoud: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God. You have told us about the one-eyed antichrist and the most deceitful of liars. So who is the third? He said: “A man will emerge among a people, the first of whom will be destroyed, and the last of them will be destroyed. The curse will be upon them constantly in the sweeping tribulation, and he is the Antichrist. Is it not? He eats the servants of God.” Muhammad said: “And he is the furthest of people from gray hair than the condition of Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq, may God be pleased with him.” He narrated a hadith that does not make it authentic for him to say in his narration: It was narrated on the authority of so-and-so and so-and-so, and I do not know him to be just, such-and-such, “and it has This hadith was narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah on the condition of authenticity, and he is the role model in this knowledge.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8565 - The hadith is completely objectionable"
"8566","Ahmed bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Muqri informed us, in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Raja told us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Abu Sabrah al-Hudhali, who said: I met Abdullah bin Amr and he narrated a hadith to me. On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I understood it and wrote it with my own hand: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is what Abdullah bin Amr narrated, on the authority of the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God Almighty does not like the obscene nor the obscene.”
Then he said: “By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the Hour will not come until indecency and indecency, bad neighbourliness, severing of family ties, and even The trustworthy person is betrayed and the traitor is trusted.”
Then he said: “The example of a believer is like that of a palm tree that fell and consumed good things, then it fell and did not spoil or break. And the example of a believer is like the example of a believer. A piece of red gold was brought into the fire and it was blown on, but it did not change. It was weighed and did not decrease. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8566 - True"
"8567","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us: Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Hussein bin Waqid told us, he said: Muadh Ibn Harmala Al-Azdi said: I heard Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A time will come upon the people. “The sky rains rain but the earth does not bring forth.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8567 - True"
"8568","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih informed us of a dictation in Baghdad. He said: It was read to Yahya bin Hafs bin al-Zabarqan, and I was listening. Khalaf bin Tamim Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Kufi told us, Ismail bin Ibrahim bin al-Muhajir told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Abd told me Allah bin Abbas: If I had not heard that you are like Ahl al-Bayt, I would not have narrated this hadith to you. He said: “Mujahid said: It is in a concealment that is not Mention it to whomever you dislike. He said: Ibn Abbas said: “There are four of us, the Ahl al-Bayt: of us is the Saffah, of us is the Warner, of us is the Mansour, and of us is the Mansur. “The Mahdi,” he said: Then Mujahid said to him: Explain these four to me, and he said: “As for the murderer, perhaps he killed his supporters and pardoned his enemy. As for Al-Mundhir, he said: He gives a lot of money without being arrogant in himself, and withholds a little of what is due to him. As for Al-Mansour: he is given Victory over his enemy is half of what was given to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. His enemy is terrified of it over a period of two months’ journey, and Al-Mansur is terrified. his enemy from him at a distance of a month, and as for the Mahdi who will fill the earth with justice as it was filled with injustice, and the animals and wild animals will be safe and “The earth, what are the places of its liver?” He said: I said: What are the places of its liver? He said: “The likes of a cylinder of gold and silver.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8568 - Where is the validity of it, when Ismail is unanimously agreed upon his weakness, and his father is not that?"
"8569","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Sarjis, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You have been overtaken by temptations like pieces of a dark night. The people are saved therein by a man riding a high mountain eating from the messengers of his sheep, or a man taking a “His horse from behind the path eating from his sword” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8569 - True"
"8570","Abu Al-Tayyib Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Hairi told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abi’s brother Wael, he said: Abdullah said: “How will you be when a trial overwhelms you in which the old grow old, the young grow up in it, and the people take it as a sunnah? If it was changed, they would say: Has the Sunnah been changed? “It was said: When is that, Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: “If your readers are many, your jurists are few, your wealth is abundant, your trustworthy people are few, and you seek this world by doing the hereafter.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8570 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8571","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Duri told us, Abu Amer Abd Al-Malik bin Omar Al-Aqdi told us, Kathir ibn Zaid, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Salih, said: Marwan came one day and found a man with his face on the grave, so he grabbed his neck. He said: Do you know what you are doing? He said: Yes, so he approached him and found it was Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him. He said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and I did not come Al-Hijr I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “Do not cry over the debt when its people are in charge of it, but cry over it when someone else is in charge of it.” “His family” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8571 - True"
"8572","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Abu Ismah Sahl bin al-Mutawakkil told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Raqqashi told us, Ja`far bin Sulaiman told us, Farqad al-Sabkhi told us, on the authority of Asim bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “A people from this nation spend the night on food, drink, and amusement, and then they become transformed into pigs, and they will be swallowed up by tribes within it and houses within it, until In the morning, they say: “Tonight’s eclipse was in the house of so-and-so.” Tonight’s eclipse was in the house of so-and-so’s house, and pebbles of stones were sent upon them just as they were sent upon The people of Lot, and the destructive wind was sent upon them, and it destroyed them as it had destroyed those before them by drinking wine and consuming usury. And their clothing of silk, and their wearing of maidens, and their severing ties of kinship.” He said: “And he mentioned another characteristic, but I forgot.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. He surrendered to Ja`far, but as for Farqad, they did not expel him.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8572 - True"
"8573","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hasan told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Samak Ibn Harb, who said: I heard Jabir Ibn Samurah, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Let treasures be opened for you.” “Khosrau Al-Abyad - or the one in Al-Abyad - is a group of Muslims.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8573 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8574","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, in Egypt, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Imran Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Hasten to do deeds; Six days before the sun rises from the west, and the smoke, and the antichrist, and the beast of the earth, and the beast of one of you, and the affairs of the common people.” Muslim protested. By Abdullah bin Rabah, this is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8574 - True"
"8575","Muhammad ibn al-Mu'mil ibn al-Hasan told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha'arani told me, Nu'aym ibn Hammad told us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid told us, on the authority of Yazid. Ibn Abdullah Al-Jahmi, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: I entered upon Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and a man with her, and he said The man: O Mother of the Believers, tell us something about the earthquake. She turned her face away from it. Anas said: So I said to her: Tell us, O Mother of the Believers. About the earthquake, she said: “O Anas, if I told you about it, you would live sad, and you would be sent back when you were sent, with that sadness in your heart.” So I said: O mother. Tell us, and she said: “If a woman takes off her clothes in someone other than her husband’s house, she violates the veil between her and God Almighty, even if If she perfumes herself for someone other than her husband, then fire and hooks will be upon her. If they make adultery permissible and drink alcohol after this and play musical instruments, God will be jealous of her. His sky, and He said to the earth: Shake with them, and if they repent and withdraw, otherwise He will destroy it for them. “So Anas said: A punishment for them? She said: “Mercy, blessing, and admonition to the believers, and punishment, wrath, and torment for the unbelievers.” Anas said: “I have not heard after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. A hadith with which I am more happy than I am with this hadith. Rather, I live with joy and I am sent when I am sent, and that joy is in my heart - or he said: in Myself - “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8575 - Rather, I consider it fabricated"
"8576","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Kathir bin Zaid, He said: Al-Walid bin Rabah, the client of Ibn Abi Dhubab, told me that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “I asked my Lord for three things, and He gave me two, but withheld one from me. I asked Him not to destroy my nation with years, and He gave me, and I asked Him: He does not let an enemy from anyone else dominate them. So he gave me, and I asked him: That he not divide them into sects, and let them taste the violence of one another, so he prevented me. “This is a hadith.” The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"8577","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Balawayh Al-Aqbi told me, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Hanbal told us, Hadba bin Khalid told us, Abd told us Al-Aziz bin Abdul-Samad Al-Ammi, Yazid bin Al-Miqdam told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: He We saw from everything that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us, except that he said: “It will be said to the men on the Day of Resurrection, ‘Cast down your whips and enter. Hell” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8577 - True"
"8578","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Khaled bin Arfata, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “O Khaled, there will be events and temptations after me.” There is a difference. If you are able to be Abdullah who was killed and not the killer, then do so. Ali bin Zaid al-Qurashi was the only one to do so, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi. And they did not use Ali as evidence.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8578 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8579","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Hafiz al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Ishaq bin Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ishaq bin Suleiman Al-Razi, said: I heard Malik bin Anas speaking, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Jabir bin Atik, that he said: Abdullah came to us Ibn Amr in Bani Muawiyah - which is one of the villages of the Ansar - and he said: Do you know where the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in your mosque? This? He said: I said: Yes, and I pointed to him towards a side of it, and he said: Do you know what the three things he prayed for were? I said: Yes, and he said: Tell me about them, so I said: “He prayed that no enemy from anyone else would appear against them, and that he would not destroy them with years, so I would give them both. “He prayed that He would not cause trouble among them, but he prevented it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8579 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8580","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil ibn al-Hasan told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, Nu’aym ibn Hammad told us, Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Maslama bin Ali, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “It will be A rumbling in the month of Ramadan wakes the sleeper and frightens the awake, then a group appears in Shawwal, then a crowd in Dhul-Hijjah, then it is violated. Incests in Muharram, then there will be death in Safar, then there will be conflict between tribes in the spring, then all the wonder between Jumada and Rajab, then a she-camel. A quote is better than a raid of less than a hundred thousand.” The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, argued that they narrated this hadith on the authority of the last of them without a Muslim Ibn Ali Al-Khushani, and it is a hadith with a strange text, and it is also Muslim, one of those for which there is no evidence.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8580 - The subject"
"8581","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Al-Awza’i told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Many times, Abu Salamah told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: I went back to Abu Hurairah and put him to my chest, then I said: Oh God, heal Abu Hurairah. He said: “Oh God, do not return her.” Then he said: “If you are able, O Abu Salamah, to die, then die.” So I said: O Abu Hurairah, we love. Life, so he said: “By the One in whose hand is Abu Hurairah’s soul, there will come to the scholars a time of death more beloved to any of them than red gold. If one of you comes to his brother’s grave and says: “I wish I were in his place.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8581 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8582","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Musa bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad told me, Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Bayhaqi told us, Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, said: I used to ask people about the hadith of Adi bin Hatim while he was next to me. In Kufa, I came to him and said: A hadith that I told about you, so tell me about it. He said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent, I hated him the most I hated him. Nothing at all, so I came to the farthest corner of the Arab land and hated it, then I came to the land of the Romans and I hated it as much as I had hated it before or more, so I said: We will come to this man. If he is truthful, then I will hear from him. If he is lying, then he is not malicious. So I went to him and asked him. He said: “You are To ask about something that is not permissible for you in your religion.” It was as if I saw him in relief, and he said: “O Uday bin Hatim, accept Islam,” twice, and he said: He has shown me - or I may think, or as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said - and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Perhaps he is only preventing you from “Islam is that you see poverty around me, but you see people as being oppressive to us.” Then he said: “Have you seen the confusion?” I said: I did not see her, but I knew her place. He said: “It will soon be the case that Al-Dha’inah will leave from Al-Hira without a neighbour, until she circumambulates the Kaaba, and it will be opened.” On us are the treasures of Khosrau.” I said: Khosrau ibn Hurmuz. He said: “Khosrau ibn Hurmuz, and it is about time that a man will no longer find that his money is given in charity.” And he said: “I saw The woman departs and I swear that the second will be opened according to the words of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which is the truth. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not take him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8582 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8583","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us about irrigation, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris told us, Muhammad bin Yazid bin Sinan told us, My father, Sulaiman Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God is about to That He will fill your hands with non-Arabs and make them into lions that will not flee, so that they will strike your necks and eat your prey.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8583 - Rather, Muhammad bin Zaid bin Sinan is as weak as his father."
"8584","Abu Hafs Ahmad bin Hanbal, the jurist in Bukhara, told us, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Usama told us, saying: I heard Sufyan bin Saeed saying: Al-Amash reported, Abu Amara reported, on the authority of Silah ibn Zufar, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: “There will be over you princes who abandon the Sunnah like this - and he pointed to the point of his finger - even if You abandoned them, they brought the great catastrophe, and there was no nation except that the first thing they left of their religion was the Sunnah, and the last thing they called upon prayer was. “And had they not been ashamed, they would not have prayed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8584 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8585","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi told us, Yusuf bin Suhayb told us, Musa bin Abi told me Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Bilal bin Yahya Al-Absi, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a mission to Dumat Then he said, “Go, for you will find Acheder-Dumah out hunting for game, so take him.” So they went and found him just as he said. They took him, and the people of the city fortified themselves and supervised the Muslims speaking to them. He said: A Muslim man said to some of the people who supervised: I remind you, by God, do you find Muhammad in your book? He said: No. Another person next to him said: We find him in our book resembling a Quraysh who was touched by the pen of Satan. Then the man said: O Abu Bakr, has he not These people disbelieved. He said: “Yes, and you will disbelieve.” When the army returned and Musaylimah left and he prophesied, the man said to Abu Bakr: Do you not remember? What did you say, “And we are at Dumat al-Jandal, and you will disbelieve” that is the matter of Musaylimah? He said: “No, that is at the end of time.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8585 - True"
"8586","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Zakaria bin Yahya Al-Saji told us, Muhammad bin Ismail bin Abi Saminah told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim, Al-Awza’i narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “A man called Al-Sufyani will emerge in the depths of Damascus, and most of the dogs will follow him, and he will be killed until He rips open the stomachs of women, and kills children, so Qays gathers for them and kills her so that the sin of Talah is not prevented, and a man from my household comes out in Then it reaches Al-Sufyani, and he sends an army of his to him and defeats them. Then Al-Sufyani marches to him with those who are with him, until when it becomes In a clearing of the earth, they will be swallowed up, and none of them will be saved except the one who informs about them. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8586 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8587","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulayman told us, he said: I heard Praiseworthy, Al-Hasan told us, Hattan bin Abdullah Al-Raqqashi told me that they came with Abu Musa as raiders, and when they camped at a house, he said: “We were We say that there will be chaos before the Hour. They said: What is the chaos, O Prince? He said: “Killing.” We said, “The most we kill is that we kill in a year, God willing, more than a hundred thousand.” He said: “Your killing is not by the polytheists.” But killing one another.” He said: We said, “And with us were our minds at that time.” Abu Musa said: “Most of the minds of that time will be taken away, and left in vain.” Of the people, most of them think that they are upon something, but they are not upon anything. By God, I will not find it for you or me if it catches up with me and you in what we read. The Book of our Lord, and in what our Prophet has covenanted with us, that we should not depart from it as we entered it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8587 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8588","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abi Al-Abbas, who was a Shiite, on the authority of Abu Al-Tufayl, on the authority of Bakr bin Qarawish, heard Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The devil of the parlor.” A man from Bujaila called him: Al-Ashhab - or Ibn Al-Ashhab - a horse herder, and a horse herder is a sign among the unjust people. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8588 - What is farthest from it and denied it"
"8589","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Shayban bin Abdul Rahman told us, On the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rab’i ibn Harash, on the authority of Al-Baraa ibn Najiya Al-Kahili, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The mills of Islam revolve for thirty-five or thirty-six days. If they perish, then it is the way of those who perished, and if they are resurrected, They will have their religion, which will last for them for seventy years. Then Omar said: O Messenger of God, for what has passed or for what remains? He said: “With what remains.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. It is a hadith whose chain of narration is outside the three books. I narrated it out of amazement, since “It is close to where we are.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8589 - True"
"8590","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn al-Musayyab told us, Nu’aym ibn Hammad told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Abd Al-Wahhab bin Hussein, on the authority of Muhammad bin Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The emergence of an animal after the sun has risen from the west. When it came out, it would strike Satan while he was prostrating and enjoying himself.” The believers will be on earth forty years after that, not wishing for anything but they will be given it, and they will find it, and there will be no injustice or injustice, and He has submitted all things. To the Lord of the Worlds, willingly or unwillingly, to the point that the seven do not harm an animal or a bird, and a believer is born and does not die until he completes forty years after the appearance of an animal. the earth, then death returns among them, and they remain like that as long as God wills. Then death hastens among the believers, and no believer remains, so the unbeliever says: We were terrified of the believers, but not a single one of them remained, and no repentance would be accepted from us, so they would flee in the streets like animals, then they would arise. One of them takes his mother, his sister, and his daughter and has intercourse with her in the middle of the road. One of them gets up on her behalf and another goes down on her without denying it or changing it. The best of them on that day will be those who say: If you had recanted from the path, that would have been better. And they will be like that until not one of the children of the marriage remains. And the people of the land will be the children of incest, and they will remain like that as long as God wills. Then God will barren the women’s wombs for thirty years, so that no woman will give birth or “There will be a child on earth, and they will all be the children of fornication, the worst of people, and upon them the Hour will come.” Muhammad bin Thabit bin Aslam Al-Bunani, one of the most honorable Basra and the children of the Successors, except that Abdul-Wahhab bin Al-Hussein is unknown.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8590 - The subject and peace"
"8591","Al-Hussein bin Halim Al-Maruzi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed, Abdul Razzaq informed, Abdullah informed, Sufyan informed, about Al-Mugheerah bin Al-Numan told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Bahili told us, Al-Ahnaf bin Qais told us, he said: I was in Medina when I saw a man fleeing. People like him when they see him, so I said: Who are you? He said: I am Abu Dharr, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I said: Why do people flee from you? He said: “He forbade them from hoarding as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to forbid them.” He said: I said: Our gifts have increased. Today, do you fear anything for us? He said: As for today, no, but it is about to be the cost of your religion, so if it is the cost of your religion, leave it and beware. This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8591 - True"
"8592","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Kamil Al-Muradi told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Sa’id bin Abi told me Ayoub, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Alqamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, and I do not know him except on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “God will send to this nation at the beginning of every hundred years someone who will renew its religion.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8592 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8593","So I heard Professor Abu Al-Walid, may God be pleased with him, saying: I was in the council of Abu Al-Abbas bin Shurayh when a sheikh came up to him and praised him. So I heard him say: Abu Al-Tahir Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told me, on the authority of Sharahil bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Alqamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God sends at the head of all For a hundred years, who will renew her debt? So give good news, O judge, for God sent Omar bin Abdul Aziz to be at the head of the hundred, and he sent The head of the two deaths was Muhammad ibn Idris al-Shafi’i, and you are the head of the three hundred. He said:
[full sea]
Two have passed away, and he was blessed in them... The age of the Caliph, then he succeeded Al-Saud.
Al-Shafi’i Al-Abtahi Muhammad... The legacy of prophecy and Muhammad’s cousin
Give good news to Abu Abbas that you are the third... after them to irrigate the soil of Ahmad.
He said: Judge Abu Abbas, may God Almighty have mercy on him, began to cry and said: This sheikh mourned for me, so a group of people spoke to me. My friends, they attended the gathering of Sheikh Imam Abu Al-Tayyib Sahl bin Muhammad bin Suleiman, and this story was mentioned, so they told it about me. In his presence, and in the council was Abu Amr al-Bistami, the arja’i jurist, so Abu Amr established at that time:
[full sea]
And the fourth famous one, Sahl Muhammad... became an imam for every monotheist.
Muslims take refuge there with all their families... in knowledge. If they go out, then yes, supporter.
There is still a sheikh among us... the chosen doctrine has the best renewal.
So I asked the jurist Abu Amr in my gathering, and he recited it to me.”"
"8594","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi told me, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Sufyan informed, on the authority of Jami’ Ibn Abi Rashid, on the authority of Abu Ya`la Mundhir al-Thawri, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali, on the authority of a loyalist to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, she said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went to see Aisha - or some of the wives of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him - while I was with him, and he said: “When the bad thing appears, do not Forbid it. God has sent down His punishment upon them. Then a person said: O Prophet of God, even if there are righteous among them? He said: “Yes, what befell them will happen to them, then they will go to God’s forgiveness and mercy - or to God’s mercy and forgiveness -.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8594 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8595","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein Al-Hamdani told us, and Muhammad bin Ghalib bin Mahran told us, they said: Abu Hammam told us Muhammad bin Habib, Sufyan bin Saeed Al-Thawri told us, Jafar bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, He said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned the hour, his cheeks would turn red, his anger would intensify, and his voice would raise as if he were warning an army. He says: “Good morning and evening.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8595 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8596","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Al-Awza’i told us, Ismail bin Ubaid Allah, Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanm al-Ash’ari told me, he said: Abu al-Darda’ said to me: How do you see people? I said: It is fine, for their call is one, their imam is one, their enemy is exiled, and their gifts and livelihoods are at hand. He said: “So how? When their hearts enmity each other, and their tongues curse, and their enmity becomes apparent, and relations become corrupt between them, and they strike the necks of one another. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8596 - True"
"8597","Muhammad ibn al-Mu’mil told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn al-Musayyab told me, Nu‘aym ibn Hammad told us, Uthman ibn Kathir ibn Dinar told us, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Sinan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Abu Shajara Kathir ibn Murrah, on the authority of Hudhayfah ibn Al-Yaman, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “My nation will not be tried until distinction, sway, and oppression appear among them.” I said: O Messenger of God, what is distinction? He said: “Differentiation: a fanaticism that people introduced to Islam after me.” I said: What is swaying? He said: “The tribe leans against the tribe and deprives it of its sanctity.” I said: What are the persecutions? He said: “The countries marched one to another, their necks differing in the war.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8597 - Rather, Saeed is accused of it"
"8598","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Kamil al-Qadi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sa’id al-Jamal narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abd al-A'la bin Abd al-Hakam, a man from Bani Amir, on the authority of Kharijah bin al-Salt al-Burjami, who said: I entered the mosque with Abdullah, Then, when the people were bowing, he bowed, and a man passed by and greeted him, and Abdullah said: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. Then he reached the line, and when he finished, I asked him about His saying: God and His Messenger spoke the truth, and he said: He used to say: “The Hour will not come until the mosques take roads, and until one man greets another.” With knowledge, until a woman and her husband trade, and until horses and women go to extremes, then they take it easy and do not go to extremes until the Day of Resurrection.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8598 - True"
"8599","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, in Egypt, Safwan bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Awf bin Abi told us Jamila, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the Day of the Camel came, I wanted to go to them and fight with them, until I mentioned I recently heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he heard that Chosroes or some of the non-Arab kings had died, so they made a woman their ruler, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A people who are owned by a woman will not prosper.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"8600","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmed bin Mahran bin Khaled Al-Asbahani told us, Ubaid told us Allah bin Musa, Yunus bin Abi Ishaq reported, on the authority of Hilal bin Khabab, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he mentioned the sedition - or it was mentioned to him - and he said: “Then the people have postponed their covenants. And their trustworthiness diminished, and they became like this.” He interlaced his fingers, and I stood up to him and said: “What should I do then, O Messenger of God? God made me May I be sacrificed for you? He said: “Control your tongue, sit at home, and take what you know and leave what you deny, and you must control yourself especially, and leave behind the affairs of the public.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8600 - True"
"8601","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told me, Hashim bin Yunus al-Assar in Egypt told us, Sa`id bin Abi Maryam told us, Yahya informed us Ibn Ayyub, Amara Ibn Ghaziyah told me, on the authority of Muslim Ibn Abi Hurra, he said: When Ibn al-Zubayr was besieged, and the doors of the mosque were fortified from... The people of the Levant. He heard two of his guardians behind him, and they spoke some words, so he turned to them and said: “None of the books I followed have followed. I read the books and heard the hadiths, and I found everything to be false except what is in the Book of God Almighty.” He said: So he left and received the pillar, then he went in to his mother. Asmaa, so he kissed her and kissed from between the veil to the face above the forehead, and she said: What do I hear? She was told: The people of the Levant. She said: Are they all Muslims? It was said to her: Yes, that is what they claim. She said: I have seen Islam, and if they had gathered together over a sheep, they would not have eaten it. Then she said: O my son, die with honor. And do not give up. Abdullah said: “Where are the people of Egypt?” They said to him: At the gate, the gate of Bani Juma, and he had the most people at the gates, so he attacked them and they were exposed to the market. He said: And indeed, Khubayb He strikes them with the sword from behind them, and says: Carry on, and no one will enter upon it. He said: Then he will carry it, and they will be uncovered. He said: When they saw That's when they brought Aswad in, and when they saw him they turned around so he could see him. He said: So Aswad entered until he was between the curtains of the Kaaba, and when he came to him, he came out. Then Ibn al-Zubayr hit him and both of his legs staggered, he said: so he began to bear down, he said: then he fell down, and he did not look at him until a stone came to him. So he struck him at the ear, and he fell down, so they killed him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8601 - True"
"8602","So Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Awf told us, Abu Al-Siddiq narrated to us, saying: When Al-Hajjaj defeated Ibn Al-Zubayr, killed him and mutilated him, then he went to see Umm Abdullah, who is Asma’, my father’s daughter. Bakr, so she said: How can you ask permission to do so when you killed my son? He said: Your son was an atheist in the sanctuary of God, so you killed him as an atheist and a sinner until God made him taste a painful punishment, and he did to him and he did so, so she said: You lied, oh The enemy of God and the enemy of Muslims. By God, I killed him for fasting, upholding righteousness to his parents, and preserving this religion, even though his world was ruined for him. He has spoiled your hereafter, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us: “Indeed, two liars will emerge from Thaqeef. The other of them is worse than the The first, which is Al-Mubir, and it is no one but you, O Hajjaj.”"
"8603","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abu Omar Al-Hudhi told us, and Amr bin Marzuq told us: We told him: Shu'bah, on the authority of Husayn, so he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner, and added to it, so Al-Hajjaj said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke the truth, and I, Al-Mubir, spoke the truth. The greatest hypocrites said: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8603 - True"
"8604","Muhammad bin Musa bin Imran, the muezzin, informed me. Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad bin Jafar told us, Shu’bah, he said: I heard Abu Hamzah speaking, on the authority of Iyas ibn Qatada, on the authority of Qais ibn Abbad, he said: I was approaching Medina and met people from The companions of the Messenger of God, and the most beloved of them to me was Ubayy ibn Ka’b. He said: So I came to Medina at the time of Omar, and they performed the morning prayer, so Omar came out. May God be pleased with him, and some men went out with him, and behold, a man from among the people was looking at the faces of the people. He recognized them and denied me, so he pushed me away and stood in my place. So I prayed, and what was the most reasonable of my prayers? When he prayed, he said: O my son, may God not harm you. I did not do what I did out of ignorance. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “Be in the row next to me,” and I looked at the people’s faces and recognized them as different from you. He said: And he sat down. I did not see the men craning their necks towards something, heading towards it. Then, behold, it was Ubayy ibn Ka’b, and he was as he said: The people of Al-Aqad have perished, and by God The people of Al-Aqd and the Lord of the Kaaba have perished, and God is not saddened by them. He is only saddened by those of the Muslims who were destroyed. This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8604 - True"
"8605","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Samak bin War. He said: I heard Malik bin Zalim speaking, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The destruction of my nation is at my hands.” “Aghailam from Quraysh” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it due to a dispute between Shu’bah and Sufyan Al-Thawri regarding it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8605 - True"
"8606","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, we told him Sufyan, and Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, Abdullah bin Zalim told me, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, saying: I heard Abu Al-Qasim, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, he said: “The corruption of my nation is at the hands of foolish people from Quraysh.” So I heard Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub saying: I heard Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Qabbani, saying: I heard Amr bin Ali, saying: “The correct one is Malik bin Zalim.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8606 - True"
"8607","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Amr bin Malik Al-Nakri told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawza, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he said: “Gog and Magog are a span and two spans, and three spans, and they are from the descendants of Adam.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8607 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8608","Ahmad ibn Kamil al-Qadi informed us, Ahmad ibn Sa`id al-Jamal told us, Ruh ibn Ubadah told us, Sa`id ibn Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, On the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Subay’, on the authority of Amr ibn Harith, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told us: “The Antichrist will emerge from a land in the East called Khurasan, followed by people whose faces look like hammered shields.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
It was narrated by Abdullah bin Shudhab, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Subay, on the authority of Amr bin Harith, who said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq fell ill. May God be pleased with him, then his appearance was revealed and he led the people in prayer. They thanked God and praised him, then he said: I am an adviser to you. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, he says: “The Antichrist will emerge from the east, from a land called Khurasan, and with him will be people whose faces are like demons.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8608 - True"
"8609","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Abd Al-Aziz bin Hatim Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Saeed bin Saqiq told us, Amr bin Abi Qais, Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hurairah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He said: “The Antichrist will emerge from here, or here, or from here. Rather, he will emerge here,” meaning the East. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8609 - True"
"8610","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told me, Al-Hussein bin Sufyan and Imran bin Musa told us, they said: Abu Kamil Al-Jahdari told us, Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman al-Taffawi, Ayoub told us, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, he said: People used to pass by Hisham bin Amir and go to Imran bin Husayn. Hisham said: These people are going to a man whom we used to see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, more than him, and from whom we learned more. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Between the creation of Adam and the arrival of the Hour there is a trial greater with God than the Antichrist.” This is an authentic hadith. According to Al-Bukhari’s condition, they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8610 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8611","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Omar bin Yunus bin Al-Qasim Al-Yamami told us, Jahdam bin Abd told us. Allah Al-Qaysi, on the authority of Abdul-Ala bin Amir, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: I was in Al-Hateem with Hudhayfah, and he mentioned a hadith, then he said: “The bonds of Islam will be torn down, one by one, and they will be misguided imams, and they will revolt against The effect of this was the three impostors. I said: O Abu Abdullah, have you heard this what you say from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, I heard him
And I heard him say: “The Antichrist will emerge from the Judea of Isfahan. His right eye will be wiped and the other will look like a flower that will split the sun. And the bird from the round makes three calls, which the people of the East and the people of the West hear, and with it are two mountains, a mountain of smoke and fire, and a mountain Of trees and rivers, and he says, “This is Paradise and this is Hell.”
And I heard him say: “A liar will emerge from before him.” He said: I said: What is the third? He said: “He is the most deceitful of liars. He will emerge from the east, followed by the tribe of the Arabs and the lowliest of the slaves. The first of them will be destroyed. And the last of them are destined to be destroyed according to the extent of their authority over them. The curse of God will be upon them forever.” He said: So I said: It is absolutely astonishing. He said: “And I am astonished.” From that it will happen, so if you hear about it, then flee.” He said: I said: What should I do with whomever I left behind? He said: “Order them to follow the tops of the mountains.” He said: I said: If they are not left behind, and that. Their homes,” he said: I said: If they are not left behind, and that, he said: “O Ibn Omar, the time of fear, chaos, and plunder.” He said: I said: O Abu Abdullah, what Why is there any relief for this commotion? He said: “Indeed, there is no turmoil that does not have relief, but where is there anything left for it? It is a tribulation, which is called sweeping, that comes upon the plains of the Arabs. And Sareh the loyalists, and those with treasures, and the rest of the people, then it was revealed from less than a little: “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8611 - Rather, it is objectionable"
"8612","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoob Al-Hafiz, may God Almighty have mercy on him, told us: Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Muadh told us Ibn Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, he said: I was in Kufa, and it was said: The Antichrist has come out, he said: So we came upon Hudhayfah ibn Usayd was speaking, so I said: This imposter has come out. He said: Sit down, so I sat down, and the sergeant came to me and said: This impostor has come out. And the people of Kufa were disobeying him. He said: Sit down, so I sat down and it was called out. It is a false lie. He said: So we said: O Abu Sariha, you have only made us sit down. For something, he told us, he said: “If the Antichrist had come out in your time, the children would have slandered him with malice, but the Antichrist will come out in hatred of the people, and out of fear.” of religion, and bad character, so every outlet will be returned, and the earth will be folded for him like a ram’s scalp, until he comes to Medina, and he will be defeated by outside it and forbidden inside it, then he mounts Elijah and besieges a band of Muslims, and those who are against them say to them: What do you expect from this tyrant? That you fight him until you join God or an victory is granted to you. Then they plot to fight him when they wake up, and they arrive in the morning, with Jesus, son of Mary, with them. Then he will kill the Antichrist and defeat his companions, to the point that the tree, the stone, and the cairn will say: “O believer, this is a Jew with me, so kill him.” He said: And there are three signs in it: He is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed, and written between his eyes is an unbeliever, which every believer, illiterate and scribe, will read, and no one will mock him. Mounted creatures, except the donkey, for it is an abomination upon an abomination. Then he said: “I am more afraid of me and you than the Antichrist.” He said: So we said: What is it, O Abu? A hairstyle? He said: “Trials as if they were parts of the dark night.” He said: So we said: Which of the people is evil in them? He said: “Every fiancée will be banished, and every passenger will be placed in place.” He said: So we said: Which of the people is good in it? He said: “Every rich person is hidden.” He said: So I said: I am neither rich nor hidden. He said: “So be like the son of a lion, neither a back to ride nor an udder.” So he is milked.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8612 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8613","Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zamjari told us, Ahmed bin Muaz Al-Sulami told us, and Muhammad bin Issam told us, they said: Hafs bin Abdullah told us. Al-Sulami, Ibrahim bin Tahman told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The Antichrist will emerge in Lightness of religion, and maturity of knowledge, and He has forty days in which He goes, of which one day is like a year, and one day is like a month, and one day is like a year. Like Friday, then the rest of his days are like your days, and he has a donkey that he rides, the width of which is forty cubits between his ears. People come and he says: I Your Lord, and indeed your Lord is not one-eyed. Written between His eyes is the Qur’an, which every believer, scribe and non-writer, will read. He will pass by every water and outlet except Medina and Mecca were made sacred to him by God, and the angels stood at their gates. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8613 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8614","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Muawiyah told me Ibn Salih, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Jubayr Ibn Nufayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned the Antichrist, and he said: “If he comes out and I am among you, then I will be his plea, and if he comes out and I am not among you, then every person will be his own plea, and God is my successor over every Muslim. And his eye is smeared as if it were the eye of Abd al-Uzza ibn Qatan al-Khuza’i. Indeed, written between his eyes is an infidel. Every Muslim reads. He met him among you, so let him recite the Fatihah of the Cave. He came out from between the Levant and Iraq. He moved to the right and to the left. O servants of God, stand firm” three times. It was said: O Messenger of God, how long did he stay on earth? He said: “Forty days: one day like a year, one day like a month, one day like a Friday, and the rest of its days are like your days.” They said: O Messenger of God. So how will we perform prayers on that day or perform the prayers of a day? He said: “Rather, you can.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8614 - True"
"8615","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Yahya bin Sa’id told us, Hisham told us Ibn Hassan, Humayd Ibn Hilal told me, on the authority of Abu Ad-Dahma, on the authority of Imran Ibn Husayn Al-Khuza’i, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever among you hears of the appearance of the Antichrist, let him stay away from him, for a man comes to him and thinks he is a believer, but he continues to follow him.” From what he sees of doubts.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration on the condition of Muslim, and he did not narrate it, and I do not know of anyone who mentioned on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan in Its chain of transmission is other than Yahya bin Saeed.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8615 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8616","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever hears of the Antichrist should stay away from him - So he said it three times - for the man comes to him and he follows him, so he thinks that he is telling the truth because of the doubts with which he was sent.”"
"8617","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Muqri informed us in Baghdad, and Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi. Bamru, they said: Abu Qalaba al-Raqqashi told us, Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith bin Sa`id told us, my father told me, Yazid bin Salih told us, that Aba Al-Wadhi Abbad bin Naseeb narrated to him that he said: We were on a march heading towards Kufa with the Commander of the Faithful Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, when we reached two or three nights’ journey from Harwara, some of us deviated from us, so we mentioned that to Ali, and he said: Do not be alarmed by their situation. They will return, so we camped, and when the next day, a group of people like me left a group of groups, so we mentioned that to Ali, and he said: Do not be alarmed by their situation. Their matter is easy, and Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: Do not start a fight with them until they are the ones who start you, so they knelt down on We rode them and protected us with our shields, so they attacked us with crossbows and arrows. Then they approached us and supported us with spears, then they attacked us with swords. Until they were about to put swords on us, then a man from Abd al-Qais, called Sa`sa’a bin Suhan, came out to them. He called out to three of them and they said: What do you want? He said: I remind you, by God, that you should not go out with a land that will be an insult to the people of the land.And I remind you, by God, to escape from debt as the arrow escapes from the target. When we saw them laying swords among us, Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: Arise. With the blessing of God Almighty, it was nothing but hiccups during the day until those of us who had slept went to bed and those who had fled fled, so praise be to God for Ali, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: My friend, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me, “The leader of these people is a man with a scarred hand and hairs on his nipple, as if they were “The tail of a jerboa, so look for it.” They looked for it but did not find it, so we came to it and said: We did not find it. He said: Look for it, for by God I have not lied. And I did not lie, for we continued to touch him until Ali himself came to the last battle that they had, and he continued to say: Turn that around. Turn that around, until a man from the people of Kufa came and said: Here he is, and Ali said: God is the Greatest, and by God no one will come to you and inform you. Whose father is a king, so people said: This is a king. This is a king. Ali says: Whose son? They say: We do not know. Then a man from the people of Kufa came and said: I am the most knowledgeable of the people about this. I was taming a foal for so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, an old man from among the children. So-and-so, and I put easy collars on her back with which I could move forward and backward, when the filly ran away and he called me and said: O boy, look, for the foal has fled,So I said: I saw a horse as if it were a crow or a sheep, when this man loomed over us, and he said: Who is the man? He said: A man from the people of Al-Yamamah. He said: Why did he bring you shaggy and pale? He said: I came to worship God in the prayer hall of Kufa, so he took in his hand, “We have no fourth place but God,” until he took him home, and said to his wife: “Indeed, God God Almighty has brought good to you. She said: By God, I am in need of it. So what is that? He said: This man is shaggy and pale as you can see. He came from Al-Yamamah to worship God in the prayer hall of Kufa. He used to worship God there and pray to the people until People gathered around him, and Ali said: My friend, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me, “They are three brothers from the jinn, and this is the eldest of them.” The second has a large number of plurals, and the third has double. Muslim, may God have mercy on him, narrated the hadith of al-Mukhdāj by way of succinctness in the musnad. The correct one, and they did not narrate it in this context, “and it has an authentic chain of narration.”"
"8618","Ahmad ibn Uthman al-Muqri and Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi told us, saying: Abu Qalaba told us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd told us. The heir, my father told us, Husayn bin Dhakwan Al-Mu’allim told us, Ubayd Allah bin Buraidah Al-Aslami told us, that Suleiman bin Rabi’ah Al-Anazi told him. He once performed Hajj under the command of Muawiyah, and with him was Al-Muntasir bin Al-Harith Al-Dhabi, in a group of Quran reciters from the people of Basra. He said: When they finished Their sacrifice, they said: By God, we will not return to Basra until we meet a satisfactory man from the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, who will narrate to us a hadith. We will tell our companions about it when we return to them. He said: We did not stop asking until he told us that Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas was satisfied. By God, he was descending on their behalf at the foot of Mecca, so we headed towards him, and behold, we were traveling with a great burden in three hundred mounted groups, of which one hundred were mounted. And two hundred burdens, so we said: Who is this burden for? They said: By Abdullah bin Amr, so we said: Is this all for him? And we were talking about him being one of the most humble people. He said: So they said: Who are you from? So we said: From the people of Iraq. He said: So they said: The fault of you is due, O people of Iraq. As for this hundred departing, it is for his brothers. He carries them on it, and as for the two hundred in a group, it is for those of the people upon whom it descends.He said: So we said: Show us him, and they said: He is in the Sacred Mosque. He said: So we went looking for him until we found him at the back of the Kaaba sitting. Then he saw that he was short, with a scarf, bald, with two cloaks and a turban on him, no shirt on him, his sandals hanging on his left side, so we said: O Abdullah, you are A man from the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he told us a hadith that God Almighty will benefit us from after today. He said: Then he said to us: Who are you? He said: So we said to him: Do not ask who we are, talk to us, may God forgive you. He said: Then he said: I will not speak to you anything until you tell me who you are. We said: We wish that you had not saved us and pardoned us and told us some of what we ask you about. He said: He said: By God, I will not speak to you until you inform me. Which country are you from? He said: When we saw him swore and entered, we said: We are people from Iraq. He said: So he said: Is it wrong for all of you, O people of Iraq? You are lying. And you deny and mock. He said: When he reached the level of mockery, we found that to be very severe. He said: So we said, God forbid, that we should mock someone like you. As for your statement of lying, by God, lying has spread among people and among us, and as for lying, by God, we will hear a hadith that we have not heard from anyone. Someone we trust, then we almost lie to him,As for your saying “the mocker,” no one mocks the Muslims like you. By God, today you are the master of the Muslims as far as we know. You are one of the first immigrants, and we have learned that you recited the Qur’an to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and that there was not on earth a more righteous Quraysh. His parents are better than you, and you were the best of people with eyes, so your eyes were spoiled by crying, and then you read all the books after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. No one has better knowledge of ourselves than you, and we do not know of any Arab man remaining who was superior to the jurists of the people of Egypt until he He enters another Egypt seeking knowledge from an Arab other than you. Tell us, may God forgive you. He said: I will not speak to you until you give me Covenanting that you will not deny me, nor deceive me, nor mock. He said: So we said: Take from us whatever covenants you wish. Then he said: God’s covenant is upon you. And His covenants are that you shall not deny me, nor lie against me, nor ridicule what I tell you. He said: So we said to him, “It is against us.” He said: Then he said: Indeed, God God Almighty is a guarantor and agent over you. So we said: Yes, and he said: O God, bear witness over them. Then he said at that time: As for the Lord of this mosque and the land. The sacred, the sacred day, the sacred month,And I have taken the right, isn't that? We said: Yes, you have worked hard. He said: “It is about to be that the Banu Qantura bin Karkari will have short noses and small eyes, as if their faces were of madness.” The hammer in the revealed Book of God is that they will drive you out of Khorasan and Sijistan in a violent manner, a people who are full of their burdens and who wear hair. And they hold the swords on their waists until they bring down the deer. Then he said: “How many deer are from Basra?” We said: Four farsakhs. He said: “Then they will tie the head of a horse to each of the Tigris palm trees, then they will send to the people of Basra to Get out of it before We send it down to you. Then the people of Basra will leave Basra, and someone who comes will join the Holy House, and others will join. In Medina, others will join Mecca, and others will join the Bedouins.” He said: “They will stay in Basra for a year, then they will be sent to the people of Kufa: Get out of it before We descend upon you. Then the people of Kufa will leave it, and someone who will follow will join the Holy House, and what will follow. In Medina, others in Mecca, and others among the Bedouins, so not a single one of the worshipers will remain except one killed or a prisoner, and their blood will be judged as they wish.” He said: So we left him, and we were upset by what he had told us, so we walked away from him not far away, then Al-Muntasir bin Al-Harith Al-Dhabi left.He said: O Abdullah bin Amr, you spoke to us and stabbed us, for we do not know who among us could realize it, so tell us, is there a sign of that in my hands? Abdullah bin Amr said: “Do not lose your mind. Yes, there is a sign in my hands.” Al-Muntasir bin Al-Harith said: What is the sign? He said: “The sign is the sign.” He said: “And what is that sign?” He said: “It is the emirate of the boys. If you see the emirate of the boys having spread over the earth, know that what I am telling you has come.” He said: So he departed. On the authority of Al-Muntaser, he walked close to a distance and then returned to him. He said: So we said to him: Why are you bothering this sheikh from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: By God, I will not finish until he explains it to me. When he returned to him, he clarified it: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8618 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8619","Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ziyad al-Qattan told us in Baghdad, Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Narsi told us, Azhar told us Ibn Saad, Abdullah Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Imran Ibn Muslim Al-Khayyat, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Wahb, he said: We were with Hudhayfah on this occasion. The mosque, and he said: “The temptations have come to you, targeting you with violence, then the next one you attack with subjugation, then the darkness after them. There is not even a man among you. He sees what you see. He has never seen the temptation of the Messiah. He will never see it.” He said: “And among us are Bedouins from Rabi’ah, and there is no living among us other than him.” He said: Glory be to God, O Companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, how about the Messiah when he has described to us a broad forehead overlooking the good side, far between the shoulders, for I saw Hudhayfah said goodbye to her and said: I called upon you by God. Do you know how I said that? He said: I said: “There is not a man among you who sees what you see. He has not seen the temptation of the Antichrist and will never see it.” He said: I saw Hudhayfah struggling with his face. He said: I said: Because he memorized the hadith according to its authenticity? He said: Yes, he said: Then he said a weak word: “Did you see the day of the battle yesterday? It was a general turmoil that engulfed the people.” He said: And among us are Bedouins from Rabia, there is no one alive among us other than him. He said: Glory be to God, O companions of Muhammad, so where are those who inject our pollen and dig into our homes? He said: “Those are the sinners” - twice - He said: “I went out on the day of the dose and I learned that not a cup of blood had been spilled in it, and that I forbade it except Ibn al-Hasramah. “And among us are Bedouins from Rabi’ah, and none of us is alive except him.” He said: Glory be to God, O companions of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Ibn Al-Hasramah greeted the people, excluding the people, and said: “When it comes, it will be for the one who is standing and the one who said it, and Ibn Al-Hasramah is a man who is a narrator.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They used Imran ibn Muslim as evidence, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8619 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8620","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Mihran informed us, my father told us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb informed us Al-Qurashi, my uncle told me, Yunus bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Amr al-Sibani, on the authority of Amr’s hadith. Al-Hadrami, from the people of Homs, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us one day, and it was Most of his sermons mentioned the Antichrist. He spoke to us about him until he finished his sermon, when he said to us that day: “Indeed, God Almighty has not sent A prophet except that he warns his nation of the Antichrist, and I am the last of the prophets and you are the last of the nations, and he will inevitably emerge among you. If he emerges and I am in the midst of I show you that I am the pilgrim for every Muslim, and if he comes among you after me, every person will be the pilgrim for himself, and God is my successor over every Muslim. He emerges from a gap between Iraq and the Levant, so he spreads to the right and to the left. O servants of God, stand firm, for he begins to say: I am a prophet and there is no prophet. After me, then he will be repeated until he says: I am your Lord, and you will not see your Lord until you die, and indeed, written before his eyes is an unbeliever, and every believer will read it. So whoever of you meets him, let him spit on his face, and recite the opening verses of Surah Ashab al-Kahf, and he will give authority over any soul among the children of Adam. So he kills her, then brings her back to life, and that he does not go beyond that and does not control the soul of anyone else, and that part of his temptation is that with him is a garden and a fire, so his fire is Paradise and his paradise is fire, so whoever is afflicted by its fire should close his eyes and seek help from God. It will be coolness and peace for him just as the fire was coolness. And peace be upon Ibrahim, peace be upon him, and one of his temptations is that he passes by a neighborhood, and they believe in him and believe him, and he prays for them and it rains from the sky. They will be upon them from that day, and the land will be fertile for them from that day, and their livestock will be upon them from that day, the greatest and fattest they have ever been. And He stretched out his waist and rounded his udders, and he passes by the living, but they disbelieve in him and deny him. Then he supplicates against them, but no one who wanders free becomes theirs. Its days are forty; a day is like a year, a day is like a month, a day is like a Friday, and a day is like a day, and its last days are like a mirage. At the gate of Medina in the evening before reaching its gate to the Hereafter. They said: How do we pray, O Messenger of God, in those short days? He said: “You can do it during it and then pray as you can during the long days.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it with this. ""driving""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8620 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8621","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Baghawi Al-Adl informed us in Baghdad, Ja`far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, Abu Muawiyah Shaiban bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Atiya al-Awfi, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that he heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “Indeed, every prophet has warned his nation of the Antichrist, and that on this day he has eaten food, and I am covenanted with it.” A covenant that no prophet had made before his nation before me, except that his right eye, which is anointed, has a bulging pupil, and it is not hidden as if it were marrow in the side. A wall, except that his left eye is as if it were a shining star, and with it are like paradise and like fire, for fire is a green meadow, and paradise Smokey dust. Indeed, before him were two men warning the people of the villages. Whenever they entered a village, they warned its people, and when they left it The first of the companions of the Antichrist will enter it, and he will enter all the villages other than Mecca and Medina, which were sacred to him, while the believers are dispersed in the land, and he will gather them together. God has him, then a man of the believers says to his companions: Let us go to this man and see if he is the one whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, warned us about. Peace be upon him or not, then he passed away.Then his companions said to him: By God, we will not let you come to him, even if we know that he will kill you if you come to him. We will leave you on your way, but we fear that He will tempt you, but the believing man refused to go to him, so he started walking until he came armed with one of his weapons, so they took him and asked him what What is your business and what do you want? He said to them: I want the antichrist, the liar. They said: You say that? He said: Yes, so send for the Antichrist. We have captured someone who says such-and-such, and shall we kill him or send him to you? He said: Send him to me, so he set off with him until the Antichrist was brought. When he saw him, he recognized him and described the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Antichrist said to him: What? What's your business? Then the believing servant said: You are the antichrist and the liar whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, warned us about. The antichrist said to him: Are you saying this? He said: Yes. The Antichrist said to him: You must obey me in what I command you, otherwise I will divide you into two parts. So he called out to the believing servant and said: O people, this is the Messiah. He is a liar, so whoever disobeys him will be in Paradise, and whoever obeys him will be in Hell. The Antichrist said to him: By what I swear by, you will obey me or I will make you miserable. Two parts, so the believing servant called out and said: O people, this is the false Messiah. Whoever disobeys him will be in Paradise, and whoever obeys him will be in Hell.He said: So he extended his foot and placed his iron on his tailbone and split it in two. When he did that to him, the Antichrist said to his friends: Did you see? If I revive this for you, do you not know that I am your Lord? They said: “Yes.” - Attiya said: Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri told me that the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: - “He struck one of his parts or the high land.” Then he stood upright, and when his friends saw him, they believed him and were certain that he was their Lord, and they answered him and followed him. The Antichrist said to the believing servant: Don't you believe in me? The believer said to him: Because now I have more insight into you than before. Then he called out to the people, “This is the false Messiah. So whoever obeys him is in Hell, and whoever disobeys him will be in Paradise. The Antichrist said: And by what I swear, you will obey me, or I will slaughter you, or I will throw you into Hell. So he said to him: The believer: By God, I will never obey you. So he ordered him to lie down - he said: Then Abu Saeed said to me: The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: - “Then he made Two copper plates between his collarbones and his neck” - he said: Abu Sa’id said: I did not know what copper was before that day - “so he went to slaughter him. But he was not able to do so, and he did not gain power over him after he killed him.” He said: “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace,He said: “So he took him by his hands and feet and threw him into Paradise, which was dusty and full of smoke, as though it were fire. That man is the closest of my nation in degree to me.” - He said: Abu Saeed said: The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not think that this man was anyone except Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, until he walked Omar is on his way. He said: Then I said to him: How will he perish? He said: God knows best. He said: So I said: I was informed that Jesus, the son of Mary, peace and blessings be upon him, will destroy him. So he said: God knows best, other than that He will destroy him. God and whoever follows him. He said: I said: Who will be after him? He said: The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told me - “Indeed, they will plant trees after him.” And they will take the wealth after him.” He said: I said: Glory be to God, remove the Antichrist. They will plant plants and take the wealth after him. He said: Yes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me about that. “This is the most amazing hadith in mentioning the Antichrist, and it was only mentioned by Atiya bin Saad, on the authority of my father.” Saeed Al-Khudri, and the two sheikhs did not use Attiya as evidence.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8621 - Atiyah is weak"
"8622","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, On the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah, the client of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, on the authority of Ka’b bin Alqamah, on the authority of Ibn Hujayra, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir Radi On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Before the hour a black cloud will rise over you from the west, like a shield. It continued to rise in the sky until it filled the sky, then a caller would call out: O people! Let the people turn to one another. Have you heard? Some of them say: Yes, and some of them doubt, then he calls the second: O people, and the people say: Have you heard? They say: Yes, then he calls: O people, the command of God has come, so do not rush it. The two men spread the garment and never fold it or exchange it, and the man spreads his cistern and does not water anything in it, and the man To milk his she-camel, but he will never drink it, and the people will be busy.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8622 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8623","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Al-Jamahir Muhammad bin Othman Al-Dimashqi told us, Al-Haytham bin Humaid told me, Abu Ma’bad told me Hafs bin Ghaylan, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, said: I was with Abdullah bin Omar when a young man came to him asking him about lowering the turban. Ibn Umar said: I will tell you about that with knowledge, God willing. He said: I was the tenth of ten people in the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted: Abu Bakr, Omar, Uthman, Ali, Ibn Masoud, Hudhayfah, Ibn Awf, and Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with them. Then a young man from the Ansar came and greeted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he sat down and said: O Messenger of God, which of the believers is best? He said: “The best of them in character.” He said: Which of the believers is the most intelligent? He said: “The ones who remember death the most and prepare best for it before they take them out of the sack.” Then the boy remained silent.
The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, approached him and said: “O community of immigrants, there are five things that if you are afflicted with them and it descends upon you, I seek refuge in God that You will overtake them: Never has an indecency appeared among a people until they act upon it, except that plague and torments that had not occurred in the past will appear among them. Their predecessors, and they did not diminish the measure and the balance, but they were oppressed by the years, the severity of the provisions, and the injustice of the authority over them, and they did not withhold zakat. Unless they prevented the rain from the sky, and if it were not for the animals, it would not rain, and they did not break the covenant of God and the covenant of His Messenger, unless their enemy imposed power over them. changed them and took some of what was in their hands, and as long as their imams did not rule by the Book of God, God cast their punishment among them.” Then he ordered Abd Al-Rahman ibn Awf was preparing for a expedition he had sent, and Abdul Rahman was veiled with a turban of black scarves, so the Prophet brought him to him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then he tore it off, turbaned it with a white turban, and sent four fingers or something like that behind it and said: “This is it, O son of “Awf is dark, for it is more expressive and better.” Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered Bilal to give him the banner, so he thanked God and sent blessings upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. peace be upon him, then he said: Take Ibn Awf and fight all of you in the way of God, and fight those who disbelieve in God. Do not exaggerate, do not deceive, do not impersonate, and do not You kill a newborn, for this is the covenant of God and the life of His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8623 - True"
"8624","Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad, the grammarian in Baghdad, told us, Abd al-Karim ibn al-Haytham told us, and Abu Muhammad told me Al-Muzani and the pronunciation for it, Ali bin Muhammad bin Issa told us, saying: Abu Al-Yaman told us, Shuaib told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: He told me Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf, on the authority of Abu Bakra, Ziyad’s maternal brother, and Muhammad bin Ali bin Abd al-Hamid al-San’ani told me, In Mecca, protected by God Almighty, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Abbad told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Talha Ibn Abdullah Ibn Awf, on the authority of Abu Bakra, Ziyad’s maternal brother, said: Most people spoke about Musaylimah the liar before he said anything about him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and praised God as he deserved, then he said: “As for what follows: You have said much about this man, and he is one of thirty liars who will emerge before the Antichrist, and there is no country in which terror does not enter. Messiah, except for Medina, over each of its domes on that day will be two angels removing the terror of Christ from it.” Muslim protested with Talha ibn Abdullah bin Awf, and Muammar and Shuaib bin Abi Hamza mixed this chain of narration, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, because Talha bin Abdullah did not He heard it from Abu Bakra. He only heard it from Iyad bin Musafa’, on the authority of Abu Bakra like this. It was narrated by Yunus bin Yazid and Aqeel bin Khaled, on the authority of Al-Zuhri “
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8624 - Talha did not hear it from Abu Bakra"
"8625","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Yunus told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf narrated to him, on the authority of Iyad bin Musafa’, on the authority of Abu Bakra, Ziyad’s maternal brother, who said: When the number of people in The case with Musaylimah the liar, before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said what he said about him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and praised... God for what he deserves. Then he said: “As for what follows, you have raged about this man, and he is a liar out of thirty liars who will come out before Antichrist, and there is no country but the terror of the Messiah will enter except the city, on every one of its sides, on that day two angels will defend it. The terror of Christ”"
"8626","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Anazi narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi narrated to us, Abdullah bin Saleh Al-Masry narrated to us, Al-Layth told me, Aqeel told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf told me, that Iyad bin Musafa’ told him that Abu Bakra, Ziyad’s maternal brother, told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and delivered a speech and praised God as he deserved it. Then He said: “As for what follows, you have exaggerated regarding Musaylimah, and he is a liar from among thirty liars who will emerge before the Antichrist.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Saad bin Ibrahim Al-Zuhri, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakra, briefly."
"8627","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my father told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, on the authority of Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The terror of the Antichrist will not enter Medina. That day there will be seven gates, and each gate will have two kings.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8627 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8628","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Usama told us, about Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Qarat, said: I heard Saad bin Malik and Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with them, saying: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “O God, bless the people of Medina in their debt and in their hardship, and bless them in their city. O God, Abraham He, peace be upon him, is your servant and your friend, and I am your servant and your messenger, and Abraham asked you for Mecca, and I ask you for Medina just as he asked you. Abraham for Mecca and the same with him, except that the city is surrounded by angels, at each of its gates there are two angels guarding it, no one will enter it. The plague and the antichrist. Whoever intends harm on its people, God will dissolve him just as salt is dissolved in water.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, and it was not ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8628 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8629","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari and Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi informed us, saying: Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Suraqa, on the authority of Abu Ubaida bin Al-Jarrah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he mentioned the Antichrist and dressed him with an ornament that I do not remember. They said: O Messenger of God, our hearts On that day like today? He said: “Or better.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “It was narrated by Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha, and his leg was more perfect than anyone.” Hadith of Shu`bah
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8629 - True"
"8630","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Khaled Al-Hadha told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Suraqa, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “Indeed, there was no prophet after Noah except that he warned his nation of the Antichrist, and indeed I warn you of him.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, described him to us. He said: “You will realize it, or some of those who saw me and heard from me will realize it.” We said: O Messenger of God, our hearts will be as they are on that day. Today? He said: “Or better.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8630 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8631","Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Khalid Al-Hudha’ told us, On the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Muhjan bin Al-Adra’, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed the people, and said: “On the day ""Salvation and the Day of Salvation"" three times, then it was said: O Messenger of God, what is the Day of Salvation? He said: “The Antichrist will come and take someone up and look at the city and say to his companions, ‘Don’t you see this white palace? This is the mosque of Ahmad. Then he comes to the city and finds in every veil a king praying, so he comes to the rosary of the cliff and strikes Then the city will tremble three times, and there will not remain a hypocrite, male or female, or immoral or immoral, unless he goes out to it, and the city will be saved. “And that is the Day of Salvation.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8631 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8632","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marw, Abu Al-Mujah Muhammad bin Amr Al-Fazari told us, Abdan bin Uthman told us, My father told me, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salim, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: By God, if it were not for anything I have not spoken to you recently. They said: You said: The Hour will not come until such and such. He said: I only said: Such and such will not happen until it is a matter. Great, it happened that, the house was burned and it happened like that, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Antichrist will come out and stay in my nation as long as he wants.” “God will remain for forty,” and I do not know whether it was a night, a month, or a year. He said: “Then God sent Jesus, son of Mary, peace and blessings be upon him, as if he were a handhold.” Ibn Masoud Al-Thaqafi” He said: “Then he will seek him until he destroys him” He said: “Then the people will remain for seven years with no enmity between the two” He said: “Then God will send A cold wind comes from the Levant, so it does not leave anyone who has an atom’s weight of faith in his heart without taking his soul, even if one of you is in “Like a mountain,” he said: “Then the worst of people will remain those who do not He recognizes what is right and does not deny what is wrong, such as the fear of birds and the dreams of wild beasts.” He said: “Then Satan comes to them and says: Will you not respond? “He said: “Then they say: What do you command us to do? He said: “Then he commands them to worship idols, and they worship them, and in that they are provided with a good livelihood.” He said: “Then the trumpet will be blown.” No one will hear him unless he listens, and the first person to hear him will be a man who sodomizes his camel’s pelvis.” He said: “He will be shocked, then people will be shocked, and God will send Rain as if it were dew.” He said: “Then their bodies will sprout.” He said: “Then it will be blown upon, and lo, they are standing and looking, and it will be said: Come to your Lord.” Stop them, for they will be held responsible.” He said: Then it will be said: “Bring out the creatures of the Fire.” He said: “It will be said: How much?” It is said: Out of every thousand nine hundred and ninety-nine, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8632 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8633","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, about Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Muwarriq, on the authority of Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I see what You do not see, and I hear what you do not hear. Indeed, the sky is enlarged, and it has the right to surround what is in it - or whatever is in it - the place of four fingers except And an angel with his forehead prostrated to God Almighty. By God, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and cry much, and you would not enjoy women. On the plains, and you would go out to the ascents, daring to God. By God, I wish I were a tree that was supported. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not ""He takes him out""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8633 - True"
"8634","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya and Abu Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Dawrqi told us, saying: Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah, Muhammad bin Hassan Al-Azraq told us, Rayhan bin Saeed told us, Abbad told us, he is Ibn Mansour, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abi Qalaba, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Men from my nation will come to Jesus, son of Mary, may blessings be upon them both.” And peace, and they will witness the fight of the Antichrist.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8634 - Munkar"
"8635","Muhammad bin Al-Muzaffar Al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, Mahmoud bin Musfa Al-Homsi told us, Ismail told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever among you finds Jesus, son of Mary, let him recite it.” From me, may God’s peace and blessings be upon them both, “I think this Ismail is Ibn Ayyash, and they did not use him as evidence.”"
"8636","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Raba’i, On the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He studies Islam as he studies the hem of a garment. He does not know what fasting means.” There is no charity or rituals, and the Book of God Almighty is revealed in one night, and not a sign of it will remain on earth, and groups of people will remain. Sheikh The old man and the old woman say: We taught our fathers this word: “There is no god but God,” so we say it. “So Silah said: So what It is of no use to them: There is no god but God. They do not know what fasting, charity, or rituals are? So Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, turned away from him, so he repeated to him three times, all of which he turned away from, then he turned to him for the third time, and said: “O Silah, You will save them from the Fire, you will save them from the Fire, you will save them from the Fire.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8636 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8637","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ali al-Shaybani told me about Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim al-Ghafari told us, Qubaisah ibn Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, On the authority of Awf, on the authority of Anas ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “Only four verses have passed: the Dajjal, the beast, and Gog.” And Magog, and the rising of the sun from the west, and the verse with which God seals the sun: “Then He recited: {Do they wait except that it should come to them? The Angels} [Al-An’am: 158] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8637 - True"
"8638","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Wasiti told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, the common people informed us Ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Jablah Ibn Suhaim, on the authority of Muathir Ibn Afaza, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: “When it was the night The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was taken on captivity. He met Abraham, Moses, and Jesus, may the peace and blessings of God be upon them. They started with Abraham and asked him about the hour. He did not He had no knowledge of it, so they asked Moses, but he had no knowledge of it, so they referred the hadith to Jesus, and he said: God’s covenant with me concerning I appointed it. As for its destiny, no one knows it except God Almighty. He mentioned the emergence of the Antichrist, so I will go down and kill him, and the people will return to Their country, and Gog and Magog will meet them, and they will descend from every direction. They will not pass by any water without drinking it, or by anything without spoiling it. Then they would come to me, so I would pray to God, and He would send water from the sky and carry them and throw their bodies into the sea. Then the mountains would be blown up and stretched out. The earth is the expanse of the earth, and God has covenanted with me that when the Hour comes, people will be like a pregnant woman who has died, and its people will not know when it will surprise them. By her giving birth, night or day.” The common people said: “I found confirmation of that in the Book of God Almighty. Then he read: {Until when Gog is opened And Magog, and they are slipping away from every direction, and the true promise has drawn near.” [Al-Anbiya’: 97]"
"8639","Abu Amr Uthman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Sammak, the ascetic in Baghdad, informed us. Hanbal ibn Ishaq ibn Hanbal informed us. Musa ibn Hanbal informed us. Ismail, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Signs are beads.” “Arranged with wires, so if the wires are cut, they follow one another.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not take it out.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8639 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8640","Abu Al-Tayyib Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Hairi told me, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, Ismail bin Abi told us Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, who said: Hudhayfah went out at the back of Kufa, with a man with him, and he turned to the side of the Euphrates and said to his companion: “How? On the day you see them leaving - or emerging from - it, they will not taste a drop of it.’ A man said: And do you think so, Abu Abdullah? He said: “I do not think it is, but I know it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8640 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8641","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Affan bin Muslim, and Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, they said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Abu al-Bakhtari speaking, on the authority of Abu Thawr, who said: I was sitting with Hudhayfah and my father. Masoud, where the people of Kufa disdained Saeed bin Al-Aas on the day of the potion, so Abu Masoud said: I did not think that he would return without rushing there. Blood, then Hudhayfah said: But by God, I knew that we would return on our heels and not spill a cup of blood in it, and I knew nothing of that except something. I knew him while Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is alive “that a man in the morning is a believer and in the evening an unbeliever, having nothing of his religion with him, and he enters the evening a believer and becomes an unbeliever.” And he has nothing of his religion. He fights in today’s strife, and God Almighty kills him tomorrow. His heart will be broken and his head will rise above him. I said: the bottom of it? He said: Ask him"
"8642","Abu Al-Hussein Ali bin Abdul Rahman Al-Subaie told us in Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim Abi Gharza told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, he reported Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Amr ibn Qais Al-Malali, on the authority of Atiya, on the authority of Ibn Umar, in this verse: {And when the word falls upon them, We will expel “For them is an animal of the earth that speaks to them.” [An-Naml: 82] He said: “If they do not enjoin what is right and do not forbid what is wrong.”"
"8643","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan bin Ayyub told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Zakaria bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Yazid told us The reciter, Haywa bin Shurayh told us, Bashir bin Abi Amr Al-Khawlani told me that Al-Walid bin Qais Al-Tajibi told him that he heard Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “There will be a successor after sixty years who neglected the prayer. And they follow their desires, they will meet with destruction. Then there will be a successor after sixty years. They will recite the Qur’an, no more than their throats. And three people will recite the Qur’an. A believer, a hypocrite, and an immoral person.” Bashir said: So I said to Al-Walid: Who are these three? He said: “The hypocrite disbelieves in it, the immoral person eats in it, and the believer believes in it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8643 - True"
"8644","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the Martyr told us, and Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us. Al-Shaarani, they said: Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Zufar bin Abdul-Rahman bin Adrak told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sulayman bin Walabah, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, no The Hour will come until immorality and miserliness will appear, and the trustworthy will be betrayed and the traitor will be trusted, and the deer will perish, and the whale will appear.” So they said: Oh Messenger of God, what are the deer, and what are the whales? He said: “The deer are the faces of the people and their nobles, and the Tuhut who were under the feet of the people are not known.” This hadith was narrated by all of them. Civilians with no type of wound attributed to them.”"
"8645","Abu Al-Fadl Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab bin Habib Al-Abdi told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us. Al-Umari, Abu Hayyan Al-Taymi reported, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, who said: Three people in the city sat with Marwan, and they listened to him. He talks about the signs, the first of which is the emergence of the Antichrist, so the group got up from Marwan, and they sat with Abdullah bin Amr and told him what Marwan had said. Abdullah said: Marwan did not say anything. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The first of the signs to emerge is the rising of the sun from its west, or the animal, whichever was first, then the other will soon follow it.” Then he began to narrate, saying: “That is because when the sun sets She came under the throne and prostrated and asked for permission to return, but nothing was answered for her. He said: “Then she returned to ask permission to return, but nothing was answered for her. He said: O Lord, how far is the east for me to have people, until, when night came, she came and asked permission, and He said to her: Get out of your place. He said: Abdullah was reading books, so he recited: “And that is a day when {no soul will be of benefit if it had not believed before or gained in its faith.” Good} [Al-An’am: 158] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”"
"8646","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abdullah bin Yusuf Al-Tanisi told us, Abu Hafs Al-Qadi Othman told us. Ibn Abi Al-Atika, Sulayman bin Habib Al-Muharbi told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “When the epics take place, a delegation of loyalists will emerge from Damascus. They are the most noble of the Arabs in horsemanship and the finest in weapons. May God strengthen the religion through them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8646 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8647","Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Aqeel bin Khuwaylid Al-Khuza’i told me, my father told us, on the authority of his father, Hafs bin Abdullah told me, Ibrahim told me Ibn Tahman, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj Ibn Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Muhallab Ibn Abi Sufra, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr Ibn Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him About them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fire will be sent upon the people of the East, and it will gather them to the West, and you will spend the night with them, where They spent the night, and she would go with them wherever they said, and she would have whatever of them that had fallen and left behind, and she would drive them to the market of a broken camel.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not take him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8647 - True"
"8648","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Attab Al-Makki told us, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Abi Talib told us, Ali bin told us Asim, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Harb ibn Abi Al-Aswad, Talha Al-Nadhari told me, he said: The man was one of us when he came to Medina. He descended upon the suffah, and if he had a master there, he descended upon his master, and if he did not have a master there, he descended upon the suffah. I came to Medina but he was not there for me. Arif, so the description was revealed, and every day a mudd of dates between two people would come to us from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they would cover us with sheep. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led some of the daytime prayers with us. When he said the salutation, the people of Suffah called out to him, right and left: O Messenger of God, burn our bellies. Dates and the sheep were torn from us, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose to his pulpit and went up and thanked God and praised Him, then he mentioned the severity of He did not meet any of his people until he said: “And there has been brought upon me and upon my companion some portion of what is mine and his food, except for the wild.” - He said: So I said to Abu Harb: And what is righteous? He said: Bad food, the fruit of arrak. I will find for you bread and meat to satisfy you with, but perhaps you will reach a certain time, or whoever of you will reach it, will have lunch and rest for you dry. And you will be clothed like the curtains of the Kaaba.” Dawud said: Abu Harb said to me: “O Dawud, do you know what the coverings of the Kaaba were at that time?” I said: No. He said: “White clothes that were brought from Yemen.”
Dawud said: I narrated this hadith to Al-Hasan bin Al-Hasan, and he said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Today you are better than yourselves.” On that day, you will be brothers by the grace of God, and on that day you will be enemies, striking each other’s necks.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”
[p. 592]

[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8648 - True"
"8649","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Asam told us about the Qantara Burdan, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Abd told us Al-Hamid bin Jaafar, Suwayd bin Al-Ala told us, and Muslim narrated on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Al-Ala, and Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Faqih narrated to me, May God Almighty have mercy on him, Abu Hamid bin Al-Sharqi told us, Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdul Hamid bin Hafs told us, Al-Aswad bin Al-Ala told us, On the authority of Abu Salamah, he mentioned it similarly."
"8650","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Abu Asim Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, Abdul-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, Al-Aswad bin Al-Ala told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her. On her authority, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Night and day will not pass until Al-Lat and Al-Uzza are worshipped, and God sends A pleasant wind, and he who had in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of goodness will die, and those in whom there is no good will remain, and they will return to the religion of their fathers.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”"
"8651","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman bin Al-Hasan Al-Faqih narrated to us in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Mala’ab bin Hayyan narrated to us, Ali bin Asim narrated to us, Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, said: Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, narrated an example of strife, and he said: “The example of strife is only that of a group Three were accompanied on a journey, so they traveled at night and gathered at a crossing of three, and one of them said: Turn to the right, so he turned to the right and lost the way, and the other said: Then he took the left path and left the path. The third said: He stayed in my place until morning, so he took the path. Then in the morning, he took the path.”
Ali bin Asim said: Awf told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, he said: “We were talking that a good time will come upon the people. His family is he who sees the truth near and avoids temptations.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8651 - Ali bin Asim Wah"
"8652","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, Mas’ar told us, On the authority of Ubaid Abi Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Abdullah bin Mughaffal, he said: Ibn Abdullah bin Salam wanted to go towards the Levant, so Abdullah informed him. God is from above a house, and he said: “O my son, do not make me sad because of yourself, for the cry of every Muslim will come from the Levant.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8652 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8653","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told me in Bukhara. Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Hafiz told us, Abdullah bin Omar bin Maysarah, Muadh bin Hisham told us, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad Al-Dili, he said: Zur’ah bin Damra and I set out. Al-Ash'ari, to Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, and we met Abdullah ibn Amr, and he said: It is likely that he will no longer remain in the land of the non-Arabs. Except for a dead person or a prisoner whose blood is to be judged. Zur’ah said: Will the polytheists support Islam? He said: Who are you from? He said: From Banu Amir bin Sa’sa’a, and he said: The Hour will not come until the women of Banu Amir will defend Dhul-Khalasa - an idol that was called in the pre-Islamic era - He said: So we mentioned to Omar bin Al-Khattab what Abdullah bin Amr said, and Omar said three times: Abdullah bin Amr knows best what he is saying. Then Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, delivered a sermon on Friday, and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is still a group of My nation will follow the truth until the command of God comes.” He said: Then we mentioned what Omar said to Abdullah bin Amr, and he said: “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke the truth.” And peace be upon him, if that is as you said, “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8653 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8654","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, They said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salem, he said: I heard Ya’qub bin Asim bin Masoud, he said: I heard a man say To Abdullah bin Amr: You say that the Hour will come to such-and-such, so he said: I intended not to talk to you about anything, but I told you You will see that a little while later something great happened, and the house was burned. Shu`bah said, Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Antichrist will emerge among my nation and will remain.” “There are forty among them.” I do not know whether it is a day, forty years, forty nights, or forty months. Then God will send Jesus, son of Mary, may the blessings of God be upon him. And the greeting is as if it were Urwa bin Masoud Al-Thaqafi, seeking him and destroying him, then some people will remain after him for years without enmity between the two, then he will send God will blow from the Levant, and no one will have an atom’s weight of faith left in his heart, but I will seize it. Even if one of you were in the middle of a mountain, he would enter. “On him.” Abdullah said: I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Then the worst of people remain in the stealth of birds, and the dreams of wild beasts, which they do not know.” And they do not deny any evil, then Satan appears to them and says: Will you not respond? And he commands them to turn to idols and they worship them while they are in That is the source of their livelihood and a good life. The trumpet is blown and no one hears it unless he listens, and the first person to hear it is a man who soils his pelvis. Then it will be struck, and then there will be no one left who will not be struck by shock, then God will send - or God will send down - rain as if it were a shadow - or the suspicious anemone dew - and it will sprout. Their bodies, then another mouth will be blown into it, and behold, they stand and see.” Then He said: “Come to your Lord and stand before them. They will be questioned.” Then It will be said: Bring out the fire, and it will be said: How much? It will be said: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine. On that Day He will make the children grey. And on that day a leg will be uncovered.” Muhammad ibn Ja’far said: Shu’bah told me this hadith several times, and I presented it to him several times. “An authentic hadith according to The conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not include it.”"
"8655","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told me, my father told me, Abu Al-Tahir and Abu Al-Rabi’ Al-Misrian told us, they said: Abd told us. Allah bin Wahb, Abd al-Rahman bin Shurayh informed me, on the authority of Rabia bin Saif al-Maafiri, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah, that Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja'i, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to him and greeted him, then said: Congratulations to you, O Messenger of God, may God reward you for your victory. Show your religion and the war has taken its toll with its wrath. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in a dome of human beings. He said: “Come in, O Awf. He said: Should I enter all of it or some of it? He said: “Come in, all of you.” He said: “The war will not end until six of them are dead, the first of whom are dead.” Then Awf cried. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Say: One, and the second is the conquest of the Holy House, and the third is a trial that will be among the people like the punishment of sheep, and the fourth is a trial. It will be among the people, and no family will remain unless their share of it enters upon them. And the fifth: A boy will be born among the Yellows, one of the children of kings. He grows old in a day as a child grows in a month, and he grows in a month as a child grows in a month, and he grows in a month as a child grows in a year.When he had reached twelve years, they made him king over them. Then he stood up among them and said: How long will these people prevail over us over the noble things of our land? I decided to go to them until I expelled them from it, so the preachers appeared and improved his opinion, so he sent to the islands and the wilderness with work ships, then he carried the fighter in them until he landed between Antioch and Al-Arish - Ibn Shurayh said: I heard someone saying: They are twelve targets under Each target was twelve thousand, so the Muslims gathered to meet their companion in the Holy House, and were unanimous in their opinion that they would march to the city of The Messenger, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, until their interests are in Sarh and Khaybar - Ibn Abi Ja’far said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “They will go out “My nation is from the springs of wormwood.” He said: Or Al-Harith bin Yazid said: “They will reside there, and a third of them will flee and a third of them will be killed.” Then God Almighty will defeat them with the patient third.” Khalid bin Yazid said: “On that day, by God, he will strike with his sword and stab with his spear.” The Muslims will follow it until they reach the strait at Constantinople, where they will find that its waters have dried up, so they will cross to Medina until... They will descend therein, and God will tear down their walls with takbeer.Then they will enter it and divide their wealth by the shields,” and Abu Qabil al-Ma’afiri said: “While they were doing that, when it came to them A passenger, and he said: You are here and the Antichrist has quarreled with you regarding your family, but it was a lie, so whoever heard the scholars about that stayed on what It struck him, and as for the others, they dispersed, and the Muslims were building mosques in Constantinople and attacking after that until he was expelled. The sixth antichrist: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8655 - There is a break"
"8656","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Abi told us, Abu Al-Tahir and Abu Al-Rabi’ told us, they said: Ibn Wahb told us, Abd told me Al-Rahman bin Shurayh, on the authority of Bakr bin Amr Al-Maafiri, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Kurayb, the client of Ibn Abbas, that He was with Ibn Abbas and Ibn al-Zubayr with him in a group, and Abu Hurairah entered upon them and said: “Die.” Then Ibn al-Zubayr said to him: O Abu Hurairah. The religion is established, and the jihad is established, and the prayer, zakat, Hajj, and fasting of Ramadan are established. Abu Hurairah said: “If you die before you realize what is not... The benefactor can increase his good deeds, but the evildoer cannot stop his evil.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8656 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8657","Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Kamil al-Qadi narrated to us and mentioned it in a similar way, Abu Qalaba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Al-Waddah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Tarfat Al-Sulami, said: I heard Ali, may God be pleased with him, say: “It was not a state of truth.” There was never a time except that Adam was forced to attack Iblis, and there is never a state of falsehood except that Iblis was forced to attack Adam. Satan was commanded to prostrate, but he disobeyed, so Adam was forced to attack him. Until the two men killed one of them, then Satan accused him, and there will be tribulations, a specific tribulation, a general tribulation, and a specific tribulation. And general strife. It was said: O Commander of the Faithful, what is private strife and general strife, and private strife and general strife? He said: So he said: “Iman is the imam of truth and the imam of falsehood, so it passes from truth to falsehood, and from falsehood to truth. This is a trial. And the faith is the imam of truth and the imam of falsehood, and it flows from truth to falsehood and from falsehood to truth. This is the temptation of the common people.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, for this narrator is Abu Awanah, and he did not narrate it for the chain of transmission, not for the chain of transmission.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8657 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8658","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Nafi’ bin Yazid informed us, Ayyash bin Abbas told me that Al-Harith bin Yazid told him that he heard Abdullah bin Zurayr Al-Ghafiqi saying: I heard Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said: “There will be a trial from which people will be harvested just as gold is extracted from a mine, so do not curse the people of the Levant, and curse You wronged them, for among them are the ungrateful, and God will send to them a torrent from the sky and drown them, so that even if the foxes fought them they would be defeated, then At that time, God will send a man from the family of the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, with twelve thousand if they are few, and fifteen thousand if they are many. Their sign or sign is based on three banners. The people of seven banners fight them. There is no owner of a banner unless he aspires to dominion. They fight and are defeated, then Al-Hashimi appears and God returns to the people their kindness and blessings, so they remain like that until he comes out. Al-Dajjal “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8658 - True"
"8659","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Amr bin Muhammad Al-Anqazi told us, Yunus bin Abi told us Ishaq, Ammar al-Dahni told me, on the authority of Abu al-Tufayl, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, who said: We were with Ali, may God be pleased with him, and a man asked him about Al Mahdi, then Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: Far from it, then he held seven with his hand and said: “That will come out at the end of time when the man says: God, God.” He was killed, and God Almighty will gather for him a people as distinct as the speck of a cloud. God will unite their hearts so that they will not feel lonely toward anyone, nor will they rejoice over anyone. He is included among them according to the number of the companions of Badr, the first ones did not precede them and the others do not overtake them, and according to the number of the companions of Taloot who passed with him. The river, Abu Tufayl said: Ibn al-Hanafiyyah said: Do you want it? I said: “Yes.” He said: “He will emerge from between these two woods.” I said: “No crime, and by God, I will not show them until I die.” So he died, meaning Mecca is protected by God Almighty. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8659 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8660","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Musa Al-Khazen, may God have mercy on him, told us in Bukhara, Ibrahim bin Yusuf Al-Hasanjani told us, narrated to us Hisham bin Ammar, Yahya bin Hamza told us, Amr bin Qais Al-Kindi told me, he said: I was with my father Al-Fawares when I was a young boy, and I saw People gathered around a man. I said: Who is this? They said: Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, so I heard him narrating on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “As the Hour approaches, The bad people will be exalted and the good people will be put down, speech will be praised and deeds will be shamed, and the people will be praised, and there will not be a single one among them who denies it.” It was said: And what The dual? He said: “Nothing was written except the Book of God Almighty.” It was narrated by Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Amr ibn Qais Al-Sakouni."
"8661","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Musa bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad told us, Abu Yusuf Muhammad bin Kathir Al-San’ani told us, Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Amr bin Qais Al-Sakouni said: I went out with my father in the delegation to Muawiyah, and I heard a man speaking to people, saying: “One of the signs of the Hour is that... The evil people will be exalted and the good people will be put down, and the deeds and deeds will be preserved and the words will appear, and it will be read with the double in the people, but not among them. Who will change it or deny it? It was said: What is the double? He said: “I wrote down nothing but the Book of God Almighty.” He said: So I narrated this hadith to a people, including Ismail bin Ubayd Allah, and he said: I Are you with you in that meeting? Do you know who the man is? I said: No. He said: Abdullah bin Amr: “This hadith is authentic with all its chains of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8661 - True"
"8662","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Abu Al-Tahir told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told me, On the authority of Abu Qabil Al-Maafiri, he said: We were with Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, and he was asked which of the two cities would be conquered first, Constantinople or Romans? He said: So he called for a box of cooked food - and cooked food is good - and took out a book from it and looked at it, then said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We write what he said: He was asked which city would be conquered first, Constantinople or Rome? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The city of Heraclius will be conquered first,” meaning Constantinople. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8662 - True"
"8663","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr told me, Muawiyah ibn Amr told me, Zaydah told me, Abu Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Thabit ibn Qutubah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Stick to this obedience.” And the community, for it is the rope of God that He commanded, and what you dislike in community is better than what you like in division, and God Almighty has not He never created anything unless He created an end for it, and this debt has been completed and is about to be diminished, and the sign of that is that the ties of kinship are severed. Money is taken unlawfully, blood is shed, and a relative complains about his kinship, and nothing is gained from him, and the beggar circumambulates between the two Friday prayers without Something is placed in his hand, and while they were like that, when the cows mooed, all the people thought that it had only mooed before them. So while the people were like that, when “The earth has strewn with its abundance of gold and silver. After that, nothing of gold and silver will be of use.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of the two sheikhs, and they did not take it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8663 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8664","Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told me, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaida told us, Abu Ishaq told us Al-Shaybani, Yasir bin Amr reported that he said to Abu Masoud: I had two companions to whom I used to worry: Hudhayfah and Abu Musa. And I adjure you by God, if you have heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, anything about turmoil, not to tell me, or else strive to give me your opinion. He said: Abu Masoud thanked God and praised him, then said: “You have to make the nation of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, great, for God did not gather the nation of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” May peace be upon him and grant him peace forever upon misguidance, and be patient until a righteous person is relieved and relieved from an immoral person. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. “And We have written it with a wondrous and high chain of transmission.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8664 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8665","Abu Jafar Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Waez told us, Al-Hussein bin Dawud bin Muadh told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Ayman told us Ibn Nabel, on the authority of Qudamah Ibn Abdullah Ibn Ammar Al-Kallabi, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “You must obey God and this group, for God Almighty will never unite the nation of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, in error, and you must be patient.” “Until the righteous person finds rest and is relieved from the ungodly.” This is a hadith. We did not write from the hadith of Ayman ibn Nabil al-Makki except with this chain of transmission, and Al-Hussein ibn David is not one of the requirements of this book.”"
"8666","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, and Abu Nu’aym said: We told us: Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah ibn Kuhail, on the authority of Abu al-Za’ra’, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: “God Almighty sends a wind Therein will be a cold wind. Do not leave a believer on the face of the earth unless he dies by that wind. Then the Hour will come upon the wickedest of people.” This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” It was also narrated with an authentic chain of transmission, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8666 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8667","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Amr bin Marzuq told us, Imran Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Adam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, said: “The Hour will not come until God sends a wind that will not leave anyone in “His heart is an atom’s weight of piety or prohibition except his fist, and every people follows what their fathers worshiped in the pre-Islamic period.”"
"8668","Muhammad ibn al-Mu'mil ibn al-Hasan told me, al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn al-Musayyab told us, Nu`aym ibn Hammad told us, Yahya ibn Hamza told us, Thawr ibn Yazid, on the authority of Khalid ibn Ma’dan, Umair ibn al-Aswad told me, he said: I came to Abdullah ibn al-Samit while he was staying in a building of his. And with him was his wife, Umm Haram. Umm Haram told us that she heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The first army of my nation to attack... The sea has become obligatory.” She said: I said: O Messenger of God, am I among them? He said: “You are among them.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The first of my nation to attack the city of Caesar will be forgiven.” I said: O Messenger of God, I In them? He said: “No.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8668 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8669","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Balawayh told us, they said: Bishr told us Ibn Musa Al-Asadi, Hawdhah Ibn Khalifa told us, Awf Ibn Abi Jamila told me, Al-Hussein Ibn Ali Al-Darimi told me, Muhammad Ibn Ishaq told me. The Imam, Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Awf, Abu Al-Siddiq Al-Naji told us, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Hour will not come until the earth is filled with injustice, oppression, and aggression, then some of my household will leave.” “Who will fill it with justice and justice as it was filled with injustice and hostility?” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and the interpreted hadith. In that way and the methods of Asim’s hadith, on the authority of Zurr, on the authority of Abdullah, all of them are authentic, according to what I have established in this book by using Asim’s narrations as evidence. Ibn Abi Al-Najjoud, since he is one of the imams of the Muslims.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8669 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8670","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Amr bin Asim Al-Kalabi told us, Imran Al-Qattan told us, Qatada, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The Mahdi is from among us, the people of the House.” He will fill the earth with equity and justice as it was filled with oppression and injustice. He will live like this.” He spread out his left hand and two fingers. From his right hand is the rosary, the thumb, and holding three “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8670 - Imran is weak and no Muslim came out for him"
"8671","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told me, Abdullah bin Salih told me, Abu Al-Malih Al-Raqqi told me, Ziyad told me Ibn Bayan, and mentioned his grace, he said: I heard Ali bin Nufayl, saying: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab saying: I heard Umm Salama, saying: I heard The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned the Mahdi, and he said: “Yes, he is true and he is from the children of Fatima.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8671 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8672","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrafi told us about Marw, Abu al-Ahwas Muhammad bin al-Haytham al-Qadi told us, Amr bin Khalid told us Al-Harrani, Abu Al-Malih told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Bayan, on the authority of Ali bin Nufayl, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned the Mahdi, and he said: “He is from the descendants of Fatima.”"
"8673","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, Suleiman bin Ubaid told us, Abu Al-Siddiq Al-Naji narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He will emerge at the end of my nation.” The Mahdi will be watered by God with rain, and the earth will produce its plants, and the money will be given in good health, and the livestock will increase and the nation will be great. He will live for seven or more years. Eighthly - meaning as evidence - this is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8673 - True"
"8674","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Hajjaj bin Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Matar, and Abi Harun, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The earth will be filled with Unjust and unjust, then a man from my family will leave.” The hadith “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not expel him.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8674 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8675","Abdullah bin Saad Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib, Ibrahim bin Ishaq, and Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Ahmed Al-Hafiz told us, They said: Nasr bin Ali told us, Muhammad bin Marwan told us, Amara bin Abi Hafsa told us, on the authority of Zaid Al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq Al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There will be among my nation the Mahdi. If he shortens, then seven, and if not, then nine. Enjoy.” In it will be a blessing for my nation, the like of which they have never enjoyed. The earth will yield its fruits, not withholding anything from them, and wealth on that Day will be a heap. The man will stand up and say: O Mahdi, give me, and he says: Take.” Al-Hakim, may God Almighty have mercy on him, said: “I have narrated what my knowledge has reached of the temptations of the end of time on the authority of The Chosen One, may God bless him and grant him peace, provided the chain of narrations appropriate to this book. As for the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, they mentioned the horrors of The Resurrection and the Resurrection are included in the tribulations, and in that I followed the choice of Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, in isolating this from the emerging temptations, and God grants success to what I have chosen, and He is sufficient for me, and He is the best disposer of affairs.”"
